          "httpVersion": "HTTP/1.1",
          "method": "POST",
          "postData": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "params": [],
            "text": "{\"input\":[{\"content\":\"<instructions>\\nYou are a customer service agent that helps the user according to the <policy> provided below.\\nIn each turn you can either:\\n- Send a message to the user.\\n- Make a tool call.\\nYou cannot do both at the same time.\\n\\nTry to be helpful and always follow the policy. Always make sure you generate valid JSON only.\\n</instructions>\\n<policy>\\n# Rho-Bank Customer Service Policy\\n\\nYou are a helpful customer service agent for Rho-Bank.\\nYour goal is to help customers by searching the knowledge base and providing accurate information.\\n\\n## Guidelines\\n\\n1. Do not make up policies, information or actions that you can take on behalf of the user. All instructions will be found here or in the knowledge base. If you cannot find relevant information, let the user know. \\n2. Do not ask for any documentation, receipts... from the customer unless it states very clearly in the knowledge base how to process it, and whether you're allowed to do so. \\n3. Be polite and professional\\n4. If you need the current time, always use the get_current_time() tool. Do not make up or assume the current time. \\n5. Generally, if the issue cannot be resolved or is outside your capabilities, ask the user whether they would like to be transferred to a human agent. If they do, invoke the appropriate transfer_to_human_agents tool. Do this only if you absolutely have to, and you are sure that there are no potential actions you can take as specified in the knowledge base, or in your policy. Do not transfer without asking the user first. This guidance may be overridden by specific scenario-based transfer guidance in the knowledge base. \\n6. If an issue falls within your capabilities and the user still wants to be transferred to a human agent, kindly inform the user that you can help them, and try to help them first. If the user asks for a human agent 4 times, then you may invoke the transfer_to_human_agents tool. This guidance may be overridden by specific scenario-based transfer guidance in the knowledge base. \\n7. Do not give intermediate responses to users while processing that would give away internal rho-bank information/policies. \\n\\n\\n**Search the knowledge base** for relevant information when appropriate using the provided `KB_search` tool (uses BM25 for retrieval).\\n\\n\\n## Additional Instructions\\n\\n### Discoverable Tools\\n\\n#### Giving Discoverable Tools to Users\\nThe knowledge base may contain instructions that indicate certain actions should be performed by the user themselves rather than by you. These are called \\\"user discoverable tools.\\\" A user discoverable tool is a tool that you provide to the user so they can execute it on their own (e.g., through a customer portal or app).\\n\\n**When to give user discoverable tools:**\\n-  Only give a tool when the user would like to perform an action, and the knowledge base explicitly has a tool that allows the user to perform this action (e.g., \\\"to do X, have the user call tool_name(args)\\\"). IMPORTANT: Do not unlock tools that you do not plan on giving to the user and actually using: this causes issues in database logging.\\n- You must search the knowledge base to find tools that you can give. Do not invent or guess user discoverable tools \\n- Only use tool names and arguments discovered in the knowledge base\\n\\n**How to give a tool:**\\n- Use the `give_discoverable_user_tool(discoverable_tool_name)` function\\n- Provide the exact tool name  as specified in the knowledge base\\n- Explain to the user what the tool does and how to use it, and what arguments to provide. Just explaining isn't enough, you must use the `give_discoverable_user_tool(discoverable_tool_name)` function.\\n\\n#### Unlocking and Using Agent Discoverable Tools\\nThe knowledge base may contain references to specialized internal tools that you can unlock and use. These are called \\\"agent discoverable tools.\\\" Unlike regular tools which are always available, these tools must be explicitly unlocked after discovering them in the knowledge base.\\n\\n**When to use agent discoverable tools:**\\n- Only unlock a tool when the knowledge base explicitly mentions it (e.g., \\\"use tool_name to perform X\\\"), and do not unlock tools you do not plan to use.\\n- You must search the knowledge base to find tools that you can unlock. Do not invent or guess tool names - only use tool names discovered in the knowledge base.\\n\\n**How to use agent discoverable tools:**\\n1. First, unlock the tool using `unlock_discoverable_agent_tool(agent_tool_name)` with the exact tool name from the knowledge base: you must unlock the tool before using it to get information on the proper params. IMPORTANT: Do not unlock tools that you do not plan on actually using: this causes issues in database logging.\\n2. Then, call the tool using `call_discoverable_agent_tool(agent_tool_name, arguments)` with the required arguments\\n3. The unlock step is required before calling - you cannot call a tool that hasn't been unlocked\\n\\n### Authenticating Users\\n\\nGenerally, for any scenario involving accessing customer information in internal databases, you must first verify their identify before proceeding. No need to verify more than once in a single conversation. You should ONLY verify a user's identity if you need to access or modify their customer information in internal databases on their behalf.\\n\\nHere are some concrete examples:\\n* Looking up account balances, transaction history, referral history...\\n* Changing account settings (e.g., address, phone number, email)\\n* Closing an account\\n* Adding or removing authorized users\\n* Requesting information about specific transactions\\n* Discussing specific loan or credit details\\n* Filing a dispute on behalf of the user\\n\\nTo verify the identity of the user, call the appropriate read tools, and ensure that they are able to give correctly any 2 out of the following values: date of birth, email, phone number, address. Knowing full name or userID is not enough to verify. After verification, you must call the verification logging tool to properly log the information into the verification records. Do not leak any information about the user before they are verified.\\n</policy>\",\"role\":\"system\"},{\"content\":\"Hi! How can I help you today?\",\"role\":\"assistant\"},{\"content\":\"Hi, I run a landscaping business and I need to open a better business checking account. I already have a Navy Blue business checking with you but it’s pretty basic — I want something with more features. I’ve looked at your website but there are way too many options. Can you just tell me which account is right for me?\",\"role\":\"user\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"business checking Navy Blue upgrade account options comparison recommend business checking accounts features\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_iEVqj3yIvVksygEx1IrzUtpp\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc472253b487d1b33c14720373e8e2\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_iEVqj3yIvVksygEx1IrzUtpp\",\"output\":\"1. Internal: Opening Business Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_003\\n   Score: 29.1492\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nTo open a business checking account, ensure all of the following are true:\\n1. The customer is verified.\\n2. The customer has at least one existing personal checking account with status OPEN.\\n3. The customer does not exceed 6 business checking accounts.\\n4. The customer has no accounts with status CLOSED.\\n5. The customer's existing checking account has a balance of at least $500.\\n\\n## Opening Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify customer identity.\\n2. Check eligibility requirements listed above.\\n3. Confirm the customer's desired account_class selection.\\n   - Business checking account_class options include Navy Blue, Cobalt Blue, True Blue, etc.\\n4. Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account.\\n\\n2. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_013\\n   Score: 26.5624\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Sky Blue account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Lime Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Sky Blue nor Lime Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our startup and premium business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n3. How to transition a Light Green Account to Blue or Green Account (checking)\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_light_green_account_010\\n   Score: 24.9483\\n   Content: ## Determine if the change is automatic\\n- If Yes is True, your account will convert to an eligible adult checking option automatically at the appropriate time.\\n\\n## If the change is not automatic\\n- If Yes is False, initiate a move to Blue or Green Account (checking) by submitting an upgrade request and selecting your preferred account type.\\n\\n### Before you switch\\n- Compare features and fees of Blue and Green Account (checking) to choose the best fit.\\n- Confirm that any scheduled payments or deposits will continue without interruption after the transition.\\n\\n4. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - October 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_014\\n   Score: 20.7974\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 10/12/2025 TO 11/12/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Lime Green account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Hunter Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Lime Green nor Hunter Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our premium and eco-conscious business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n5. Navy Blue Business Checking: Complete Guide\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_navy_blue_001\\n   Score: 19.6259\\n   Content: ## Key Account Costs and Limits\\n\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: $0.00\\n- Annual Percentage Yield (APY) on balances: 0.5%\\n- Daily digital transfer limit: $25,000\\n\\n### What you can expect day to day\\n- No minimum balance requirement, so you can use the account flexibly.\\n- Unlimited digital transfers within the daily limit of $25,000.\\n- Optional overdraft settings are available if you want coverage on eligible transactions.\\n- E-statements are included at no additional cost.\\n\\n### Practical tips for managing your account\\n- Use e-statements to keep records organized and accessible.\\n- Plan larger transfers with the daily limit of $25,000 in mind; schedule across days if needed.\\n- Keep an eye on your balance to maximize earnings at 0.5%.\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n| Item | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $0.00 |\\n| APY | 0.5% |\\n| Daily digital transfer limit | $25,000 |\\n\\n## Business Referral Program\\n\\nGrow your network and earn rewards by referring other businesses to Navy Blue:\\n\\n| Referral Detail | Value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Your referral bonus | $100 |\\n| New business welcome bonus | $75 |\\n| Maximum referrals per year | 10 |\\n| Required qualifying deposit | $5,000 |\\n| Deposit must be made within | 90 days |\\n| Your account age requirement | 60 days |\\n\\nTo qualify: The referred business must open a Navy Blue account and deposit at least $5,000 within 90 days of account opening. Referrer eligibility requires having been a Rho-Bank checking customer for 60 days or more.\\n\\n6. Internal: Opening Business Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_004\\n   Score: 19.3585\\n   Content: ## Description\\n\\nProcedure for opening business savings accounts. Eligibility requirements: 1) Customer must be verified, 2) Customer must already have at least one business checking account with status OPEN, 3) Customer cannot have more than 4 business savings accounts, 4) Customer must not have any accounts with negative balances, 5) Existing business checking account must have been open for at least 30 days, 6) Existing business checking account must have a balance of at least $2,500. Steps: 1) Verify customer identity, 2) Check eligibility requirements, 3) Confirm account selection with customer (business savings account_class options include Bronze Saver Account, Silver Saver Account, etc.), 4) Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account, 5) Ask the customer if they would like you to transfer the opening deposit from their business checking account now. If yes, use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount. If no, inform them they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nConfirm all of the following before proceeding:\\n- Customer identity is verified.\\n- Customer has at least one business checking account with status OPEN.\\n- Customer has fewer than 4 existing business savings accounts.\\n- Customer has no accounts with negative balances.\\n- At least one existing business checking account has been open for at least 30 days.\\n- That business checking account has a current balance of at least $2,500.\\n\\nNotes:\\n- Use the qualifying OPEN business checking account that meets both the tenure and balance thresholds as the source for the optional opening deposit transfer.\\n\\n## Step-by-Step Procedure\\n\\n1) Verify customer identity.\\n2) Check eligibility requirements (see list above).\\n3) Confirm account selection with the customer:\\n   - Ask for the desired business savings account_class (e.g., Bronze Saver Account, Silver Saver Account, etc.).\\n   - Ensure you capture the exact official account_class name ending with “Account.”\\n4) Open the new business savings account using the agent tool (see Tool Instructions below).\\n5) Funding the opening deposit:\\n   - Ask the customer if they want you to transfer the opening deposit now from their eligible business checking account.\\n   - If yes: initiate the internal transfer using the agent tool (see Tool Instructions below).\\n   - If no: inform the customer they have 30 days to fund the account via internal transfer or external deposit; otherwise, the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Agent Tool Instructions\\n\\nThe AGENT calls these tools directly to perform actions on behalf of the customer. Do not expose tool details to the customer.\\n\\n### Tool: open_bank_account_4821\\n\\n- Signature:\\n  - open_bank_account_4821(user_id, account_type, account_class)\\n- When to call:\\n  - After eligibility is confirmed and the customer has selected the desired business savings account_class.\\n- How to call:\\n  - Set account_type to 'savings'.\\n  - Set account_class to the exact official name provided by the customer (e.g., 'Bronze Saver Account').\\n- Expected outcome:\\n  - Returns a new savings account record (capture the new account_id for subsequent actions).\\n\\n### Tool: transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291\\n\\n- Signature:\\n  - transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291(source_account_id, destination_account_id, amount)\\n- When to call:\\n  - Only if the customer authorizes transferring the opening deposit now.\\n- How to call:\\n  - source_account_id: the qualifying OPEN business checking account that meets the 30-day tenure and $2,500 balance requirements.\\n  - destination_account_id: the newly opened business savings account_id.\\n  - amount: the required opening deposit amount confirmed with the customer.\\n- If the transfer fails (e.g., insufficient funds):\\n  - Inform the customer and remind them they have 30 days to fund the account via internal transfer or external deposit, or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Checklist Before Opening\\n\\n- Customer identity verified.\\n- OPEN business checking account identified and qualified (≥ 30 days open and ≥ $2,500 balance).\\n- Savings account count confirmed is < 4.\\n- No negative balances across any accounts.\\n- Customer-confirmed account_class captured exactly.\\n\\n## Post-Opening Actions\\n\\n- If the customer funds now: complete the transfer and confirm success.\\n- If the customer defers funding: clearly communicate the 30-day deadline and acceptable methods (internal transfer or external deposit), and note that the account will be closed if not funded within that timeframe.\\n\\n7. Internal: Ordering a Debit Card for a Bank Account\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023\\n   Score: 19.3424\\n   Content: Procedure for if the customer inquires about ordering a debit card linked to a specific checking account. Debit cards can only be ordered for checking accounts (personal or business) - savings accounts are not eligible for debit cards.\\n\\nEligibility requirements:\\n1) Customer must be verified\\n2) The account must be a checking account (account_type must be 'checking')\\n3) Account status must be OPEN\\n4) Account must have been open for at least 3 business days (excluding weekends)\\n5) Customer cannot have more than 1 active debit cards per checking account\\n6) Account must have a minimum balance of $25 (to cover potential fees)\\n7) Customer must be at least 18 years old (verify using date_of_birth)\\n8) Customer cannot have a pending debit card order for the same account (check debit_cards table for PENDING status)\\n9) Customer's address on file must be a valid US domestic address (international shipping is not available)\\n \\n\\nDelivery Options:\\n- STANDARD: Free shipping, arrives in 7-10 business days\\n- EXPEDITED: $15 fee, arrives in 3-5 business days\\n- RUSH: $35 fee, arrives in 1-2 business days, fees may vary based on account tier. \\n\\nCard Design Options:\\n- CLASSIC: Standard Rho-Bank blue design (default, no fee)\\n- PREMIUM: Metallic silver finish ($10 one-time fee)\\n- CUSTOM: Customer-uploaded image ($25 one-time fee, subject to approval), fees may vary ased on account tier. \\n\\nSteps:\\n1) Verify customer identity\\n2) Confirm which checking account the debit card should be linked to. \\n3) Check eligibility requirements for the specified account\\n4) Ask customer for preferred delivery option (STANDARD, EXPEDITED, or RUSH) and explain fees. \\n5) Ask customer for preferred card design (CLASSIC, PREMIUM, or CUSTOM) and explain fees. \\n6) Confirm the address that the customer would like to mail the card to. \\n7) Use order_debit_card_5739 to order the card. \\n8) Inform customer of expected delivery timeframe and any applicable fees\\n\\nImportant Notes:\\n- Expedited and rush delivery fees are automatically deducted from the linked checking account\\n- If the account has insufficient funds for delivery or design fees, the order will fail\\n- Customers can track their card shipment status using the Rho-Bank mobile app\\n- New cards are automatically activated upon first use with PIN entry\\n- The customer's existing debit card (if any) will remain active until the new card is activated.\\n\\n8. FAQ: Checking Account Referrals\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_048\\n   Score: 18.2423\\n   Content: ## Frequently asked questions about checking account referrals\\n\\n### How many people can I refer at once?\\nYou can have multiple referrals in progress, but you can only receive a maximum of 2 referral bonuses in any rolling 9-day window. If you exceed this limit, additional referrals will be automatically denied until enough time passes.\\n\\n### Can I refer someone who used to have a Rho-Bank account?\\nNo. The referred person must be a new Rho-Bank customer with no existing or closed accounts within the past 12 months. Former customers must wait 12 months after their last account closure before being eligible as a referral.\\n\\n### Can I refer someone who lives at the same address as me?\\nNo. The referrer and referred person cannot be registered at the same address. This restriction helps prevent abuse of the referral program.\\n\\n### What counts as a qualifying deposit?\\nThe qualifying deposit must be new money brought into Rho-Bank. Transfers from another Rho-Bank account do not count. The deposit can come from an external bank transfer, direct deposit, mobile check deposit, or cash/check deposit at a branch.\\n\\n### What happens if the person I referred closes their account early?\\nIf the referred account is closed within 90 days of opening, your referral bonus may be reversed (clawed back). Both accounts must remain in good standing for bonuses to be retained.\\n\\n### Can I combine the referral bonus with other promotions?\\nNo. The referral bonus cannot be combined with other new account promotions or sign-up bonuses. Only one promotional offer can be applied per new account.\\n\\n### What do the referral statuses mean?\\n- **COMPLETE**: The referral was successful and bonuses will be paid.\\n- **IN_PROGRESS**: The new account is open but hasn't met the qualifying deposit yet.\\n- **NO_PROGRESS**: The referred person hasn't started an application.\\n- **APPLIED**: An application has been submitted and is being reviewed.\\n- **REJECTED**: The referral was denied (usually due to hitting the rolling window limit or eligibility issues).\\n- **ERROR**: A system error occurred; try again later or contact support.\\n\\n### Why was my referral rejected?\\nCommon reasons for rejection include:\\n- You already received 2 referral bonuses in the past 9 days (rolling window limit).\\n- The referred person already has or recently had a Rho-Bank account.\\n- You and the referred person are registered at the same address.\\n- For business referrals: The referred business has the same primary owner as an existing account.\\n\\n### How long do I have to wait after a rejection to refer again?\\nIf your referral was rejected due to the rolling window limit, you must wait until your oldest qualifying referral is more than 9 days old. The limit is based on a rolling window, so you become eligible again as older referrals age out.\\n\\n### Can I refer someone for a business checking account?\\nYes, but the referred business must have a different primary owner (based on SSN of the primary authorized signer) than any existing Rho-Bank business account.\\n\\n### Do I need to have the same account type to refer someone for it?\\nNo. Referrer eligibility hinges on how long you've been a Rho-Bank checking customer, not which product you currently use. The tenure threshold is measured from when you opened your very first checking account with us. Someone with a Navy Blue account can refer others for World Blue, True Blue, or any other checking product—provided they've met the duration requirement.\\n\\n### How long does the referred person have to make the qualifying deposit?\\nThe deposit window varies by account type, typically between 60-120 days. Check the specific account's referral terms for the exact timeframe. After the deposit is made, it must remain in the account for at least 30 additional days.\\n\\n9. What happens when the primary account holder turns 25\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_light_green_account_008\\n   Score: 18.0476\\n   Content: ## Timeline\\n- As you approach 24, we will prompt you to prepare for the next account type.\\n\\n## Transition\\n- If Yes is True: your account will automatically move to an eligible adult checking option at 24, with no action required.\\n- If Yes is False: you will choose a new account type and complete a simple upgrade process when you reach 24.\\n\\n### What you should do now\\n- Review adult account options ahead of reaching 24.\\n- Ensure your contact information is current so you do not miss transition notices.\\n\\n10. True Blue Account: Fee Waivers and Balance Requirements\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_002\\n   Score: 17.8149\\n   Content: ## Waiving your monthly maintenance fee\\n- You will be charged $75.00 each month unless you meet the waiver threshold.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is waived when your balance is at least $50,000 during the statement period.\\n\\n## Minimum balance requirement vs. fee waiver threshold\\n- Minimum balance requirement: $25,000 to maintain the account and access premium features.\\n- Fee waiver threshold: $50,000 to waive the $75.00 monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Falling below $25,000 may limit access to premium features until your balance is restored.\\n\\n## Overdrafts and shortfalls\\n- If your balance goes negative, a per-occurrence overdraft fee of $25.00 may apply.\\n\\n## How to avoid fees\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $50,000 to waive the monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Set internal processes to monitor balances against both $25,000 and $50,000.\\n- If a shortfall is anticipated, transfer funds promptly to avoid the $25.00 and preserve eligibility for the fee waiver.\\n\\n## True Blue Referral Program\\n\\nRefer other high-volume businesses to True Blue and earn significant rewards:\\n\\n| Benefit | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Referrer bonus | $350 per referral |\\n| New member bonus | $250 |\\n| Maximum referrals per year | 15 |\\n| Qualifying deposit | $50,000 |\\n| Deposit window | 120 days |\\n| Account age requirement | 90 days |\\n\\n### Referral requirements\\n- The referred business must deposit $50,000 within 120 days of opening their True Blue account.\\n- Eligibility is based on how long you've been a Rho-Bank checking customer. The account age threshold is 90 days, calculated from when you opened your oldest checking account.\\n- Referral bonuses are paid after qualification is confirmed and are subject to the annual limit of 15.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEcnApVLx1PvdakziLbGlEPOlWuOyFQhJ1j82OcnLI70pMcTv-RdpTNz04Uz4MBKWKVEw_XYcKF4-gw6NWae7krBO7V67awxZ3nF12byFNt8Rm828fAlTUHPLtPwNzcPLAA-9j_s-jj8prkTubfauKG3Fb29TPAWzG2QjqHKGI1ubQsh5wD6sCbha9zKGiUCcgYTawqFnfkCAn9rSpAHBSnMkGfLHdK55CEIyuNz3IVtRBDHf3aqWoh-LxTIufPJgWr3POGhFkGyyFWMtSrxEYvoyrBv_6ePscci5H3IsPMJeL5HpJ8leHxwBPb3Apy_RPh0Pyj9ES6USfnarW0UXpVZlfycx8fAxdWWry21tPkXSpYgoi5v0tfGcQyydRUA66xndQw9m5DEDxGtFc2Z42_nnlaOKWFHP2OATqvKkin1ELEel2lIZrJs5RuKRMbtdgevayIierWhDfqyv8_0rPnAo8_X-1waDyfp7EFVG6el7nKxJYGgVYYqBmk8MIdT7tGALzJAxL41rJH1CJEqrbCk8tHLJ4hOdmN9oBdNO2oCXTvRb45Ph_SsWfcRXGXp5GtwqkaHACpc9_cyP3dkpXr22LHPmBebVg10Qy7vDiOoq8PAJTNscf2a_ItLAyBvUZairzJ_mqNTXb8PCyBbvpGER54hA9H0C7N9Es3OrHlQJIycP-3iRaBleB9CY69VcYm55uBTwW6PPi50YCnvFEcISCXev_MVAs6I-RyGnDnMnIEj9qhh4X0Km78L5VGqH-9E5DLr05U82wqx0kRIqq6PjCoCC_CiVLoY7vlP_zifW-N-rtO4Cf0_RdV5M1gXfZ5DU4Qrw6z4EhMaGRC45UEJMkowijm53yS7Ha28o6fCbyT-GSE8PpClUmrN5TET2xiD2tgWAeT3zHWSJEe_ug7QPMwy4vaEpMccfu_bxFfgFGFo3A8UBJjQJ15Vc7yLFJuMIrwxzm-kNkZz7ayrq18gOap6Cx1qSnlvL479hJzL8eKhg3hDZn1DBewJRWLibFE6GxRoNwP8-Y-JScLlHdwl5UHeyIhV81ZI-vO6oXkiVW7lBOMUPZncakzqpTBR7KXUTLPtE5YyMY1F9DwqVBl7hlWw3Z6CFn4LvLYA-TASU1sehijJ9Bs688aV85RfyXjspklVVHgS1LPIMg2j-FeiyBYY7lKLcfnFlKn0DxKWmWCcpc3sRUdJpTSChElgkguKzhzEbSK-cNeQe-18cKyiqKnjiEvABPL3GtZI8_iV5TJK4pvCELewbzG8QPP3tngJXYPkVSaoGXkjlvMGlpD1fk1s_OQAzaUcpt-kK4r85O8JbqvhtqAy1I-S-BLDTqS0FHKlxTUoLD5evwAtAHrmSMRmTTE3LhRYoDoT5uhMU8W2JOjCKUO7KBaq5DQQ9USPTczD_oWeg3uR-S0E6bjeBik8RzF4lbw8fvlxKKC4TcbZsx11XP5iYXfNK6bxgExXnrDLgOrSZvoBRzqpSHEcO-s5CbaUO_2HhZOy6qqk321kItKgr7_xU4yXAbXYQ_LPtKJmnK0PpOQs8b_XPUBVb4bNBM0PwtW9gPwO82p1XEHQgX2kzz3pE-rdsLYnuICsv6cZGMQN7JVNs1LSEnRSTHbzyD5JOYYem-9aFa5C-nqtxYMMPfgbwOvh6kNNKOsFsJCpBEy49tnP9lc-yYuDdp0vvEy0MRzY0QVrZm50Q-rBndiRsG4GTZSNmhj1U0hlfyrc40oFWg8lgjCWmUxAXB4iYE43mnZR8qPNeJDd9DtBckxdejYzwga8Fp37wK0Z\",\"id\":\"rs_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc4724802087d1b77365488dbc7343\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Narrowing down account options**\\n\\nI need to respond with a valid JSON format and focus on narrowing down the user’s request without making specific recommendations just yet. The user wants to know the right account but needs details about features and criteria. I could say something like, \\\"I can narrow this down to one recommendation. What features are important to you, like balance or fees?\\\" I'll need to research and gather details about different business accounts, especially regarding payroll and invoicing support.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"business checking accounts comparison features payroll invoicing cash deposits accounting integration Sky Blue Lime Green Cobalt Blue Hunter Green\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_66M0yTostCLxVnl3KmCHWCEo\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc47276e1887d1a5a786b47d331a96\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_66M0yTostCLxVnl3KmCHWCEo\",\"output\":\"1. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_013\\n   Score: 45.3208\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Sky Blue account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Lime Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Sky Blue nor Lime Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our startup and premium business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n2. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - October 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_014\\n   Score: 35.1810\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 10/12/2025 TO 11/12/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Lime Green account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Hunter Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Lime Green nor Hunter Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our premium and eco-conscious business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n3. How to transition a Light Green Account to Blue or Green Account (checking)\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_light_green_account_010\\n   Score: 31.6774\\n   Content: ## Determine if the change is automatic\\n- If Yes is True, your account will convert to an eligible adult checking option automatically at the appropriate time.\\n\\n## If the change is not automatic\\n- If Yes is False, initiate a move to Blue or Green Account (checking) by submitting an upgrade request and selecting your preferred account type.\\n\\n### Before you switch\\n- Compare features and fees of Blue and Green Account (checking) to choose the best fit.\\n- Confirm that any scheduled payments or deposits will continue without interruption after the transition.\\n\\n4. Linked Checking Account APY Boosts for Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_012\\n   Score: 23.1717\\n   Content: Certain personal checking and savings account pairings provide bonus APY on your savings account balance. When you hold both a qualifying checking account and savings account under the same customer profile, the APY boost is automatically applied to your savings account. The following checking and savings account pairings qualify for APY boosts:\\n\\n1. Green Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n3. Evergreen Account (checking) + Green Account (savings)\\n4. Blue Account (checking) + Silver Plus Account (savings)\\n5. Light Green Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n6. Dark Green Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n7. Bluest Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n8. Purple Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n9. Gold Years Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n10. Light Green Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n11. Green Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n12. Evergreen Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n13. Bluest Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n14. Purple Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n15. Gold Years Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n16. Blue Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n17. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n18. Dark Green Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n\\nNote: Only these specific pairings qualify for the linked checking account APY boost. All other checking and savings account combinations do not receive any APY boost from linking. The boost is additive to your savings account's base APY and any credit card APY bonuses you may already have. For the exact APY boost percentages for each pairing, please refer to the specific savings account documentation.\\n\\n5. Lime Green Account: Your Dedicated Account Manager\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_003\\n   Score: 18.1155\\n   Content: ## Response commitments\\n- Direct messages receive a response within 2 business hours.\\n- When calling the priority line, the maximum expected wait is 6 minutes.\\n\\n## How to reach your manager\\n- Send a secure message from within your account's support center and select the option to route to your dedicated manager.\\n- For urgent matters, call the priority support line; your call is queued with elevated priority and subject to the 6 minute maximum wait.\\n\\n## Getting the most out of manager support\\n- Provide context upfront:\\n  - The specific transaction or transfer you need help with.\\n  - Any relevant dates and counterparties.\\n  - Screenshots of error messages (if applicable).\\n- Set your preferred contact method so your manager can follow up quickly.\\n- For time-sensitive requests, note the deadline in your initial message; your manager will respond within 2 business hours.\\n\\n## Escalations\\n- If an issue requires faster handling than messaging, use the priority phone line for a live update within the 6 minute window.\\n\\n## Referral program for Lime Green members\\n\\nAs a Rho-Bank checking account holder, you can refer other businesses to Lime Green and earn substantial rewards:\\n\\n- **Your bonus**: $200 for each successful referral\\n- **Their bonus**: $150 welcome bonus for the referred business\\n- **Annual cap**: 12 referrals per year\\n- **Qualification**: Referred business must deposit $15,000 within 90 days\\n- **Eligibility**: You must have maintained checking account status with Rho-Bank for a minimum of 90 days.\\n\\nSpeak with your dedicated account manager for personalized referral strategies and tracking.\\n\\n6. True Blue Account: Fee Waivers and Balance Requirements\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_002\\n   Score: 17.3688\\n   Content: ## Waiving your monthly maintenance fee\\n- You will be charged $75.00 each month unless you meet the waiver threshold.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is waived when your balance is at least $50,000 during the statement period.\\n\\n## Minimum balance requirement vs. fee waiver threshold\\n- Minimum balance requirement: $25,000 to maintain the account and access premium features.\\n- Fee waiver threshold: $50,000 to waive the $75.00 monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Falling below $25,000 may limit access to premium features until your balance is restored.\\n\\n## Overdrafts and shortfalls\\n- If your balance goes negative, a per-occurrence overdraft fee of $25.00 may apply.\\n\\n## How to avoid fees\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $50,000 to waive the monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Set internal processes to monitor balances against both $25,000 and $50,000.\\n- If a shortfall is anticipated, transfer funds promptly to avoid the $25.00 and preserve eligibility for the fee waiver.\\n\\n## True Blue Referral Program\\n\\nRefer other high-volume businesses to True Blue and earn significant rewards:\\n\\n| Benefit | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Referrer bonus | $350 per referral |\\n| New member bonus | $250 |\\n| Maximum referrals per year | 15 |\\n| Qualifying deposit | $50,000 |\\n| Deposit window | 120 days |\\n| Account age requirement | 90 days |\\n\\n### Referral requirements\\n- The referred business must deposit $50,000 within 120 days of opening their True Blue account.\\n- Eligibility is based on how long you've been a Rho-Bank checking customer. The account age threshold is 90 days, calculated from when you opened your oldest checking account.\\n- Referral bonuses are paid after qualification is confirmed and are subject to the annual limit of 15.\\n\\n7. Internal: Credit Card Rewards - Points vs Cash Back Representation\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_credit_cards_(general)_006\\n   Score: 16.5452\\n   Content: ## Rewards representation\\nDue to a legacy backend migration that has not yet been completed, all credit card rewards in the transaction database are stored as 'points' regardless of whether the card is a cash back card or a points-based card. For cash back cards (Bronze Rewards Card, Silver Rewards Card, Gold Rewards Card, Platinum Rewards Card, Diamond Elite Card, Crypto-Cash Back, Business Bronze Rewards Card, Business Silver Rewards Card, Green Rewards Card, Silver Zoom Card, Business Gold Rewards Card, and Business Platinum Rewards Card), these 'points' should be interpreted as cash back with a conversion rate of 1 point = $0.01 when redeemed as a statement credit or as a credit to the user's Rho-Bank checking account. For example, 250 points equals $2.50 in cash back, which matches a 2.5% cash back rate on a $100 purchase. The only true points-based card is the EcoCard, which earns 'sustainability points' (5 points per dollar on green purchases, 1 point per dollar on other purchases) that also redeem at $0.01 per point when redeemed as a statement credit or checking account credit.\\n\\n8. Earning Cashback from Eco-Friendly Vendors\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_hunter_green_003\\n   Score: 16.3947\\n   Content: ## Your cashback rate and network\\n- Earn 2.0% cashback on eligible purchases from certified eco-friendly vendors.\\n- The network includes approximately $2,500 certified green vendors across categories relevant to sustainable operations.\\n\\n## How to earn\\n- Pay with your Hunter Green business debit or payment instrument at participating certified vendors.\\n- Ensure the merchant is identified as certified in our green vendor network at the time of purchase for 2.0% to apply.\\n\\n## Posting, tracking, and returns\\n- Cashback accrues after eligible transactions finalize. You can track accumulated rewards in your account activity.\\n- If a purchase is refunded or disputed, the related cashback may be reversed.\\n\\n## Common exclusions\\n- Purchases at non-certified merchants do not earn 2.0%.\\n- Certain transaction types may be ineligible at the merchant or network level if they cannot be categorized as certified green.\\n\\n9. Internal: Opening Business Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_003\\n   Score: 16.1108\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nTo open a business checking account, ensure all of the following are true:\\n1. The customer is verified.\\n2. The customer has at least one existing personal checking account with status OPEN.\\n3. The customer does not exceed 6 business checking accounts.\\n4. The customer has no accounts with status CLOSED.\\n5. The customer's existing checking account has a balance of at least $500.\\n\\n## Opening Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify customer identity.\\n2. Check eligibility requirements listed above.\\n3. Confirm the customer's desired account_class selection.\\n   - Business checking account_class options include Navy Blue, Cobalt Blue, True Blue, etc.\\n4. Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account.\\n\\n10. Internal: Closing Personal Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_005\\n   Score: 15.9381\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Light Blue Account, Light Green Account, Green Fee-Free Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $15 if closed within 30 days\\n  - Notice period: 0 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (Blue Account, Green Account (checking))\\n  - Early closure fee: $25 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 3 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Evergreen Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $50 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 7 days\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (Bluest Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $100 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 14 days\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=3ms, reranking=0ms, total=3ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEcuIxA-2df71jIPhFpimPcK8rhGCEx1J9H9lRIcgD1hMkozEmGaIQPzatAfKbjJZPsTW77zI7q3n-dfJ7IZ5MhBE2-VZZ9zOVRjZluMgsiLdIx-N33E5RkUoiuBTvBN6mgFb_wyKxMr-bDmgjyXEbzXoStT5MiNt20n6KQHRC59m5I7ygyN_ZrUiY-iy7galjXJsOGnRbwJ2mT_VI26Esv_B48scZ3DAd4gSp_zu8i4lt6BJw2Hw7Xb0zuc2l460BwvJNHzIVggd365DBjEHM9zZP0NdG9ycg-h0FTVooz-6BpwduX9y8Rk4rg8hL4muqDX5QnEgGV7ihfSkLXyuOPdQs5nkV_TgBlDOhsBIcVeyYCPJz_Vs0RKVu2bBTYFG_8JWyACspfyCzpgkG2-x6C2YDNdlRxIbYAcnLHbodiLMwTMiaAWzLaDh0LJ5ogZ6rEo1GlPjUyLka9GQr2-rZr6dnpXVoEc-S2XlGTnHB6gglOoLSU99TBFmk1NpaEiAGGNNjbGT0nUMFpOLzl-OBySkXU5P6hAVX_MV4_DFF9bzJ-Z9bldHD-B_f4fy2-3FCJ4NxdwoYJb8FuisDX6RXH_ZMaUGVSmSXYwGEpulqPVX7dW_7JSKcHudJNPsnks36NmHyxO8dnjlSsPpITvfT9gYBUN85pNF4szfeh1oTMN9FWoCIJimXbZcEX0ideN86m8ABsjQnRvWyJVNDBYp9UoGSOdccbysAG8OtRK6i9oPgGQ2WLqm0P_X-vTv5VBrqLuUF-efspbqgmbNoqOBmQUpeSHBdGvua0UA1qps9uaaL0i-K8za5rBuwfXYzp6HfbwJzfP3a8YS0crfA19NUdq5uPlUP3jmfAwXFG1UIDZOeXdjALF-w18XxKJMT2TojJBTAedOHPOEAHldZZS0YtH28XNMrPZJWEr5qESBk7oBq2veIOm3yGgHjb20ELRCJQzLxW1-Qg4as9d_rribTDs5_uWRrFWGfKn4KzoiPkW2lO3jFwtYCBI_PYA8K6l_2IO8CvVQ0Q4iVdUOrAluLZICTmxNeQEUpCxU6w3MFqQ5CJXuveRPE9pMCQYygM8MGqu8vhjDkcT4i2ndARLhQOmQAZK19OdYIcacJPNHwe_xzDFYrS0PV9JCvmMiLqJnlp_Fiw0LZVb9ZacI2bZ9DCksjbklnbbzjIE1xFBnyqdD2clW-57-_BUucRCdkqee2G4BDho5-8fL7gGdilbnNw_QbUTh8OTgGmwlP9_7WidU3PHjQiy0DgTxxZXHkw2SULGjwVBud1dEPB_NkFqjtUirS_AghLd0Whrtinxre13UektA_XdBvLgTp8BB6MtousDPr55BdnzPkn0_3SojcO8-hLz2sHex74Z76NzHdQneKAW6W003dFFqBOu5UviQylKyQm9ZgC6mhkTWzZVM22brlk3qOW0P4d0x_AULnn-xZgo6U99JQ_TiHdPrf2hKHpTeexsqrbwnt8A12mQR1AOKzuRYiq4gTysJEYGIjMeVOwMhOV0gnwjcIJDiqV-FYrDvzirlXtsiXNf62-Yt3UznJBslbH6jODbQGkSCMVpYD0ygI-WugXw2JH4FJZS5-RgvSPq3e_fxPULQrNprZ_SNg4rremxNjdCUpcOtLLK67SUZdyEU9j_52yEe-BnhzngEjiLry2Yad96mdoDEzkkusb7_ymkR3RRY0agMXJ3D_gLIj63n-efKL7XDV6Z_z-LBKKgfQH3oBw4hWvszFTTqpIIeGbXV7qx3PtbYufeTSgNzcF93WCxZQQyqA8mruCBUFHJibGaIzKaof9lCLl615jAY6hWvLxGJxMv07_nq1Gkjyx0-776K1Dbriv69AShuseNctu-C_Q5yYiK_SNdag==\",\"id\":\"rs_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc4729322087d1a526e496fefcc2e0\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"content\":[{\"annotations\":[],\"logprobs\":[],\"text\":\"{\\\"message\\\":\\\"Absolutely—I can help narrow it down to one account instead of giving you another long list. To find the best fit for your landscaping business, tell me:\\\\n\\\\n1. What do you most want that Navy Blue isn’t giving you—higher transfer limits, better earnings on your balance, more personalized support, or something else?\\\\n2. Roughly what balance would you keep in the account, including during your slower season?\\\\n3. Is avoiding a monthly fee essential, or would you pay one for features you’ll actually use?\\\\n\\\\nEstimates are fine; I don’t need to access your account to compare options.\\\"}\",\"type\":\"output_text\"}],\"id\":\"msg_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc472bbe4887d18928d22be8bc70f8\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"message\"},{\"content\":\"What I need most is to stop getting nickeled-and-dimed and have something that actually helps day to day.\\n\\n1) First off, cash flow in landscaping is unpredictable. Some months we’re waiting on big payments. I’ve been burned by overdraft fees before — I absolutely NEED zero overdraft fees. Non-negotiable.\\n\\n2) Balance-wise, I can keep around $3,000 to $5,000 in there most of the time, even in slower months.\\n\\n3) I’m trying to keep overhead low. I don’t want to pay more than $30–40 a month, definitely less than $50. If there’s a fee, I’d want it waived with a balance like that — I don’t want to need $10,000+ just to avoid the fee.\\n\\nAlso, my crews hit ATMs 4–5 times a week at gas stations/convenience stores and we probably spend $15–20 a month on ATM fees. Any rebates? And we spend like $3–4k/month on the debit card for supplies and gas — any cashback on that?\",\"role\":\"user\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"business checking \\\\\\\"overdraft\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"ATM\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"cashback\\\\\\\"\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_7XMBRaTFHkbHIDR6qUrG8kiZ\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc47343e9c87d1a032139cc4a18183\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_7XMBRaTFHkbHIDR6qUrG8kiZ\",\"output\":\"1. Internal: Opening Business Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_003\\n   Score: 7.1174\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nTo open a business checking account, ensure all of the following are true:\\n1. The customer is verified.\\n2. The customer has at least one existing personal checking account with status OPEN.\\n3. The customer does not exceed 6 business checking accounts.\\n4. The customer has no accounts with status CLOSED.\\n5. The customer's existing checking account has a balance of at least $500.\\n\\n## Opening Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify customer identity.\\n2. Check eligibility requirements listed above.\\n3. Confirm the customer's desired account_class selection.\\n   - Business checking account_class options include Navy Blue, Cobalt Blue, True Blue, etc.\\n4. Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account.\\n\\n2. Internal: Opening Business Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_004\\n   Score: 6.6849\\n   Content: ## Description\\n\\nProcedure for opening business savings accounts. Eligibility requirements: 1) Customer must be verified, 2) Customer must already have at least one business checking account with status OPEN, 3) Customer cannot have more than 4 business savings accounts, 4) Customer must not have any accounts with negative balances, 5) Existing business checking account must have been open for at least 30 days, 6) Existing business checking account must have a balance of at least $2,500. Steps: 1) Verify customer identity, 2) Check eligibility requirements, 3) Confirm account selection with customer (business savings account_class options include Bronze Saver Account, Silver Saver Account, etc.), 4) Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account, 5) Ask the customer if they would like you to transfer the opening deposit from their business checking account now. If yes, use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount. If no, inform them they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nConfirm all of the following before proceeding:\\n- Customer identity is verified.\\n- Customer has at least one business checking account with status OPEN.\\n- Customer has fewer than 4 existing business savings accounts.\\n- Customer has no accounts with negative balances.\\n- At least one existing business checking account has been open for at least 30 days.\\n- That business checking account has a current balance of at least $2,500.\\n\\nNotes:\\n- Use the qualifying OPEN business checking account that meets both the tenure and balance thresholds as the source for the optional opening deposit transfer.\\n\\n## Step-by-Step Procedure\\n\\n1) Verify customer identity.\\n2) Check eligibility requirements (see list above).\\n3) Confirm account selection with the customer:\\n   - Ask for the desired business savings account_class (e.g., Bronze Saver Account, Silver Saver Account, etc.).\\n   - Ensure you capture the exact official account_class name ending with “Account.”\\n4) Open the new business savings account using the agent tool (see Tool Instructions below).\\n5) Funding the opening deposit:\\n   - Ask the customer if they want you to transfer the opening deposit now from their eligible business checking account.\\n   - If yes: initiate the internal transfer using the agent tool (see Tool Instructions below).\\n   - If no: inform the customer they have 30 days to fund the account via internal transfer or external deposit; otherwise, the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Agent Tool Instructions\\n\\nThe AGENT calls these tools directly to perform actions on behalf of the customer. Do not expose tool details to the customer.\\n\\n### Tool: open_bank_account_4821\\n\\n- Signature:\\n  - open_bank_account_4821(user_id, account_type, account_class)\\n- When to call:\\n  - After eligibility is confirmed and the customer has selected the desired business savings account_class.\\n- How to call:\\n  - Set account_type to 'savings'.\\n  - Set account_class to the exact official name provided by the customer (e.g., 'Bronze Saver Account').\\n- Expected outcome:\\n  - Returns a new savings account record (capture the new account_id for subsequent actions).\\n\\n### Tool: transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291\\n\\n- Signature:\\n  - transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291(source_account_id, destination_account_id, amount)\\n- When to call:\\n  - Only if the customer authorizes transferring the opening deposit now.\\n- How to call:\\n  - source_account_id: the qualifying OPEN business checking account that meets the 30-day tenure and $2,500 balance requirements.\\n  - destination_account_id: the newly opened business savings account_id.\\n  - amount: the required opening deposit amount confirmed with the customer.\\n- If the transfer fails (e.g., insufficient funds):\\n  - Inform the customer and remind them they have 30 days to fund the account via internal transfer or external deposit, or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Checklist Before Opening\\n\\n- Customer identity verified.\\n- OPEN business checking account identified and qualified (≥ 30 days open and ≥ $2,500 balance).\\n- Savings account count confirmed is < 4.\\n- No negative balances across any accounts.\\n- Customer-confirmed account_class captured exactly.\\n\\n## Post-Opening Actions\\n\\n- If the customer funds now: complete the transfer and confirm success.\\n- If the customer defers funding: clearly communicate the 30-day deadline and acceptable methods (internal transfer or external deposit), and note that the account will be closed if not funded within that timeframe.\\n\\n3. Bronze Saver Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_bronze_saver_account_002\\n   Score: 6.2973\\n   Content: ## Specifications\\n| Item | Details |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Minimum opening deposit | $0 |\\n| Interest compounding frequency | daily |\\n| Linked Rho-Bank business checking required | Yes |\\n\\n## Requirements guidance\\n- Ensure a linked Rho-Bank business checking account remains active if Yes is required for your setup.\\n- Confirm your compounding preference is set to daily in your account details.\\n- Verify the initial funding meets or exceeds $0.\\n\\n4. Gold Saver Account: How Automated Sweeps Work with Business Checking\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_gold_saver_account_002\\n   Score: 5.9537\\n   Content: ## Overview of automated sweeps\\nAutomated sweeps move available funds between your business checking and savings to help you maintain working capital while capturing interest on excess balances.\\n\\n### When sweeps run\\n- Sweeps are evaluated on a daily cadence.\\n\\n### Checking balance threshold\\n- Your checking account aims to maintain at least $1,000.\\n- When available funds exceed this threshold, the excess becomes eligible to move into savings.\\n\\n### What happens during a sweep\\n- The system checks your checking balance against the threshold.\\n- Eligible excess is transferred into savings to optimize idle funds.\\n- If your checking balance is at or below $1,000, no sweep to savings occurs.\\n\\n### Managing sweeps\\n- You can monitor sweep activity in your account activity view.\\n- If you anticipate large outgoing payments, ensure your checking balance remains at or above $1,000 so that a sweep does not reduce funds needed for those payments.\\n\\n5. Internal: Ordering a Debit Card for a Bank Account\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023\\n   Score: 5.8504\\n   Content: Procedure for if the customer inquires about ordering a debit card linked to a specific checking account. Debit cards can only be ordered for checking accounts (personal or business) - savings accounts are not eligible for debit cards.\\n\\nEligibility requirements:\\n1) Customer must be verified\\n2) The account must be a checking account (account_type must be 'checking')\\n3) Account status must be OPEN\\n4) Account must have been open for at least 3 business days (excluding weekends)\\n5) Customer cannot have more than 1 active debit cards per checking account\\n6) Account must have a minimum balance of $25 (to cover potential fees)\\n7) Customer must be at least 18 years old (verify using date_of_birth)\\n8) Customer cannot have a pending debit card order for the same account (check debit_cards table for PENDING status)\\n9) Customer's address on file must be a valid US domestic address (international shipping is not available)\\n \\n\\nDelivery Options:\\n- STANDARD: Free shipping, arrives in 7-10 business days\\n- EXPEDITED: $15 fee, arrives in 3-5 business days\\n- RUSH: $35 fee, arrives in 1-2 business days, fees may vary based on account tier. \\n\\nCard Design Options:\\n- CLASSIC: Standard Rho-Bank blue design (default, no fee)\\n- PREMIUM: Metallic silver finish ($10 one-time fee)\\n- CUSTOM: Customer-uploaded image ($25 one-time fee, subject to approval), fees may vary ased on account tier. \\n\\nSteps:\\n1) Verify customer identity\\n2) Confirm which checking account the debit card should be linked to. \\n3) Check eligibility requirements for the specified account\\n4) Ask customer for preferred delivery option (STANDARD, EXPEDITED, or RUSH) and explain fees. \\n5) Ask customer for preferred card design (CLASSIC, PREMIUM, or CUSTOM) and explain fees. \\n6) Confirm the address that the customer would like to mail the card to. \\n7) Use order_debit_card_5739 to order the card. \\n8) Inform customer of expected delivery timeframe and any applicable fees\\n\\nImportant Notes:\\n- Expedited and rush delivery fees are automatically deducted from the linked checking account\\n- If the account has insufficient funds for delivery or design fees, the order will fail\\n- Customers can track their card shipment status using the Rho-Bank mobile app\\n- New cards are automatically activated upon first use with PIN entry\\n- The customer's existing debit card (if any) will remain active until the new card is activated.\\n\\n6. Internal: Credit Card Rewards - Points vs Cash Back Representation\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_credit_cards_(general)_006\\n   Score: 5.7236\\n   Content: ## Rewards representation\\nDue to a legacy backend migration that has not yet been completed, all credit card rewards in the transaction database are stored as 'points' regardless of whether the card is a cash back card or a points-based card. For cash back cards (Bronze Rewards Card, Silver Rewards Card, Gold Rewards Card, Platinum Rewards Card, Diamond Elite Card, Crypto-Cash Back, Business Bronze Rewards Card, Business Silver Rewards Card, Green Rewards Card, Silver Zoom Card, Business Gold Rewards Card, and Business Platinum Rewards Card), these 'points' should be interpreted as cash back with a conversion rate of 1 point = $0.01 when redeemed as a statement credit or as a credit to the user's Rho-Bank checking account. For example, 250 points equals $2.50 in cash back, which matches a 2.5% cash back rate on a $100 purchase. The only true points-based card is the EcoCard, which earns 'sustainability points' (5 points per dollar on green purchases, 1 point per dollar on other purchases) that also redeem at $0.01 per point when redeemed as a statement credit or checking account credit.\\n\\n7. Gold Saver Account: Integration with Business Checking\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_gold_saver_account_004\\n   Score: 5.4598\\n   Content: ## How integration supports automated movement\\nLinking your business checking enables automatic movement of eligible funds into savings when criteria are met, helping you keep operating funds available while capturing interest on surplus balances.\\n\\n### Fees and thresholds specific to integration\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: $10.00.\\n- Minimum amount required to trigger a sweep transfer: $100.\\n- Automatic sweep transfer fee: $0.00.\\n\\n### How sweep initiation works\\n- A sweep is considered only when the amount available to move meets or exceeds $100.\\n- If activity in checking reduces available funds below the amount needed, no sweep occurs.\\n\\n### Practical tips\\n- Leave headroom in checking for pending transactions so that only true excess is moved.\\n- Review sweep activity and the monthly maintenance fee line item to reconcile your cash management strategy with actual results.\\n\\n8. Lime Green Account: Your Dedicated Account Manager\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_003\\n   Score: 5.1569\\n   Content: ## Response commitments\\n- Direct messages receive a response within 2 business hours.\\n- When calling the priority line, the maximum expected wait is 6 minutes.\\n\\n## How to reach your manager\\n- Send a secure message from within your account's support center and select the option to route to your dedicated manager.\\n- For urgent matters, call the priority support line; your call is queued with elevated priority and subject to the 6 minute maximum wait.\\n\\n## Getting the most out of manager support\\n- Provide context upfront:\\n  - The specific transaction or transfer you need help with.\\n  - Any relevant dates and counterparties.\\n  - Screenshots of error messages (if applicable).\\n- Set your preferred contact method so your manager can follow up quickly.\\n- For time-sensitive requests, note the deadline in your initial message; your manager will respond within 2 business hours.\\n\\n## Escalations\\n- If an issue requires faster handling than messaging, use the priority phone line for a live update within the 6 minute window.\\n\\n## Referral program for Lime Green members\\n\\nAs a Rho-Bank checking account holder, you can refer other businesses to Lime Green and earn substantial rewards:\\n\\n- **Your bonus**: $200 for each successful referral\\n- **Their bonus**: $150 welcome bonus for the referred business\\n- **Annual cap**: 12 referrals per year\\n- **Qualification**: Referred business must deposit $15,000 within 90 days\\n- **Eligibility**: You must have maintained checking account status with Rho-Bank for a minimum of 90 days.\\n\\nSpeak with your dedicated account manager for personalized referral strategies and tracking.\\n\\n9. FAQ: Checking Account Referrals\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_048\\n   Score: 4.8951\\n   Content: ## Frequently asked questions about checking account referrals\\n\\n### How many people can I refer at once?\\nYou can have multiple referrals in progress, but you can only receive a maximum of 2 referral bonuses in any rolling 9-day window. If you exceed this limit, additional referrals will be automatically denied until enough time passes.\\n\\n### Can I refer someone who used to have a Rho-Bank account?\\nNo. The referred person must be a new Rho-Bank customer with no existing or closed accounts within the past 12 months. Former customers must wait 12 months after their last account closure before being eligible as a referral.\\n\\n### Can I refer someone who lives at the same address as me?\\nNo. The referrer and referred person cannot be registered at the same address. This restriction helps prevent abuse of the referral program.\\n\\n### What counts as a qualifying deposit?\\nThe qualifying deposit must be new money brought into Rho-Bank. Transfers from another Rho-Bank account do not count. The deposit can come from an external bank transfer, direct deposit, mobile check deposit, or cash/check deposit at a branch.\\n\\n### What happens if the person I referred closes their account early?\\nIf the referred account is closed within 90 days of opening, your referral bonus may be reversed (clawed back). Both accounts must remain in good standing for bonuses to be retained.\\n\\n### Can I combine the referral bonus with other promotions?\\nNo. The referral bonus cannot be combined with other new account promotions or sign-up bonuses. Only one promotional offer can be applied per new account.\\n\\n### What do the referral statuses mean?\\n- **COMPLETE**: The referral was successful and bonuses will be paid.\\n- **IN_PROGRESS**: The new account is open but hasn't met the qualifying deposit yet.\\n- **NO_PROGRESS**: The referred person hasn't started an application.\\n- **APPLIED**: An application has been submitted and is being reviewed.\\n- **REJECTED**: The referral was denied (usually due to hitting the rolling window limit or eligibility issues).\\n- **ERROR**: A system error occurred; try again later or contact support.\\n\\n### Why was my referral rejected?\\nCommon reasons for rejection include:\\n- You already received 2 referral bonuses in the past 9 days (rolling window limit).\\n- The referred person already has or recently had a Rho-Bank account.\\n- You and the referred person are registered at the same address.\\n- For business referrals: The referred business has the same primary owner as an existing account.\\n\\n### How long do I have to wait after a rejection to refer again?\\nIf your referral was rejected due to the rolling window limit, you must wait until your oldest qualifying referral is more than 9 days old. The limit is based on a rolling window, so you become eligible again as older referrals age out.\\n\\n### Can I refer someone for a business checking account?\\nYes, but the referred business must have a different primary owner (based on SSN of the primary authorized signer) than any existing Rho-Bank business account.\\n\\n### Do I need to have the same account type to refer someone for it?\\nNo. Referrer eligibility hinges on how long you've been a Rho-Bank checking customer, not which product you currently use. The tenure threshold is measured from when you opened your very first checking account with us. Someone with a Navy Blue account can refer others for World Blue, True Blue, or any other checking product—provided they've met the duration requirement.\\n\\n### How long does the referred person have to make the qualifying deposit?\\nThe deposit window varies by account type, typically between 60-120 days. Check the specific account's referral terms for the exact timeframe. After the deposit is made, it must remain in the account for at least 30 additional days.\\n\\n10. Internal: Closing Business Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_008\\n   Score: 4.8719\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n- Customer must have at least one active business checking account remaining (business savings requires a linked business checking account)\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Bronze Saver Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $75 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 10 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (Silver Saver Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $125 if closed within 120 days\\n  - Notice period: 14 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Gold Saver Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $250 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 21 days\\n  - Requires supervisor review\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (Platinum Reserve Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $500 if closed within 270 days\\n  - Notice period: 30 days\\n  - Requires manager approval\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. For PREMIUM tier, obtain supervisor review. For ELITE tier, obtain manager approval.\\n4. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEc4m8r6SsqPA7mTvukJ8Qd5Y34729k6PTx0OFsWHi51eC7yAcK53vWhBdH44x1qT01Qi8H969gXN_DpQIK1F7qIl5tUQKSuOz8KIgRyPTuI3p7jNZk5yKiNZHOpE-0bE1iDrPhSyEUMNu8_9ZR93GjbrFSD9qTNoKzyRymvu3vrL5qjBn2SEhzURcC1msJvIfjrh2XHIi05APGXhfsNyCk5BcA0YCxD21chK0W1-wrTYAsRUZSOUzfgmSXiqU626twL7m5RFkr4Q9afgrpioQb0F-LCPNyrfpt4nJOojGb_LBKig98jtajueZIi0ix_D4aklPogcZ06lwzlm6XTGXRi0D6i_i7U97NaBk4mJr32EmhNpNZSb5-PssBfvDd4ePEKha2pdxJ0JqewQknPzqot7yEdvvhgCWtKxiMjpT2zy3pEQYEvl9JhopQWpPJ2IHCxmEOI2Ap4_-3f3t_iQqJhea_ZdKaw8f1pQqones9D6mdWmkEYbOXVIBI3pn_skkzLt1fIuK3t4995P0oVcGG6OSvY0Pg7oGbzHuboeY_HCzBTx-2HJOWwgHOW0hf_viEgOlm99sRQqQZgMl2QB5Mn8B1vX-6nnmna6hAa2FUuhPeJh1Oht5uTdoNBz0452E1xxtTIC4FfHzV13rvZkk8CipsO7Cv9EnpqzKWsLddffbsUHTyfH4G8gFHWnaUCf1ALWL_kNnmAj9rRYSE92L01bxAk-2ef4uvWQgiUE0xB_erVhqwyLw2PFkV-a_dyOj5NPBHs38XbSe2HbCszAxQR7le-IIAX1EW0AmfepG3EHdkNmFRwGuqm9G5AK5gFxcEGQm1J-y9YSf3RM7dLBQaLxbUl4RdTUdVd5BSVnWyeg2OtAVUGn_MsfVkYwo8SXtyH-81sOjR-zmb74rDATgPFe-mC8sduaKdkidTR_mCKBkKIaL6npwTu-SSvofcOhbrbDBH-ATm9oo7jqVhKbv9ri7VA2FgvYLnASW5zs8qBtkhsgm_P2On8_IukK69jUDMmsFNh4j1zMOrP9U1R6Uh4S0ZQe87H5huz_xXUeV868TMZRkBrO2CtoCDrTD3i43ISdbVye62k4RbL8kp6Qortql8-yb1BV5HOZDHdgUTNmOubyw2GTCymnO3vrU0EO0sPfrl4P-gIkJE2zyGG64ldXzeYeB4lK-3o-M9E367GcCwfWSj0znK0a49eSD9HvOeFtb9Be8m3E7yTQkUstGdy1fDjJJTAGDfJd8RvDOASQgmu4e8WcVgFySCxA9MHtd3J-wMo8uzxTLsXpW_uLBHaY0B2qm4l8s_fktDsidqHwtg=\",\"id\":\"rs_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc4736546887d1af6e11db3b14556f\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"overdraft business checking zero fees\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_4cSYPvrOrEegx63oT4vlDhlV\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc47382ecc87d199f96135fd33b27e\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"business checking ATM rebates debit cashback\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_D5sh1HYOqoSyEIzrTv9iPjkh\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc47382ee087d1abe952dd8c2a60ac\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_4cSYPvrOrEegx63oT4vlDhlV\",\"output\":\"1. Why does my account have a lower balance than I expected or have a negative balance?\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_006\\n   Score: 8.8035\\n   Content: ## What can cause a lower or negative balance\\n- Overdraft protections may temporarily cover transactions, which can display a negative balance until incoming funds post or adjustments complete.\\n- Authorization holds reduce your available balance while a merchant finalizes a purchase or security deposit.\\n- Pending card transactions and checks can decrease available funds before they appear as posted.\\n- Scheduled payments or transfers may be earmarked, lowering your available balance in advance.\\n\\n## How to review and resolve\\n- Check both pending and posted activity to understand current holds and recent payments.\\n- Add funds or transfer money from another account to restore a positive available balance.\\n- If a hold seems higher than expected, contact the merchant to request a release or adjustment.\\n- Review and adjust overdraft settings to align with your preferences for coverage and fees.\\n- If something looks incorrect, contact support with transaction details and timestamps.\\n\\n## Decline Codes Related to Balance Issues\\n\\nIf your debit card was declined due to balance-related reasons, you may have encountered one of these codes:\\n\\n### CODE 51 - Insufficient Funds\\n\\nThe account doesn't have enough funds for the transaction. This is the most common decline but requires careful diagnosis.\\n\\n1. **Check Current Balance**: Look up the customer's accounts to get the checking account balance.\\n\\n2. **If balance APPEARS sufficient** for the transaction amount:\\n   \\n   a. **Check Authorization Holds**: Ask the customer if they have any recent authorization holds that might be reducing their available balance.\\n      - Authorization holds reduce available balance but don't show as posted transactions.\\n      - Common sources: gas stations (often $75-$150 pre-auth), hotels, car rentals, restaurants (tip buffer).\\n      - If holds exist, explain: 'Your posted balance is $[balance], but you may have pending authorization holds reducing your available balance. These holds typically release in 1-3 business days.'\\n\\n   b. **Check Pending Transactions**: Review recent transaction history and look for transactions with status 'pending'.\\n      - Pending debits reduce available balance.\\n      - Explain: 'You have pending transactions totaling $[amount] that haven't posted yet.'\\n\\n   c. **Check Overdraft Settings**: The account's overdraft_pos_enabled field from the account lookup shows if overdraft is enabled for POS.\\n      - Regulation E requires customer opt-in for POS/ATM overdraft coverage.\\n      - If overdraft_pos_enabled is FALSE: 'Your account isn't opted into overdraft coverage for debit card purchases. Would you like me to explain your options?' Then reference the overdraft features documentation.\\n\\n3. **If balance is genuinely insufficient**:\\n   - Inform customer of their balance.\\n   - Offer options: 'Would you like to transfer funds from another account, or would you prefer to make a smaller transaction?'\\n   - If they want to transfer, help them do so.\\n\\n### CODE 52 - No Checking Account\\n\\nThe PIN was accepted but the underlying checking account has issues.\\n\\n1. Look up the customer's accounts to check the account status.\\n\\n2. If account status is CLOSED: 'The checking account linked to this debit card has been closed. This card can no longer be used for transactions.'\\n   - If customer wants to continue banking with Rho-Bank, discuss opening a new checking account.\\n\\n3. If account exists and is OPEN but still getting this code: This may be a system synchronization issue. Advise waiting 10-15 minutes and retrying.\\n\\n2. Understanding Blue Account overdraft fees\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_005\\n   Score: 8.6032\\n   Content: ## Your overdraft fee\\n- Overdraft fee per item: $0.00\\n\\n## Daily maximum\\n- A maximum of 3 overdraft fees can be charged in a single day.\\n\\n## What this means for you\\n- Because the overdraft fee is $0.00, you will not see an overdraft fee amount deducted when your balance goes negative.\\n- You may still notice changes in available balance due to transaction authorizations and settlements, but an overdraft fee amount of $0.00 applies.\\n\\n3. Getting Started with Hunter Green Business Checking\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_hunter_green_001\\n   Score: 8.3673\\n   Content: ## Quick start checklist\\n- Confirm your delivery preference: paperless statements are required (Yes). You will manage statements digitally from day one.\\n- Review pricing: the monthly maintenance fee is $25.00. You can avoid this charge by maintaining at least $5,000 in your account.\\n- Understand earnings: your account earns 1.0% APY on your balance.\\n- Know the overdraft policy: the overdraft fee is $0.00.\\n\\n## Set up essentials\\n- Activate e-statements in your profile settings to ensure uninterrupted delivery, since Yes applies.\\n- Add your funding source and make an initial deposit according to your business needs.\\n- Confirm your balance strategy so that you consistently meet the $5,000 waiver threshold if you want to avoid the $25.00.\\n\\n## Interest and statements\\n- Track your accrued interest at the 1.0% APY in your account activity.\\n- Download statements from your online documents center; statements will reflect any $25.00 assessed and interest credited.\\n\\n## Tips for a smooth start\\n- Set internal reminders to check that your balance remains at or above $5,000 before statement cycle close to avoid $25.00.\\n- If your operations are sensitive to overdrafts, note that the overdraft fee is $0.00.\\n\\n## Referral program\\n\\nOnce you're settled in, consider referring other eco-conscious businesses:\\n\\n- **Referrer reward**: $175 for each successful referral\\n- **New member bonus**: $125 for the business you refer\\n- **Annual limit**: Up to 10 referral bonuses per year\\n- **Requirement**: Referred business must deposit $10,000 within 90 days\\n- **Eligibility**: A minimum relationship duration of 60 days as a checking account holder is required. \\n\\nShare the Hunter Green commitment to sustainability while growing your professional network.\\n\\n4. Green Account (checking) at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_account_(checking)_001\\n   Score: 8.3417\\n   Content: ## Highlights\\n- No overdraft fees and no overdraft coverage; transactions that exceed your available balance are declined\\n- Earn 0.11% APY on your checking balance\\n- Get direct deposits up to 1 day early\\n- Mobile check deposits up to $3,000 per day\\n- Boost a linked savings account's APY: Gold +0.75% or Silver +0.25%\\n\\n## Fees and limits\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum daily balance to waive fee | $1,350 |\\n| Paper statement fee (monthly) | $2.50 |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $3.00 |\\n| Returned deposit fee | $17.50 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire (receive) | $15.00 |\\n| APY on balance | 0.11% |\\n| Daily mobile check deposit limit | $3,000 |\\n| Early direct deposit | Up to 1 day early |\\n\\n## Referral program\\nRefer friends and family to open a Green Account and earn rewards:\\n- You earn: $20 per successful referral\\n- They receive: $30 welcome bonus\\n- Maximum referrals per year: 5\\n- Qualifying deposit required: $500 within 60 days\\n- Account tenure requirement: 30 days since becoming a Rho-Bank checking customer.\\n\\n## Important details\\n- To avoid the monthly maintenance fee, maintain a minimum daily balance of $1,350 each statement cycle\\n- If you opt for paper statements, a $2.50 monthly fee applies\\n- Using a non-network ATM incurs a $3.00 fee; the ATM owner may charge additional fees\\n- Deposited checks returned unpaid result in a $17.50 fee\\n- Receiving a domestic wire transfer costs $15.00\\n- Early direct deposit availability depends on when your payer submits the deposit; funds can post up to 1 day early\\n- Savings APY boosts apply when you link an eligible Gold or Silver Savings Account: +0.75% or +0.25% respectively\\n\\n5. Blue Account features and fees\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_003\\n   Score: 8.3057\\n   Content: ## Key Features\\n- No overdraft fees on the account\\n- Waivable monthly maintenance fee: $20.00; waived when your minimum daily balance is at least $625\\n\\n## Optional Add-On\\n### Overdraft Protection Transfers\\n- If you opt in to overdraft protection, each transfer from a linked account to cover a negative balance incurs a $12.50 fee\\n- No overdraft fees are charged by the account itself\\n\\n## Fees\\n| Item | Amount | When it applies |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $20.00 | Charged monthly; waived with a minimum daily balance of $625 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $2.50 | Per month if you choose mailed paper statements |\\n| Returned deposit | $15.00 | Per deposited item returned unpaid |\\n| Incoming domestic wire transfer | $12.50 | Per incoming domestic wire |\\n| Stop payment on a check | $30 | Per stop payment request |\\n\\n## Linked Savings APY Boosts\\n- When linked to a Silver Plus Savings Account: +0.35% APY boost\\n- When linked to a Platinum Savings Account: +0.8% APY boost\\n\\n## Ways to Reduce or Avoid Fees\\n- Maintain a minimum daily balance of $625 to waive the $20.00 monthly maintenance fee\\n- Choose e-statements to avoid the $2.50 paper statement fee\\n- Use in-network ATMs to avoid out-of-network ATM fees\\n- Only enable overdraft protection if you need it, as each transfer incurs a $12.50 fee\\n\\n6. Internal: Ordering a Debit Card for a Bank Account\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023\\n   Score: 8.1760\\n   Content: Procedure for if the customer inquires about ordering a debit card linked to a specific checking account. Debit cards can only be ordered for checking accounts (personal or business) - savings accounts are not eligible for debit cards.\\n\\nEligibility requirements:\\n1) Customer must be verified\\n2) The account must be a checking account (account_type must be 'checking')\\n3) Account status must be OPEN\\n4) Account must have been open for at least 3 business days (excluding weekends)\\n5) Customer cannot have more than 1 active debit cards per checking account\\n6) Account must have a minimum balance of $25 (to cover potential fees)\\n7) Customer must be at least 18 years old (verify using date_of_birth)\\n8) Customer cannot have a pending debit card order for the same account (check debit_cards table for PENDING status)\\n9) Customer's address on file must be a valid US domestic address (international shipping is not available)\\n \\n\\nDelivery Options:\\n- STANDARD: Free shipping, arrives in 7-10 business days\\n- EXPEDITED: $15 fee, arrives in 3-5 business days\\n- RUSH: $35 fee, arrives in 1-2 business days, fees may vary based on account tier. \\n\\nCard Design Options:\\n- CLASSIC: Standard Rho-Bank blue design (default, no fee)\\n- PREMIUM: Metallic silver finish ($10 one-time fee)\\n- CUSTOM: Customer-uploaded image ($25 one-time fee, subject to approval), fees may vary ased on account tier. \\n\\nSteps:\\n1) Verify customer identity\\n2) Confirm which checking account the debit card should be linked to. \\n3) Check eligibility requirements for the specified account\\n4) Ask customer for preferred delivery option (STANDARD, EXPEDITED, or RUSH) and explain fees. \\n5) Ask customer for preferred card design (CLASSIC, PREMIUM, or CUSTOM) and explain fees. \\n6) Confirm the address that the customer would like to mail the card to. \\n7) Use order_debit_card_5739 to order the card. \\n8) Inform customer of expected delivery timeframe and any applicable fees\\n\\nImportant Notes:\\n- Expedited and rush delivery fees are automatically deducted from the linked checking account\\n- If the account has insufficient funds for delivery or design fees, the order will fail\\n- Customers can track their card shipment status using the Rho-Bank mobile app\\n- New cards are automatically activated upon first use with PIN entry\\n- The customer's existing debit card (if any) will remain active until the new card is activated.\\n\\n7. Why am I being charged an overdraft fee on my Blue Account?\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_008\\n   Score: 7.8450\\n   Content: ## Check the fee you see\\n- The overdraft fee on this account is $0.00. If a charge appears labeled as an overdraft fee, review the transaction details to confirm the fee type.\\n\\n## Daily limits, if a fee ever posts in error\\n- Even if a non-zero overdraft fee were posted in error, the number of overdraft fees that can be charged in a single day is capped at 3.\\n\\n## What to do next\\n- Open the transaction in your activity view and review the description to verify the fee type.\\n- Check your monthly statement for the same entry to confirm how it is categorized.\\n- If the fee appears misclassified as an overdraft fee, contact us so we can investigate and correct it.\\n\\n8. Navy Blue Account: Overdraft Protection and Fees\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_navy_blue_002\\n   Score: 7.7915\\n   Content: ## Overdraft options\\nYou can choose whether transactions are covered when your available balance is not sufficient.\\n\\n### If an overdraft occurs\\n- Overdraft fee per occurrence: $0.00\\n- The fee is assessed when a covered transaction settles into a negative available balance.\\n\\n### Overdraft protection via linked account\\n- When enabled, funds can be transferred automatically from a linked eligible account to cover a shortfall.\\n- Transfer fee for overdraft protection: $0.00\\n\\n### How to manage your settings\\n- In your online or mobile banking, navigate to account settings and choose your overdraft preference.\\n- If you enable protection, confirm the linked funding source and authorize automatic transfers.\\n- You can change your preference at any time before a transaction settles.\\n\\n### When fees do not apply\\n- If a transaction is declined due to insufficient funds, no overdraft occurs and $0.00 does not apply.\\n- If overdraft protection fully covers the shortfall, only the protection transfer fee $0.00 may apply.\\n\\n### Disputes and adjustments\\n- If you believe an overdraft was charged in error, contact support promptly with the transaction details.\\n- Reversals are evaluated case by case based on posting order and available balance at the time of settlement.\\n\\n9. Dark Green Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_dark_green_account_002\\n   Score: 7.7012\\n   Content: ## Eligibility requirements\\n- The primary account holder must be at least 17.\\n- You can maintain the account through 26.\\n\\n## Fee schedule\\nThe following fees apply to this account.\\n\\n| Fee | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Monthly maintenance | $10.00 |\\n| Overdraft protection transfer | 0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal | 2.5% of amount (max $6.00) |\\n| Returned deposit | $10.00 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire | $7.50 |\\n\\n## Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- When you withdraw cash from an ATM abroad, a fee of 2.5% of the withdrawal amount is charged.\\n- The fee is capped at a maximum of $6.00 per transaction, protecting you from excessive fees on larger withdrawals.\\n- Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n## Transaction limits\\n- Debit card daily purchase limit: $1,500\\n- Daily ATM withdrawal limit: $300\\n\\n## Overdraft protection transfers\\n- When enabled and available, transfers from a linked funding source to cover an overdraft incur a transfer fee of 0.\\n\\n10. True Blue Account: Fee Waivers and Balance Requirements\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_002\\n   Score: 7.3677\\n   Content: ## Waiving your monthly maintenance fee\\n- You will be charged $75.00 each month unless you meet the waiver threshold.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is waived when your balance is at least $50,000 during the statement period.\\n\\n## Minimum balance requirement vs. fee waiver threshold\\n- Minimum balance requirement: $25,000 to maintain the account and access premium features.\\n- Fee waiver threshold: $50,000 to waive the $75.00 monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Falling below $25,000 may limit access to premium features until your balance is restored.\\n\\n## Overdrafts and shortfalls\\n- If your balance goes negative, a per-occurrence overdraft fee of $25.00 may apply.\\n\\n## How to avoid fees\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $50,000 to waive the monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Set internal processes to monitor balances against both $25,000 and $50,000.\\n- If a shortfall is anticipated, transfer funds promptly to avoid the $25.00 and preserve eligibility for the fee waiver.\\n\\n## True Blue Referral Program\\n\\nRefer other high-volume businesses to True Blue and earn significant rewards:\\n\\n| Benefit | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Referrer bonus | $350 per referral |\\n| New member bonus | $250 |\\n| Maximum referrals per year | 15 |\\n| Qualifying deposit | $50,000 |\\n| Deposit window | 120 days |\\n| Account age requirement | 90 days |\\n\\n### Referral requirements\\n- The referred business must deposit $50,000 within 120 days of opening their True Blue account.\\n- Eligibility is based on how long you've been a Rho-Bank checking customer. The account age threshold is 90 days, calculated from when you opened your oldest checking account.\\n- Referral bonuses are paid after qualification is confirmed and are subject to the annual limit of 15.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_D5sh1HYOqoSyEIzrTv9iPjkh\",\"output\":\"1. Using ATMs worldwide\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_004\\n   Score: 15.0848\\n   Content: ## Daily ATM withdrawal limit\\n- Your Purple Account debit card has a daily ATM withdrawal limit of $1,000. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals worldwide within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n## How ATM rebates work\\n- You are eligible for refunds of ATM operator fees up to a monthly cap of $30.\\n- Rebates apply after eligible ATM fees post to your account and are credited up to the monthly cap.\\n\\n## Best practices when withdrawing cash abroad\\n- Choose the checking account option on the ATM when prompted.\\n- Retain the ATM receipt if it shows a surcharge to help with any rebate review.\\n- Avoid optional dynamic currency conversion at the ATM if you prefer to be billed in the local currency.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n- If you believe a rebate is missing, verify whether your monthly total rebates have reached $30 and confirm that the charge was coded as an ATM operator fee.\\n\\n2. ATM fee rebates for Bluest\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_007\\n   Score: 13.6572\\n   Content: ## Daily ATM withdrawal limit\\n- Your Bluest Account debit card has a daily ATM withdrawal limit of $1,500. This applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n## Monthly rebate cap\\n- You are eligible for ATM fee rebates up to $50 per month.\\n\\n### How rebates are applied\\n- Rebates are credited until you reach the monthly maximum of $50.\\n- If your aggregate ATM fees exceed $50 in a given month, the excess will not be rebated.\\n\\n### Tips for maximizing rebates\\n- Keep track of your cumulative ATM fees during the month to stay within the $50 cap.\\n- Consider using fee-free ATMs once you approach the monthly cap.\\n\\n3. Earning Rewards with Your Cobalt Blue Debit Card\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_004\\n   Score: 13.5680\\n   Content: ## Your rewards rate\\n- Earn 1.0% cashback on eligible debit card purchases\\n\\n## How rewards accrue and post\\n- Rewards accrue as your purchases settle\\n- Cashback is calculated at 1.0% on the net purchase amount after any returns or adjustments\\n- If a purchase is reversed or refunded, the associated rewards are reversed as well\\n\\n## Tips to maximize rewards\\n- Use your debit card for eligible vendor payments where cards are accepted\\n- Review settlements rather than authorizations to confirm rewards on completed purchases\\n\\n## Managing cards for your team\\n- You can request up to 6 business debit cards for team members\\n- Assign cards thoughtfully to concentrate eligible spend while maintaining operational control\\n\\n## Tracking rewards\\n- Monitor earned, pending, and posted rewards in your rewards dashboard\\n- Use category filters to identify vendors where debit is most frequently accepted\\n\\n4. Evergreen Account at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_evergreen_account_001\\n   Score: 13.4990\\n   Content: ## Key highlights\\n- One tree planted for every $750 you spend with your debit card\\n- Automatic carbon offset on purchases: $1.25 g CO2 per $1 spent\\n- Earn 0.05% APY on your checking balance\\n- Extra rewards at partner eco-friendly brands: +1.75% cashback\\n- Early direct deposit: get your paycheck up to 2 days early\\n- Mobile check deposit daily limit: $3,500\\n\\n### Linked savings boosts\\n- Link a Green Account (savings): +0.55% APY boost\\n- Link a Diamond Elite Savings Account: +0.15% APY boost\\n\\n### How tree planting works (at a glance)\\n- For every $750 in eligible spending, we plant one tree on your behalf.\\n- Example: Spend $750 → 1 tree planted; spend 5× that amount → 5 trees planted.\\n\\n### Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawal fee: 2% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $3.00 per transaction.\\n- Third-party ATM operator fees may also apply.\\n\\n### Refer and grow the green community\\n- Refer others to join Evergreen and earn $35 per successful referral\\n- New members receive $25 as a welcome bonus\\n- Earn up to 6 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n\\n## Quick reference\\n| Feature | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Tree planting threshold | $750 per tree |\\n| Carbon offset rate | $1.25 g per $1 |\\n| Checking APY | 0.05% |\\n| Eco brand cashback bonus | +1.75% |\\n| Early direct deposit | Up to 2 days early |\\n| Mobile deposit daily limit | $3,500 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 2% (min $3.00) |\\n| Green Savings APY boost | +0.55% |\\n| Diamond Elite Savings APY boost | +0.15% |\\n| Referral bonus (you earn) | $35 |\\n| Referral bonus (they receive) | $25 |\\n| Max referrals per year | 6 |\\n\\n5. Earning Cashback from Eco-Friendly Vendors\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_hunter_green_003\\n   Score: 13.3878\\n   Content: ## Your cashback rate and network\\n- Earn 2.0% cashback on eligible purchases from certified eco-friendly vendors.\\n- The network includes approximately $2,500 certified green vendors across categories relevant to sustainable operations.\\n\\n## How to earn\\n- Pay with your Hunter Green business debit or payment instrument at participating certified vendors.\\n- Ensure the merchant is identified as certified in our green vendor network at the time of purchase for 2.0% to apply.\\n\\n## Posting, tracking, and returns\\n- Cashback accrues after eligible transactions finalize. You can track accumulated rewards in your account activity.\\n- If a purchase is refunded or disputed, the related cashback may be reversed.\\n\\n## Common exclusions\\n- Purchases at non-certified merchants do not earn 2.0%.\\n- Certain transaction types may be ineligible at the merchant or network level if they cannot be categorized as certified green.\\n\\n6. Navy Blue Account: Mobile Deposits and Daily Limits\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_navy_blue_005\\n   Score: 11.8749\\n   Content: ## Mobile check deposits\\n- Daily mobile deposit limit: $5,000\\n- Endorse checks according to the app instructions and submit clear images to avoid delays.\\n\\n## Digital transfer limits\\n- Daily digital transfer limit: $25,000\\n- If your planned transfer exceeds $25,000, schedule it in multiple submissions across business days.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n- Monthly cap on ATM fee rebates for out-of-network usage: 10\\n- Rebates are applied to qualifying ATM surcharge amounts up to the monthly cap.\\n\\n## Best practices\\n- Deposit earlier in the business day to allow for review and availability under standard timelines.\\n- Retain original checks until you confirm the deposit has posted.\\n- Plan outgoing transfers with the daily ceiling of $25,000 in mind.\\n\\n7. Silver Plus: ATM fee rebate program\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_003\\n   Score: 10.7687\\n   Content: ## Monthly rebate allowance\\n- You are eligible for ATM fee rebates up to 25 per month.\\n\\n### How rebates apply\\n- Rebates are intended to offset ATM operator surcharges incurred on eligible ATM cash withdrawals.\\n- Once your monthly rebate total reaches 25, additional ATM fees will not be rebated for that month.\\n\\n### Important distinctions\\n- The ATM fee rebates are separate from any excess withdrawal charges. If you exceed your monthly free withdrawal limit, an excess withdrawal fee of $1.00 per additional withdrawal may apply.\\n\\n### Tips for maximizing rebates\\n- Use ATMs as needed and track your cumulative rebates so you stay within the 25 monthly allowance.\\n- Keep your withdrawal count in mind to avoid the separate excess withdrawal fee of $1.00 when you pass the free limit.\\n\\n8. Internal: Retrieving Debit Card Information\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_028\\n   Score: 10.5164\\n   Content: Tool for retrieving debit card information for a customer's checking account. Use get_debit_cards_by_account_id_7823 to look up all debit cards associated with a specific checking account.\\n\\n## Tool Usage\\n\\nget_debit_cards_by_account_id_7823(account_id) - account_id is the checking account ID to retrieve debit cards for.\\n\\n## Debit Card Fields Returned\\n\\n- card_id: Unique identifier for the debit card\\n- account_id: The checking account ID the card is linked to\\n- user_id: The user ID of the cardholder\\n- card_number_last_4: Last 4 digits of the card number\\n- status: Current status of the card (ACTIVE, PENDING, FROZEN, CLOSED)\\n- issue_reason: Why the card was issued (new_account, first_card, lost, stolen, fraud, expired, damaged, upgrade, bank_reissue)\\n- expiration_date: Card expiration date (MM/YY format)\\n- date_issued: Date the card was issued\\n- card_design: Design type (CLASSIC, PREMIUM, CUSTOM)\\n- daily_purchase_limit: Maximum daily purchase amount\\n- daily_atm_limit: Maximum daily ATM withdrawal amount\\n\\n## Common Use Cases\\n\\n1. Before ordering a new debit card: Check if customer already has an active or pending card for the account\\n2. Before activating a card: Look up the issue_reason to determine which activation tool to use\\n3. Before freezing/unfreezing: Verify the card exists and check its current status\\n4. Before closing a card: Confirm the card_id and current status\\n5. Customer inquiries: Look up card details when customer asks about their debit card\\n\\n## Important Notes\\n\\n- This tool only returns debit cards for checking accounts (savings accounts do not have debit cards)\\n- Multiple cards may be returned if the account has card history (e.g., old closed cards plus current active card)\\n- For privacy, full card numbers are never returned - only the last 4 digits\\n- If no cards exist for the account, an empty list is returned\\n\\n9. True Blue Account: Same-Day ACH and Mobile Deposits\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_007\\n   Score: 10.3810\\n   Content: ## Same-day ACH\\n- Same-day ACH transfers included at no additional fee: Yes\\n- Submit ACH files as same-day when time-sensitive; designate the correct same-day option during initiation.\\n\\n## Mobile check deposits\\n- Daily mobile deposit limit: $50,000\\n- If a deposit would put you over $50,000 for the day, wait until the next business day or split deposits across days.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n- Maximum ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network usage: $30\\n- Retain your ATM receipts and ensure the rebated amount does not exceed $30 in a monthly cycle.\\n\\n## Best practices\\n- Use same-day ACH for urgent disbursements and standard ACH for routine payments to optimize cost and speed.\\n- Endorse checks clearly and verify amounts before mobile deposit to avoid rejection within the daily limit.\\n\\n10. Internal: Ordering a Debit Card for a Bank Account\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023\\n   Score: 10.3619\\n   Content: Procedure for if the customer inquires about ordering a debit card linked to a specific checking account. Debit cards can only be ordered for checking accounts (personal or business) - savings accounts are not eligible for debit cards.\\n\\nEligibility requirements:\\n1) Customer must be verified\\n2) The account must be a checking account (account_type must be 'checking')\\n3) Account status must be OPEN\\n4) Account must have been open for at least 3 business days (excluding weekends)\\n5) Customer cannot have more than 1 active debit cards per checking account\\n6) Account must have a minimum balance of $25 (to cover potential fees)\\n7) Customer must be at least 18 years old (verify using date_of_birth)\\n8) Customer cannot have a pending debit card order for the same account (check debit_cards table for PENDING status)\\n9) Customer's address on file must be a valid US domestic address (international shipping is not available)\\n \\n\\nDelivery Options:\\n- STANDARD: Free shipping, arrives in 7-10 business days\\n- EXPEDITED: $15 fee, arrives in 3-5 business days\\n- RUSH: $35 fee, arrives in 1-2 business days, fees may vary based on account tier. \\n\\nCard Design Options:\\n- CLASSIC: Standard Rho-Bank blue design (default, no fee)\\n- PREMIUM: Metallic silver finish ($10 one-time fee)\\n- CUSTOM: Customer-uploaded image ($25 one-time fee, subject to approval), fees may vary ased on account tier. \\n\\nSteps:\\n1) Verify customer identity\\n2) Confirm which checking account the debit card should be linked to. \\n3) Check eligibility requirements for the specified account\\n4) Ask customer for preferred delivery option (STANDARD, EXPEDITED, or RUSH) and explain fees. \\n5) Ask customer for preferred card design (CLASSIC, PREMIUM, or CUSTOM) and explain fees. \\n6) Confirm the address that the customer would like to mail the card to. \\n7) Use order_debit_card_5739 to order the card. \\n8) Inform customer of expected delivery timeframe and any applicable fees\\n\\nImportant Notes:\\n- Expedited and rush delivery fees are automatically deducted from the linked checking account\\n- If the account has insufficient funds for delivery or design fees, the order will fail\\n- Customers can track their card shipment status using the Rho-Bank mobile app\\n- New cards are automatically activated upon first use with PIN entry\\n- The customer's existing debit card (if any) will remain active until the new card is activated.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Cobalt Blue account fees overdraft ATM waiver balance\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_mFEDzIQzGIjYbpqpCpo05D3E\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc473ac3b887d199d0e802c80338eb\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Sky Blue account fees overdraft ATM waiver balance\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_KiDSojBwpJVNjig54Fnad5Zj\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc473ac3c887d189a02fecfea09597\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Lime Green account fees overdraft ATM waiver balance\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_DRJ1KJo2seeqeYQSqR1EPYUc\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc473ac3d087d1b69d508d7a7dc07c\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_mFEDzIQzGIjYbpqpCpo05D3E\",\"output\":\"1. Troubleshooting: Unexpected Charges on Cobalt Blue\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_009\\n   Score: 19.2825\\n   Content: ## Identify the charge\\n- Review the exact transaction description on your statement or in your transaction history (e.g., “Monthly Maintenance Fee,” “Wire Transfer – Domestic,” “ATM Fee,” “International ATM Withdrawal Fee,” “Excess Transaction Fee”).\\n- Note the posting date, amount, and any memo or terminal/location details.\\n- Compare the posting date to your recent account activity (wires sent, ATM withdrawals, transaction volume, month-end).\\n\\n## Common Cobalt Blue charges that may appear\\n| Line item on statement | Why it appears | How to confirm | Amount |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly Maintenance Fee | Your account did not meet the balance waiver requirement during the statement period. | Check the Fee Summary on your statement and verify whether your balance met $2,500 for the period. | $20.00 |\\n| Excess Transaction Fee | You exceeded your monthly free transaction limit. | Count your posted transactions for the statement period and compare to your free allowance; the fee line often notes the number of excess items. | $0.25 per excess transaction |\\n| Wire Transfer Fee – Domestic | You initiated a domestic wire transfer. | Confirm a wire was submitted on or near the posting date in your transfer history. | $20.00 |\\n| ATM Fee – Out of Network | You used a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | Match the fee date to an ATM withdrawal at a non‑Rho terminal. Note: the ATM owner may also assess a separate surcharge. | $2.00 per ATM transaction |\\n| International ATM Withdrawal Fee | You withdrew cash at a foreign (international) ATM. | Match the fee date/location to an overseas ATM withdrawal. | 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, minimum $4.00 |\\n\\nNote: Cobalt Blue does not assess overdraft fees. If you see a charge that appears to be an overdraft fee, review the line’s exact description—it may correspond to one of the fees above. If still unclear, request a review.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting by charge type\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee posted unexpectedly\\n- Verify whether your account met the waiver balance requirement of $2,500 during the statement period.\\n- Check if the fee posted at or just after the statement cycle date.\\n- Compare your balance history for the full period; large debits near period‑end can affect waiver eligibility.\\n- If you believe you qualified for the waiver, request a fee review and include your statement period dates and balance evidence.\\n\\n### Excess Transaction Fee you didn’t anticipate\\n- Add up your posted transactions for the statement period and compare to your plan’s free monthly transaction limit.\\n- Open the fee detail to see how many items were assessed at $0.25 each.\\n- If the count appears off, provide a list of the transactions you believe were miscounted when requesting a review.\\n\\n### Wire Transfer Fee – Domestic you didn’t expect\\n- Confirm whether a domestic wire was sent on the fee date (or one business day prior).\\n- Distinguish wires from other transfers by the transaction description (“Wire,” routing via Fedwire, etc.).\\n- If you did not authorize a wire, report immediately for investigation. Otherwise, the standard fee is $20.00.\\n\\n### ATM fees: domestic vs. international\\n- Out‑of‑network (domestic) ATM usage: Expect $2.00 per ATM transaction. This is separate from any surcharge by the ATM owner, which can appear as a separate line item.\\n- Foreign (international) ATM withdrawals: The fee is 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00. Example: for a withdrawal, multiply the amount by 2.5%; if that result is less than $4.00, the minimum applies.\\n\\n## Quick checklist before requesting a review\\n- Match the fee’s posting date to a specific action (wire, ATM withdrawal, month‑end, spike in transaction volume).\\n- Capture screenshots of:\\n  - The fee line item (showing date, amount, and description)\\n  - Any related transaction (wire confirmation, ATM withdrawal)\\n  - The relevant statement page (Fee Summary and balance history for the period)\\n- Briefly explain why the fee appears incorrect (e.g., you met $2,500 during the period, transaction count appears miscalculated, withdrawal was domestic vs. international, etc.).\\n\\n## Requesting a review or dispute\\n- Contact us as soon as you notice the charge.\\n- Include: account name, last 4 digits, statement period, fee date/amount/description, and your supporting screenshots or documents.\\n- We will investigate and correct any misapplied fees. If additional information is needed (e.g., to verify ATM location or wire authorization), we will follow up.\\n\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account features\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_fee-free_account_005\\n   Score: 17.9215\\n   Content: ## Key Features and Fees\\n\\n| Item | Details |\\n|---|---|\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum balance to waive monthly fee | $150 (minimum daily balance) |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $0.00 |\\n| Stop payment fee (per request) | $25 |\\n| Daily ATM withdrawal limit | $500 |\\n| APY boost with linked Bronze Savings | 0.4% |\\n| APY boost with linked Gold Plus Savings | 0.35% |\\n\\n### No Overdraft Charges\\n- You are not charged an overdraft fee. The overdraft fee for this account is $0.00.\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee and Waiver\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $22.50.\\n- It is waived when you maintain a minimum daily balance of $150 during the statement cycle.\\n- If the waiver requirement is met, the fee for that cycle is not charged; otherwise, the $22.50 fee is assessed at cycle end.\\n\\n### ATM Withdrawals\\n- Rho does not charge a fee for using out-of-network ATMs: $0.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals are also fee-free: $0.00 per withdrawal. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n- Your daily ATM withdrawal limit is $500. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n### Statements\\n- Paper statements are provided without a monthly fee: $0.00.\\n\\n### Stop Payments\\n- Stop payment requests incur a fee of $25 per item.\\n\\n### Savings APY Boosts (when linked)\\n- Link a Bronze Savings Account to receive a 0.4% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n- Link a Gold Plus Savings Account to receive a 0.35% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n\\n3. True Blue Account: Fee Waivers and Balance Requirements\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_002\\n   Score: 17.2421\\n   Content: ## Waiving your monthly maintenance fee\\n- You will be charged $75.00 each month unless you meet the waiver threshold.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is waived when your balance is at least $50,000 during the statement period.\\n\\n## Minimum balance requirement vs. fee waiver threshold\\n- Minimum balance requirement: $25,000 to maintain the account and access premium features.\\n- Fee waiver threshold: $50,000 to waive the $75.00 monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Falling below $25,000 may limit access to premium features until your balance is restored.\\n\\n## Overdrafts and shortfalls\\n- If your balance goes negative, a per-occurrence overdraft fee of $25.00 may apply.\\n\\n## How to avoid fees\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $50,000 to waive the monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Set internal processes to monitor balances against both $25,000 and $50,000.\\n- If a shortfall is anticipated, transfer funds promptly to avoid the $25.00 and preserve eligibility for the fee waiver.\\n\\n## True Blue Referral Program\\n\\nRefer other high-volume businesses to True Blue and earn significant rewards:\\n\\n| Benefit | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Referrer bonus | $350 per referral |\\n| New member bonus | $250 |\\n| Maximum referrals per year | 15 |\\n| Qualifying deposit | $50,000 |\\n| Deposit window | 120 days |\\n| Account age requirement | 90 days |\\n\\n### Referral requirements\\n- The referred business must deposit $50,000 within 120 days of opening their True Blue account.\\n- Eligibility is based on how long you've been a Rho-Bank checking customer. The account age threshold is 90 days, calculated from when you opened your oldest checking account.\\n- Referral bonuses are paid after qualification is confirmed and are subject to the annual limit of 15.\\n\\n4. Why am I being charged a fee on my True Blue Account?\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_010\\n   Score: 14.6847\\n   Content: ## Common reasons you’re seeing a fee\\n\\nBelow are the most common fee types that can appear on a True Blue account and why they’re charged.\\n\\n| Fee type | When you’ll see it | Amount posted |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly Maintenance Fee | Your qualifying balance did not meet the waiver threshold for the applicable evaluation period | $75.00 (waived when balance requirement of $50,000 is met) |\\n| Domestic Wire Transfer Fee | You sent a domestic wire from your account | $5.00 per outbound domestic wire |\\n| Out-of-Network ATM Fee | You completed a transaction at a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM Withdrawal Fee | You withdrew cash at an international (non‑U.S.) ATM | 2% of the withdrawal amount; minimum $3.00 |\\n\\n### Example for foreign ATM fee\\n- If you withdraw $200 at a foreign ATM, the fee is 2% of $200 ($4). Because $4 exceeds the minimum $3.00, $4 would post.\\n\\n## How to confirm which fee was charged\\n\\n1. Check your latest statement or transaction history for the fee line item and posted amount.  \\n2. Match the posted amount to the fees above:\\n   - $75.00 typically indicates the Monthly Maintenance Fee.\\n   - $5.00 typically indicates a Domestic Wire Transfer Fee.\\n   - $1.00 typically indicates an Out-of-Network ATM Fee.\\n   - A calculated amount equal to 2% of your ATM withdrawal (or $3.00, whichever is higher) indicates a Foreign ATM Withdrawal Fee.\\n3. For the Monthly Maintenance Fee, compare your balance during the billing period to the waiver threshold of $50,000.\\n\\n## How to reduce or avoid future fees\\n\\n- Maintain at least $50,000 to have the $75.00 waived.  \\n- Use Rho in‑network ATMs to avoid the $1.00.  \\n- When abroad, be aware that each cash withdrawal will incur 2% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $3.00.  \\n- Send domestic wires only when necessary to limit paying $5.00 per wire.\\n\\n## Need help?\\n\\nIf you believe a fee was posted in error, gather the transaction date, amount, and any related activity (e.g., wire reference or ATM withdrawal details) and contact support for a review.\\n\\n5. Dark Green Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_dark_green_account_002\\n   Score: 13.8617\\n   Content: ## Eligibility requirements\\n- The primary account holder must be at least 17.\\n- You can maintain the account through 26.\\n\\n## Fee schedule\\nThe following fees apply to this account.\\n\\n| Fee | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Monthly maintenance | $10.00 |\\n| Overdraft protection transfer | 0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal | 2.5% of amount (max $6.00) |\\n| Returned deposit | $10.00 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire | $7.50 |\\n\\n## Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- When you withdraw cash from an ATM abroad, a fee of 2.5% of the withdrawal amount is charged.\\n- The fee is capped at a maximum of $6.00 per transaction, protecting you from excessive fees on larger withdrawals.\\n- Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n## Transaction limits\\n- Debit card daily purchase limit: $1,500\\n- Daily ATM withdrawal limit: $300\\n\\n## Overdraft protection transfers\\n- When enabled and available, transfers from a linked funding source to cover an overdraft incur a transfer fee of 0.\\n\\n6. Blue Account features and fees\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_003\\n   Score: 13.8335\\n   Content: ## Key Features\\n- No overdraft fees on the account\\n- Waivable monthly maintenance fee: $20.00; waived when your minimum daily balance is at least $625\\n\\n## Optional Add-On\\n### Overdraft Protection Transfers\\n- If you opt in to overdraft protection, each transfer from a linked account to cover a negative balance incurs a $12.50 fee\\n- No overdraft fees are charged by the account itself\\n\\n## Fees\\n| Item | Amount | When it applies |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $20.00 | Charged monthly; waived with a minimum daily balance of $625 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $2.50 | Per month if you choose mailed paper statements |\\n| Returned deposit | $15.00 | Per deposited item returned unpaid |\\n| Incoming domestic wire transfer | $12.50 | Per incoming domestic wire |\\n| Stop payment on a check | $30 | Per stop payment request |\\n\\n## Linked Savings APY Boosts\\n- When linked to a Silver Plus Savings Account: +0.35% APY boost\\n- When linked to a Platinum Savings Account: +0.8% APY boost\\n\\n## Ways to Reduce or Avoid Fees\\n- Maintain a minimum daily balance of $625 to waive the $20.00 monthly maintenance fee\\n- Choose e-statements to avoid the $2.50 paper statement fee\\n- Use in-network ATMs to avoid out-of-network ATM fees\\n- Only enable overdraft protection if you need it, as each transfer incurs a $12.50 fee\\n\\n7. Blue Account at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_001\\n   Score: 13.3768\\n   Content: ## Key details\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: $20.00\\n- Waiver requirement: maintain a minimum daily balance of $625\\n- Out-of-network ATM withdrawal: 1% of withdrawal amount (max $3.00)\\n- Interest earned on balances: 0.01%\\n- Mobile check deposit daily limit: $2,500\\n- Early direct deposit: 1 day(s) before payday\\n- No overdraft fees\\n\\n### Quick tips\\n- Set up alerts to keep your daily balance at or above $625 if you want the monthly fee waived.\\n- Use in-network ATMs to avoid the 1% out-of-network fee.\\n- Plan larger check deposits ahead of time if they exceed the $2,500 daily mobile deposit limit.\\n- With early direct deposit, your paycheck can arrive 1 day(s) early.\\n\\n8. Troubleshooting: Beige Fee and Balance Issues\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_beige_010\\n   Score: 13.1962\\n   Content: ## Quick Reference: Fees and Balance Thresholds\\n\\n| Item | Amount | When it matters |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $200.00 | Charged if you do not meet the waiver balance threshold within the billing period |\\n| Fee waiver balance threshold | $500,000 | Balance required to waive the monthly maintenance fee |\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $250,000 | Balance required to maintain the enterprise-level treasury account |\\n| Domestic out-of-network ATM fee | $0.00 | Per transaction at non-Rho ATMs within the U.S. |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 1% of withdrawal amount, minimum $2.00 | Per withdrawal at international ATMs |\\n\\nNote: The ATM section below addresses only fees charged by us.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Troubleshooting an Unexpected Monthly Maintenance Fee\\n\\nIf you were charged $200.00 and expected a waiver:\\n\\n1. Verify the waiver threshold was met\\n   - Confirm your Beige account balance met or exceeded $500,000 during the relevant billing period.\\n   - Do not confuse the waiver threshold with the minimum balance requirement; meeting $250,000 alone does not waive the fee.\\n\\n2. Review fund movements that may have lowered your balance\\n   - Check liquidity rules, balance aggregation flows, and auto-fund movements that could have moved funds out of the account near period end.\\n   - Review API/ERP-triggered transfers and scheduled sweeps for the period.\\n   - Confirm dual authorization did not leave an inbound transfer pending at the time the balance was measured.\\n\\n3. Reconcile timing\\n   - Compare timestamps of transfers with the date/time your period closed.\\n   - If transfers posted after the relevant cut-off, they would not count toward the waiver balance for that period.\\n\\n4. Prevent recurrence\\n   - Maintain a buffer above $500,000 to account for intraday or end-of-day movements.\\n   - Adjust auto-movement rules or transfer windows so your Beige account remains above $500,000 when the balance is measured.\\n   - Ensure dual approvers are available to approve time-sensitive transfers.\\n\\n5. Request a review if needed\\n   - If your records show the Beige account balance met $500,000 for the period and the fee still posted, provide the statement period, balance history, and transfer details for investigation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Troubleshooting Minimum Balance Issues\\n\\nIf your balance dipped below $250,000 unexpectedly:\\n\\n- Review automated transfers and aggregation\\n  - Check whether liquidity tools or auto-fund rules moved funds out of the Beige account temporarily.\\n  - Confirm any planned replenishment transfers were executed and fully posted.\\n\\n- Check approval status\\n  - Verify whether dual authorization delayed a transfer intended to keep the account above $250,000.\\n\\n- Stabilize operationally\\n  - Increase the Beige account’s target buffer so routine sweeps and settlement variances do not push the balance below $250,000.\\n  - Where applicable, shift transfer timing to earlier in the day to reduce posting-risk.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Troubleshooting ATM Fee Discrepancies\\n\\nUse this section to reconcile Rho-Bank’s ATM fees shown on your statement.\\n\\n1. Domestic out-of-network ATM transactions\\n   - Our fee per transaction: $0.00.\\n   - If you see any domestic out-of-network ATM fee from us other than $0.00, capture the transaction details and request a review.\\n\\n2. Foreign (international) ATM withdrawals\\n   - Our fee is 1% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.00 per withdrawal.\\n   - Examples:\\n     - $400 withdrawal: 1% of $400 = $4.00; fee should be $4.00.\\n     - $150 withdrawal: 1% of $150 = $1.50, which is below the $2.00 minimum; fee should be $2.00.\\n   - If the fee you see seems off, confirm the USD amount used for the posted withdrawal and recalculate using 1% with the $2.00 floor.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Common Root Causes and Fixes\\n\\n- Balance just under waiver threshold\\n  - Cause: Routine sweeps or late postings left the Beige account slightly below $500,000.\\n  - Fix: Raise the account’s target buffer and adjust sweep timing so the balance is above $500,000 at measurement.\\n\\n- Aggregation or auto-fund rules moved funds out unexpectedly\\n  - Cause: Liquidity rules executed earlier than expected or before the period closed.\\n  - Fix: Update rule timing or conditions; confirm posting order and dependencies.\\n\\n- Pending transfers due to dual authorization\\n  - Cause: A required co-approval wasn’t completed in time.\\n  - Fix: Set up backup approvers and alerts to ensure time-sensitive movements complete before balance measurement.\\n\\n- ATM fee mismatch\\n  - Cause: Misinterpreting which withdrawals are domestic vs. foreign, or not applying the minimum for foreign withdrawals.\\n  - Fix: Reconcile using $0.00 for domestic and 1% with the $2.00 floor for foreign transactions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## What to Provide When Contacting Support\\n\\nPrepare the following to expedite resolution:\\n- Statement period and date the fee posted\\n- Balance history for the period relative to $500,000 and $250,000\\n- Transfer logs (including API/ERP-initiated movements), rule configurations, and approval timestamps\\n- For ATM issues: transaction date, location (domestic or foreign), withdrawal amount in USD, and the fee posted relative to 1% and $2.00\\n\\n9. Implementing Beige: Enterprise Treasury Onboarding\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_beige_001\\n   Score: 12.2220\\n   Content: ## Onboarding timeline and responsibilities\\n- Confirm executive sponsorship and authorized signers before initiating onboarding.\\n- Prepare onboarding documentation, treasury policy, and internal approval matrix.\\n- Identify primary funding sources for initial deposits and recurring cash flows.\\n\\n## Funding and balance setup\\n- Maintain at least $250,000 to keep your enterprise-level treasury account in good standing.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $200.00. This fee is waived when your average balance meets or exceeds $500,000.\\n- If you anticipate balance variability during early implementation, align funding schedules to preserve eligibility for the fee waiver threshold.\\n\\n## Dedicated support structure\\n- You are assigned 2 dedicated account managers who coordinate onboarding milestones, entitlements, and operational readiness.\\n- Establish a recurring operating cadence with your account team for progress tracking and rapid issue resolution.\\n\\n## Overdraft settings during go-live\\n- Overdrafts incur a fee of $0.00.\\n- If you plan to stagger incoming funds across multiple institutions, configure conservative payment windows and internal approvals to avoid negative balances.\\n\\n## Operational readiness checklist\\n- Set signer roles and entitlements consistent with your treasury policy.\\n- Add internal approval rules for payments and administrative changes in line with your governance model.\\n- Validate statement delivery preferences, reporting formats, and reconciliation identifiers prior to first close.\\n- Confirm that funding sources are scheduled to achieve at least $250,000 and, if desired, the waiver threshold of $500,000.\\n\\n## Reference values for onboarding\\n| Item | Value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $200.00 |\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $250,000 |\\n| Fee waiver balance threshold | $500,000 |\\n| Dedicated account managers | 2 |\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n\\n\\n10. Light Blue Account features and fees\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_light_blue_account_004\\n   Score: 12.0740\\n   Content: ## Fees and features\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $0.00 |\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n| Overdraft protection transfer fee | $0.00 |\\n| Free out-of-network ATM withdrawals per month | 2 |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee (after free) | $2.50 |\\n| Paper statement fee (monthly) | $0.00 |\\n| Returned deposit fee | $0.00 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Stop payment fee (per request) | $30 |\\n| APY on balances | 0% |\\n| Daily ATM withdrawal limit | $400 |\\n\\n## Out-of-network ATM withdrawals\\n- You receive 2 free out-of-network ATM withdrawals each month.\\n- After using your free allowance, each additional withdrawal costs $2.50.\\n- ATM owners may charge their own surcharge, separate from our fee.\\n\\n## Daily ATM withdrawal limit\\n- Your daily ATM withdrawal limit is $400. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n## Helpful notes\\n- Returned checks may be subject to the $0.00 even if the return reason is outside your control.\\n- If you prefer paper statements, factor in the $0.00 each cycle.\\n- If you link an account for overdraft protection, each transfer to cover a shortfall is $0.00.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=2ms, reranking=0ms, total=2ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_KiDSojBwpJVNjig54Fnad5Zj\",\"output\":\"1. Green Fee-Free Account features\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_fee-free_account_005\\n   Score: 17.9215\\n   Content: ## Key Features and Fees\\n\\n| Item | Details |\\n|---|---|\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum balance to waive monthly fee | $150 (minimum daily balance) |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $0.00 |\\n| Stop payment fee (per request) | $25 |\\n| Daily ATM withdrawal limit | $500 |\\n| APY boost with linked Bronze Savings | 0.4% |\\n| APY boost with linked Gold Plus Savings | 0.35% |\\n\\n### No Overdraft Charges\\n- You are not charged an overdraft fee. The overdraft fee for this account is $0.00.\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee and Waiver\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $22.50.\\n- It is waived when you maintain a minimum daily balance of $150 during the statement cycle.\\n- If the waiver requirement is met, the fee for that cycle is not charged; otherwise, the $22.50 fee is assessed at cycle end.\\n\\n### ATM Withdrawals\\n- Rho does not charge a fee for using out-of-network ATMs: $0.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals are also fee-free: $0.00 per withdrawal. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n- Your daily ATM withdrawal limit is $500. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n### Statements\\n- Paper statements are provided without a monthly fee: $0.00.\\n\\n### Stop Payments\\n- Stop payment requests incur a fee of $25 per item.\\n\\n### Savings APY Boosts (when linked)\\n- Link a Bronze Savings Account to receive a 0.4% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n- Link a Gold Plus Savings Account to receive a 0.35% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n\\n2. True Blue Account: Fee Waivers and Balance Requirements\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_002\\n   Score: 17.2421\\n   Content: ## Waiving your monthly maintenance fee\\n- You will be charged $75.00 each month unless you meet the waiver threshold.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is waived when your balance is at least $50,000 during the statement period.\\n\\n## Minimum balance requirement vs. fee waiver threshold\\n- Minimum balance requirement: $25,000 to maintain the account and access premium features.\\n- Fee waiver threshold: $50,000 to waive the $75.00 monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Falling below $25,000 may limit access to premium features until your balance is restored.\\n\\n## Overdrafts and shortfalls\\n- If your balance goes negative, a per-occurrence overdraft fee of $25.00 may apply.\\n\\n## How to avoid fees\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $50,000 to waive the monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Set internal processes to monitor balances against both $25,000 and $50,000.\\n- If a shortfall is anticipated, transfer funds promptly to avoid the $25.00 and preserve eligibility for the fee waiver.\\n\\n## True Blue Referral Program\\n\\nRefer other high-volume businesses to True Blue and earn significant rewards:\\n\\n| Benefit | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Referrer bonus | $350 per referral |\\n| New member bonus | $250 |\\n| Maximum referrals per year | 15 |\\n| Qualifying deposit | $50,000 |\\n| Deposit window | 120 days |\\n| Account age requirement | 90 days |\\n\\n### Referral requirements\\n- The referred business must deposit $50,000 within 120 days of opening their True Blue account.\\n- Eligibility is based on how long you've been a Rho-Bank checking customer. The account age threshold is 90 days, calculated from when you opened your oldest checking account.\\n- Referral bonuses are paid after qualification is confirmed and are subject to the annual limit of 15.\\n\\n3. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_013\\n   Score: 16.8729\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Sky Blue account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Lime Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Sky Blue nor Lime Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our startup and premium business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n4. Troubleshooting: Unexpected Charges on Cobalt Blue\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_009\\n   Score: 15.5553\\n   Content: ## Identify the charge\\n- Review the exact transaction description on your statement or in your transaction history (e.g., “Monthly Maintenance Fee,” “Wire Transfer – Domestic,” “ATM Fee,” “International ATM Withdrawal Fee,” “Excess Transaction Fee”).\\n- Note the posting date, amount, and any memo or terminal/location details.\\n- Compare the posting date to your recent account activity (wires sent, ATM withdrawals, transaction volume, month-end).\\n\\n## Common Cobalt Blue charges that may appear\\n| Line item on statement | Why it appears | How to confirm | Amount |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly Maintenance Fee | Your account did not meet the balance waiver requirement during the statement period. | Check the Fee Summary on your statement and verify whether your balance met $2,500 for the period. | $20.00 |\\n| Excess Transaction Fee | You exceeded your monthly free transaction limit. | Count your posted transactions for the statement period and compare to your free allowance; the fee line often notes the number of excess items. | $0.25 per excess transaction |\\n| Wire Transfer Fee – Domestic | You initiated a domestic wire transfer. | Confirm a wire was submitted on or near the posting date in your transfer history. | $20.00 |\\n| ATM Fee – Out of Network | You used a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | Match the fee date to an ATM withdrawal at a non‑Rho terminal. Note: the ATM owner may also assess a separate surcharge. | $2.00 per ATM transaction |\\n| International ATM Withdrawal Fee | You withdrew cash at a foreign (international) ATM. | Match the fee date/location to an overseas ATM withdrawal. | 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, minimum $4.00 |\\n\\nNote: Cobalt Blue does not assess overdraft fees. If you see a charge that appears to be an overdraft fee, review the line’s exact description—it may correspond to one of the fees above. If still unclear, request a review.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting by charge type\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee posted unexpectedly\\n- Verify whether your account met the waiver balance requirement of $2,500 during the statement period.\\n- Check if the fee posted at or just after the statement cycle date.\\n- Compare your balance history for the full period; large debits near period‑end can affect waiver eligibility.\\n- If you believe you qualified for the waiver, request a fee review and include your statement period dates and balance evidence.\\n\\n### Excess Transaction Fee you didn’t anticipate\\n- Add up your posted transactions for the statement period and compare to your plan’s free monthly transaction limit.\\n- Open the fee detail to see how many items were assessed at $0.25 each.\\n- If the count appears off, provide a list of the transactions you believe were miscounted when requesting a review.\\n\\n### Wire Transfer Fee – Domestic you didn’t expect\\n- Confirm whether a domestic wire was sent on the fee date (or one business day prior).\\n- Distinguish wires from other transfers by the transaction description (“Wire,” routing via Fedwire, etc.).\\n- If you did not authorize a wire, report immediately for investigation. Otherwise, the standard fee is $20.00.\\n\\n### ATM fees: domestic vs. international\\n- Out‑of‑network (domestic) ATM usage: Expect $2.00 per ATM transaction. This is separate from any surcharge by the ATM owner, which can appear as a separate line item.\\n- Foreign (international) ATM withdrawals: The fee is 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00. Example: for a withdrawal, multiply the amount by 2.5%; if that result is less than $4.00, the minimum applies.\\n\\n## Quick checklist before requesting a review\\n- Match the fee’s posting date to a specific action (wire, ATM withdrawal, month‑end, spike in transaction volume).\\n- Capture screenshots of:\\n  - The fee line item (showing date, amount, and description)\\n  - Any related transaction (wire confirmation, ATM withdrawal)\\n  - The relevant statement page (Fee Summary and balance history for the period)\\n- Briefly explain why the fee appears incorrect (e.g., you met $2,500 during the period, transaction count appears miscalculated, withdrawal was domestic vs. international, etc.).\\n\\n## Requesting a review or dispute\\n- Contact us as soon as you notice the charge.\\n- Include: account name, last 4 digits, statement period, fee date/amount/description, and your supporting screenshots or documents.\\n- We will investigate and correct any misapplied fees. If additional information is needed (e.g., to verify ATM location or wire authorization), we will follow up.\\n\\n5. Why am I being charged a fee on my True Blue Account?\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_010\\n   Score: 14.6847\\n   Content: ## Common reasons you’re seeing a fee\\n\\nBelow are the most common fee types that can appear on a True Blue account and why they’re charged.\\n\\n| Fee type | When you’ll see it | Amount posted |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly Maintenance Fee | Your qualifying balance did not meet the waiver threshold for the applicable evaluation period | $75.00 (waived when balance requirement of $50,000 is met) |\\n| Domestic Wire Transfer Fee | You sent a domestic wire from your account | $5.00 per outbound domestic wire |\\n| Out-of-Network ATM Fee | You completed a transaction at a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM Withdrawal Fee | You withdrew cash at an international (non‑U.S.) ATM | 2% of the withdrawal amount; minimum $3.00 |\\n\\n### Example for foreign ATM fee\\n- If you withdraw $200 at a foreign ATM, the fee is 2% of $200 ($4). Because $4 exceeds the minimum $3.00, $4 would post.\\n\\n## How to confirm which fee was charged\\n\\n1. Check your latest statement or transaction history for the fee line item and posted amount.  \\n2. Match the posted amount to the fees above:\\n   - $75.00 typically indicates the Monthly Maintenance Fee.\\n   - $5.00 typically indicates a Domestic Wire Transfer Fee.\\n   - $1.00 typically indicates an Out-of-Network ATM Fee.\\n   - A calculated amount equal to 2% of your ATM withdrawal (or $3.00, whichever is higher) indicates a Foreign ATM Withdrawal Fee.\\n3. For the Monthly Maintenance Fee, compare your balance during the billing period to the waiver threshold of $50,000.\\n\\n## How to reduce or avoid future fees\\n\\n- Maintain at least $50,000 to have the $75.00 waived.  \\n- Use Rho in‑network ATMs to avoid the $1.00.  \\n- When abroad, be aware that each cash withdrawal will incur 2% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $3.00.  \\n- Send domestic wires only when necessary to limit paying $5.00 per wire.\\n\\n## Need help?\\n\\nIf you believe a fee was posted in error, gather the transaction date, amount, and any related activity (e.g., wire reference or ATM withdrawal details) and contact support for a review.\\n\\n6. Dark Green Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_dark_green_account_002\\n   Score: 13.8617\\n   Content: ## Eligibility requirements\\n- The primary account holder must be at least 17.\\n- You can maintain the account through 26.\\n\\n## Fee schedule\\nThe following fees apply to this account.\\n\\n| Fee | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Monthly maintenance | $10.00 |\\n| Overdraft protection transfer | 0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal | 2.5% of amount (max $6.00) |\\n| Returned deposit | $10.00 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire | $7.50 |\\n\\n## Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- When you withdraw cash from an ATM abroad, a fee of 2.5% of the withdrawal amount is charged.\\n- The fee is capped at a maximum of $6.00 per transaction, protecting you from excessive fees on larger withdrawals.\\n- Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n## Transaction limits\\n- Debit card daily purchase limit: $1,500\\n- Daily ATM withdrawal limit: $300\\n\\n## Overdraft protection transfers\\n- When enabled and available, transfers from a linked funding source to cover an overdraft incur a transfer fee of 0.\\n\\n7. Blue Account features and fees\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_003\\n   Score: 13.8335\\n   Content: ## Key Features\\n- No overdraft fees on the account\\n- Waivable monthly maintenance fee: $20.00; waived when your minimum daily balance is at least $625\\n\\n## Optional Add-On\\n### Overdraft Protection Transfers\\n- If you opt in to overdraft protection, each transfer from a linked account to cover a negative balance incurs a $12.50 fee\\n- No overdraft fees are charged by the account itself\\n\\n## Fees\\n| Item | Amount | When it applies |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $20.00 | Charged monthly; waived with a minimum daily balance of $625 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $2.50 | Per month if you choose mailed paper statements |\\n| Returned deposit | $15.00 | Per deposited item returned unpaid |\\n| Incoming domestic wire transfer | $12.50 | Per incoming domestic wire |\\n| Stop payment on a check | $30 | Per stop payment request |\\n\\n## Linked Savings APY Boosts\\n- When linked to a Silver Plus Savings Account: +0.35% APY boost\\n- When linked to a Platinum Savings Account: +0.8% APY boost\\n\\n## Ways to Reduce or Avoid Fees\\n- Maintain a minimum daily balance of $625 to waive the $20.00 monthly maintenance fee\\n- Choose e-statements to avoid the $2.50 paper statement fee\\n- Use in-network ATMs to avoid out-of-network ATM fees\\n- Only enable overdraft protection if you need it, as each transfer incurs a $12.50 fee\\n\\n8. Blue Account at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_001\\n   Score: 13.3768\\n   Content: ## Key details\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: $20.00\\n- Waiver requirement: maintain a minimum daily balance of $625\\n- Out-of-network ATM withdrawal: 1% of withdrawal amount (max $3.00)\\n- Interest earned on balances: 0.01%\\n- Mobile check deposit daily limit: $2,500\\n- Early direct deposit: 1 day(s) before payday\\n- No overdraft fees\\n\\n### Quick tips\\n- Set up alerts to keep your daily balance at or above $625 if you want the monthly fee waived.\\n- Use in-network ATMs to avoid the 1% out-of-network fee.\\n- Plan larger check deposits ahead of time if they exceed the $2,500 daily mobile deposit limit.\\n- With early direct deposit, your paycheck can arrive 1 day(s) early.\\n\\n9. Troubleshooting: Beige Fee and Balance Issues\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_beige_010\\n   Score: 13.1962\\n   Content: ## Quick Reference: Fees and Balance Thresholds\\n\\n| Item | Amount | When it matters |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $200.00 | Charged if you do not meet the waiver balance threshold within the billing period |\\n| Fee waiver balance threshold | $500,000 | Balance required to waive the monthly maintenance fee |\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $250,000 | Balance required to maintain the enterprise-level treasury account |\\n| Domestic out-of-network ATM fee | $0.00 | Per transaction at non-Rho ATMs within the U.S. |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 1% of withdrawal amount, minimum $2.00 | Per withdrawal at international ATMs |\\n\\nNote: The ATM section below addresses only fees charged by us.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Troubleshooting an Unexpected Monthly Maintenance Fee\\n\\nIf you were charged $200.00 and expected a waiver:\\n\\n1. Verify the waiver threshold was met\\n   - Confirm your Beige account balance met or exceeded $500,000 during the relevant billing period.\\n   - Do not confuse the waiver threshold with the minimum balance requirement; meeting $250,000 alone does not waive the fee.\\n\\n2. Review fund movements that may have lowered your balance\\n   - Check liquidity rules, balance aggregation flows, and auto-fund movements that could have moved funds out of the account near period end.\\n   - Review API/ERP-triggered transfers and scheduled sweeps for the period.\\n   - Confirm dual authorization did not leave an inbound transfer pending at the time the balance was measured.\\n\\n3. Reconcile timing\\n   - Compare timestamps of transfers with the date/time your period closed.\\n   - If transfers posted after the relevant cut-off, they would not count toward the waiver balance for that period.\\n\\n4. Prevent recurrence\\n   - Maintain a buffer above $500,000 to account for intraday or end-of-day movements.\\n   - Adjust auto-movement rules or transfer windows so your Beige account remains above $500,000 when the balance is measured.\\n   - Ensure dual approvers are available to approve time-sensitive transfers.\\n\\n5. Request a review if needed\\n   - If your records show the Beige account balance met $500,000 for the period and the fee still posted, provide the statement period, balance history, and transfer details for investigation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Troubleshooting Minimum Balance Issues\\n\\nIf your balance dipped below $250,000 unexpectedly:\\n\\n- Review automated transfers and aggregation\\n  - Check whether liquidity tools or auto-fund rules moved funds out of the Beige account temporarily.\\n  - Confirm any planned replenishment transfers were executed and fully posted.\\n\\n- Check approval status\\n  - Verify whether dual authorization delayed a transfer intended to keep the account above $250,000.\\n\\n- Stabilize operationally\\n  - Increase the Beige account’s target buffer so routine sweeps and settlement variances do not push the balance below $250,000.\\n  - Where applicable, shift transfer timing to earlier in the day to reduce posting-risk.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Troubleshooting ATM Fee Discrepancies\\n\\nUse this section to reconcile Rho-Bank’s ATM fees shown on your statement.\\n\\n1. Domestic out-of-network ATM transactions\\n   - Our fee per transaction: $0.00.\\n   - If you see any domestic out-of-network ATM fee from us other than $0.00, capture the transaction details and request a review.\\n\\n2. Foreign (international) ATM withdrawals\\n   - Our fee is 1% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.00 per withdrawal.\\n   - Examples:\\n     - $400 withdrawal: 1% of $400 = $4.00; fee should be $4.00.\\n     - $150 withdrawal: 1% of $150 = $1.50, which is below the $2.00 minimum; fee should be $2.00.\\n   - If the fee you see seems off, confirm the USD amount used for the posted withdrawal and recalculate using 1% with the $2.00 floor.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Common Root Causes and Fixes\\n\\n- Balance just under waiver threshold\\n  - Cause: Routine sweeps or late postings left the Beige account slightly below $500,000.\\n  - Fix: Raise the account’s target buffer and adjust sweep timing so the balance is above $500,000 at measurement.\\n\\n- Aggregation or auto-fund rules moved funds out unexpectedly\\n  - Cause: Liquidity rules executed earlier than expected or before the period closed.\\n  - Fix: Update rule timing or conditions; confirm posting order and dependencies.\\n\\n- Pending transfers due to dual authorization\\n  - Cause: A required co-approval wasn’t completed in time.\\n  - Fix: Set up backup approvers and alerts to ensure time-sensitive movements complete before balance measurement.\\n\\n- ATM fee mismatch\\n  - Cause: Misinterpreting which withdrawals are domestic vs. foreign, or not applying the minimum for foreign withdrawals.\\n  - Fix: Reconcile using $0.00 for domestic and 1% with the $2.00 floor for foreign transactions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## What to Provide When Contacting Support\\n\\nPrepare the following to expedite resolution:\\n- Statement period and date the fee posted\\n- Balance history for the period relative to $500,000 and $250,000\\n- Transfer logs (including API/ERP-initiated movements), rule configurations, and approval timestamps\\n- For ATM issues: transaction date, location (domestic or foreign), withdrawal amount in USD, and the fee posted relative to 1% and $2.00\\n\\n10. Implementing Beige: Enterprise Treasury Onboarding\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_beige_001\\n   Score: 12.2220\\n   Content: ## Onboarding timeline and responsibilities\\n- Confirm executive sponsorship and authorized signers before initiating onboarding.\\n- Prepare onboarding documentation, treasury policy, and internal approval matrix.\\n- Identify primary funding sources for initial deposits and recurring cash flows.\\n\\n## Funding and balance setup\\n- Maintain at least $250,000 to keep your enterprise-level treasury account in good standing.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $200.00. This fee is waived when your average balance meets or exceeds $500,000.\\n- If you anticipate balance variability during early implementation, align funding schedules to preserve eligibility for the fee waiver threshold.\\n\\n## Dedicated support structure\\n- You are assigned 2 dedicated account managers who coordinate onboarding milestones, entitlements, and operational readiness.\\n- Establish a recurring operating cadence with your account team for progress tracking and rapid issue resolution.\\n\\n## Overdraft settings during go-live\\n- Overdrafts incur a fee of $0.00.\\n- If you plan to stagger incoming funds across multiple institutions, configure conservative payment windows and internal approvals to avoid negative balances.\\n\\n## Operational readiness checklist\\n- Set signer roles and entitlements consistent with your treasury policy.\\n- Add internal approval rules for payments and administrative changes in line with your governance model.\\n- Validate statement delivery preferences, reporting formats, and reconciliation identifiers prior to first close.\\n- Confirm that funding sources are scheduled to achieve at least $250,000 and, if desired, the waiver threshold of $500,000.\\n\\n## Reference values for onboarding\\n| Item | Value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $200.00 |\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $250,000 |\\n| Fee waiver balance threshold | $500,000 |\\n| Dedicated account managers | 2 |\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_DRJ1KJo2seeqeYQSqR1EPYUc\",\"output\":\"1. Green Fee-Free Account features\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_fee-free_account_005\\n   Score: 17.9215\\n   Content: ## Key Features and Fees\\n\\n| Item | Details |\\n|---|---|\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum balance to waive monthly fee | $150 (minimum daily balance) |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | $0.00 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $0.00 |\\n| Stop payment fee (per request) | $25 |\\n| Daily ATM withdrawal limit | $500 |\\n| APY boost with linked Bronze Savings | 0.4% |\\n| APY boost with linked Gold Plus Savings | 0.35% |\\n\\n### No Overdraft Charges\\n- You are not charged an overdraft fee. The overdraft fee for this account is $0.00.\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee and Waiver\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $22.50.\\n- It is waived when you maintain a minimum daily balance of $150 during the statement cycle.\\n- If the waiver requirement is met, the fee for that cycle is not charged; otherwise, the $22.50 fee is assessed at cycle end.\\n\\n### ATM Withdrawals\\n- Rho does not charge a fee for using out-of-network ATMs: $0.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawals are also fee-free: $0.00 per withdrawal. Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n- Your daily ATM withdrawal limit is $500. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n### Statements\\n- Paper statements are provided without a monthly fee: $0.00.\\n\\n### Stop Payments\\n- Stop payment requests incur a fee of $25 per item.\\n\\n### Savings APY Boosts (when linked)\\n- Link a Bronze Savings Account to receive a 0.4% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n- Link a Gold Plus Savings Account to receive a 0.35% APY boost on that savings balance.\\n\\n2. Why am I being charged a fee on my Lime Green Account?\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_008\\n   Score: 16.9008\\n   Content: ## Common reasons you may see a fee\\n\\nYou may see one or more of the following fees on your Lime Green Account:\\n\\n- Monthly maintenance fee if your balance does not meet the waiver threshold\\n- Fees for sending domestic or international wire transfers\\n- Fees for using non‑Rho ATMs, including percentage‑based fees for foreign ATM withdrawals\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Fee type | When it’s charged | Amount |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | Your balance does not meet the waiver threshold | $25.00 |\\n| Domestic wire transfer | You send a domestic wire | $10.00 |\\n| International wire transfer | You send an international wire to a foreign bank | $25.00 |\\n| Non‑Rho ATM (U.S.) | You withdraw cash at a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | $1.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal | You withdraw cash at an international ATM | 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, minimum $2.50 |\\n\\n## Monthly maintenance fee\\n\\n- You are charged $25.00 when your account balance does not meet $15,000.\\n- To avoid this fee, maintain a balance at or above $15,000.\\n\\n## Wire transfer fees\\n\\n- Domestic wires: Each outgoing domestic wire you send incurs a fee of $10.00.\\n- International wires: Each outgoing international wire to a foreign bank incurs a fee of $25.00.\\n\\n## ATM‑related fees\\n\\n- Non‑Rho ATMs in the U.S.: You are charged $1.00 per withdrawal when using a non‑Rho ATM.\\n- Foreign (international) ATMs: You are charged 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum fee of $2.50.\\n  - How to estimate: Multiply your withdrawal amount by 1.5% and compare the result to $2.50. The higher number is the fee.\\n\\n## How to confirm which fee was charged\\n\\n1. Review your transaction history for a separate fee line item (for example, a description referencing maintenance, wire, or ATM).\\n2. Match the amount to one of the following:\\n   - $25.00\\n   - $10.00\\n   - $25.00\\n   - $1.00\\n   - For foreign ATM withdrawals, the greater of:\\n     - 1.5% of your withdrawal amount, or\\n     - $2.50\\n\\n## Ways to avoid or reduce fees\\n\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $15,000 to waive $25.00.\\n- Use Rho‑network ATMs to avoid the $1.00.\\n- Plan international cash needs to minimize the number of foreign ATM withdrawals subject to 1.5% (minimum $2.50).\\n\\n## If you believe a fee is incorrect\\n\\n- Gather details (date, amount, and description of the fee; related transaction, if any).\\n- Contact support with these details so we can review and correct any errors promptly.\\n\\n3. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - October 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_014\\n   Score: 15.6829\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 10/12/2025 TO 11/12/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Lime Green account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Hunter Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Lime Green nor Hunter Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our premium and eco-conscious business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n4. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_013\\n   Score: 14.7858\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Sky Blue account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Lime Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Sky Blue nor Lime Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our startup and premium business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n5. Green Account (checking) at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_account_(checking)_001\\n   Score: 14.0186\\n   Content: ## Highlights\\n- No overdraft fees and no overdraft coverage; transactions that exceed your available balance are declined\\n- Earn 0.11% APY on your checking balance\\n- Get direct deposits up to 1 day early\\n- Mobile check deposits up to $3,000 per day\\n- Boost a linked savings account's APY: Gold +0.75% or Silver +0.25%\\n\\n## Fees and limits\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $22.50 |\\n| Minimum daily balance to waive fee | $1,350 |\\n| Paper statement fee (monthly) | $2.50 |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | $3.00 |\\n| Returned deposit fee | $17.50 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire (receive) | $15.00 |\\n| APY on balance | 0.11% |\\n| Daily mobile check deposit limit | $3,000 |\\n| Early direct deposit | Up to 1 day early |\\n\\n## Referral program\\nRefer friends and family to open a Green Account and earn rewards:\\n- You earn: $20 per successful referral\\n- They receive: $30 welcome bonus\\n- Maximum referrals per year: 5\\n- Qualifying deposit required: $500 within 60 days\\n- Account tenure requirement: 30 days since becoming a Rho-Bank checking customer.\\n\\n## Important details\\n- To avoid the monthly maintenance fee, maintain a minimum daily balance of $1,350 each statement cycle\\n- If you opt for paper statements, a $2.50 monthly fee applies\\n- Using a non-network ATM incurs a $3.00 fee; the ATM owner may charge additional fees\\n- Deposited checks returned unpaid result in a $17.50 fee\\n- Receiving a domestic wire transfer costs $15.00\\n- Early direct deposit availability depends on when your payer submits the deposit; funds can post up to 1 day early\\n- Savings APY boosts apply when you link an eligible Gold or Silver Savings Account: +0.75% or +0.25% respectively\\n\\n6. Dark Green Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_dark_green_account_002\\n   Score: 13.8617\\n   Content: ## Eligibility requirements\\n- The primary account holder must be at least 17.\\n- You can maintain the account through 26.\\n\\n## Fee schedule\\nThe following fees apply to this account.\\n\\n| Fee | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Monthly maintenance | $10.00 |\\n| Overdraft protection transfer | 0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal | 2.5% of amount (max $6.00) |\\n| Returned deposit | $10.00 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire | $7.50 |\\n\\n## Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- When you withdraw cash from an ATM abroad, a fee of 2.5% of the withdrawal amount is charged.\\n- The fee is capped at a maximum of $6.00 per transaction, protecting you from excessive fees on larger withdrawals.\\n- Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n## Transaction limits\\n- Debit card daily purchase limit: $1,500\\n- Daily ATM withdrawal limit: $300\\n\\n## Overdraft protection transfers\\n- When enabled and available, transfers from a linked funding source to cover an overdraft incur a transfer fee of 0.\\n\\n7. Blue Account features and fees\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_003\\n   Score: 13.8335\\n   Content: ## Key Features\\n- No overdraft fees on the account\\n- Waivable monthly maintenance fee: $20.00; waived when your minimum daily balance is at least $625\\n\\n## Optional Add-On\\n### Overdraft Protection Transfers\\n- If you opt in to overdraft protection, each transfer from a linked account to cover a negative balance incurs a $12.50 fee\\n- No overdraft fees are charged by the account itself\\n\\n## Fees\\n| Item | Amount | When it applies |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $20.00 | Charged monthly; waived with a minimum daily balance of $625 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $2.50 | Per month if you choose mailed paper statements |\\n| Returned deposit | $15.00 | Per deposited item returned unpaid |\\n| Incoming domestic wire transfer | $12.50 | Per incoming domestic wire |\\n| Stop payment on a check | $30 | Per stop payment request |\\n\\n## Linked Savings APY Boosts\\n- When linked to a Silver Plus Savings Account: +0.35% APY boost\\n- When linked to a Platinum Savings Account: +0.8% APY boost\\n\\n## Ways to Reduce or Avoid Fees\\n- Maintain a minimum daily balance of $625 to waive the $20.00 monthly maintenance fee\\n- Choose e-statements to avoid the $2.50 paper statement fee\\n- Use in-network ATMs to avoid out-of-network ATM fees\\n- Only enable overdraft protection if you need it, as each transfer incurs a $12.50 fee\\n\\n8. Blue Account at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_001\\n   Score: 13.3768\\n   Content: ## Key details\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: $20.00\\n- Waiver requirement: maintain a minimum daily balance of $625\\n- Out-of-network ATM withdrawal: 1% of withdrawal amount (max $3.00)\\n- Interest earned on balances: 0.01%\\n- Mobile check deposit daily limit: $2,500\\n- Early direct deposit: 1 day(s) before payday\\n- No overdraft fees\\n\\n### Quick tips\\n- Set up alerts to keep your daily balance at or above $625 if you want the monthly fee waived.\\n- Use in-network ATMs to avoid the 1% out-of-network fee.\\n- Plan larger check deposits ahead of time if they exceed the $2,500 daily mobile deposit limit.\\n- With early direct deposit, your paycheck can arrive 1 day(s) early.\\n\\n9. Troubleshooting: Beige Fee and Balance Issues\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_beige_010\\n   Score: 13.1962\\n   Content: ## Quick Reference: Fees and Balance Thresholds\\n\\n| Item | Amount | When it matters |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $200.00 | Charged if you do not meet the waiver balance threshold within the billing period |\\n| Fee waiver balance threshold | $500,000 | Balance required to waive the monthly maintenance fee |\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $250,000 | Balance required to maintain the enterprise-level treasury account |\\n| Domestic out-of-network ATM fee | $0.00 | Per transaction at non-Rho ATMs within the U.S. |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal fee | 1% of withdrawal amount, minimum $2.00 | Per withdrawal at international ATMs |\\n\\nNote: The ATM section below addresses only fees charged by us.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Troubleshooting an Unexpected Monthly Maintenance Fee\\n\\nIf you were charged $200.00 and expected a waiver:\\n\\n1. Verify the waiver threshold was met\\n   - Confirm your Beige account balance met or exceeded $500,000 during the relevant billing period.\\n   - Do not confuse the waiver threshold with the minimum balance requirement; meeting $250,000 alone does not waive the fee.\\n\\n2. Review fund movements that may have lowered your balance\\n   - Check liquidity rules, balance aggregation flows, and auto-fund movements that could have moved funds out of the account near period end.\\n   - Review API/ERP-triggered transfers and scheduled sweeps for the period.\\n   - Confirm dual authorization did not leave an inbound transfer pending at the time the balance was measured.\\n\\n3. Reconcile timing\\n   - Compare timestamps of transfers with the date/time your period closed.\\n   - If transfers posted after the relevant cut-off, they would not count toward the waiver balance for that period.\\n\\n4. Prevent recurrence\\n   - Maintain a buffer above $500,000 to account for intraday or end-of-day movements.\\n   - Adjust auto-movement rules or transfer windows so your Beige account remains above $500,000 when the balance is measured.\\n   - Ensure dual approvers are available to approve time-sensitive transfers.\\n\\n5. Request a review if needed\\n   - If your records show the Beige account balance met $500,000 for the period and the fee still posted, provide the statement period, balance history, and transfer details for investigation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Troubleshooting Minimum Balance Issues\\n\\nIf your balance dipped below $250,000 unexpectedly:\\n\\n- Review automated transfers and aggregation\\n  - Check whether liquidity tools or auto-fund rules moved funds out of the Beige account temporarily.\\n  - Confirm any planned replenishment transfers were executed and fully posted.\\n\\n- Check approval status\\n  - Verify whether dual authorization delayed a transfer intended to keep the account above $250,000.\\n\\n- Stabilize operationally\\n  - Increase the Beige account’s target buffer so routine sweeps and settlement variances do not push the balance below $250,000.\\n  - Where applicable, shift transfer timing to earlier in the day to reduce posting-risk.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Troubleshooting ATM Fee Discrepancies\\n\\nUse this section to reconcile Rho-Bank’s ATM fees shown on your statement.\\n\\n1. Domestic out-of-network ATM transactions\\n   - Our fee per transaction: $0.00.\\n   - If you see any domestic out-of-network ATM fee from us other than $0.00, capture the transaction details and request a review.\\n\\n2. Foreign (international) ATM withdrawals\\n   - Our fee is 1% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.00 per withdrawal.\\n   - Examples:\\n     - $400 withdrawal: 1% of $400 = $4.00; fee should be $4.00.\\n     - $150 withdrawal: 1% of $150 = $1.50, which is below the $2.00 minimum; fee should be $2.00.\\n   - If the fee you see seems off, confirm the USD amount used for the posted withdrawal and recalculate using 1% with the $2.00 floor.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Common Root Causes and Fixes\\n\\n- Balance just under waiver threshold\\n  - Cause: Routine sweeps or late postings left the Beige account slightly below $500,000.\\n  - Fix: Raise the account’s target buffer and adjust sweep timing so the balance is above $500,000 at measurement.\\n\\n- Aggregation or auto-fund rules moved funds out unexpectedly\\n  - Cause: Liquidity rules executed earlier than expected or before the period closed.\\n  - Fix: Update rule timing or conditions; confirm posting order and dependencies.\\n\\n- Pending transfers due to dual authorization\\n  - Cause: A required co-approval wasn’t completed in time.\\n  - Fix: Set up backup approvers and alerts to ensure time-sensitive movements complete before balance measurement.\\n\\n- ATM fee mismatch\\n  - Cause: Misinterpreting which withdrawals are domestic vs. foreign, or not applying the minimum for foreign withdrawals.\\n  - Fix: Reconcile using $0.00 for domestic and 1% with the $2.00 floor for foreign transactions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## What to Provide When Contacting Support\\n\\nPrepare the following to expedite resolution:\\n- Statement period and date the fee posted\\n- Balance history for the period relative to $500,000 and $250,000\\n- Transfer logs (including API/ERP-initiated movements), rule configurations, and approval timestamps\\n- For ATM issues: transaction date, location (domestic or foreign), withdrawal amount in USD, and the fee posted relative to 1% and $2.00\\n\\n10. Troubleshooting: Hunter Green Fees and Charges\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_hunter_green_009\\n   Score: 13.0127\\n   Content: ## Identify and Resolve Unexpected Charges\\n\\nUse the sections below to diagnose why a fee posted, how it’s calculated, and what to do if you believe it’s incorrect.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Monthly Maintenance Fee\\n\\nYou were charged $25.00 if the account did not meet the waiver criteria for the statement period.\\n\\nTroubleshooting steps:\\n- Confirm your statement period and check the “Fees & Charges” section for the $25.00 line.\\n- Verify whether your balance met the waiver threshold of $5,000 for the period.\\n- If you recently moved funds near the end of the cycle, the timing of deposits/withdrawals may have affected the period-end balance used to determine the waiver.\\n- If you believe your balance qualified for the waiver but the fee posted, request a review and include your statement period and balance details for the period.\\n\\nTips to avoid future charges:\\n- Keep your balance at or above $5,000 throughout the statement period.\\n- Set internal alerts to notify you before the cycle ends if your balance is trending below $5,000.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Domestic Wire Transfer Fee\\n\\nAn outgoing domestic wire triggers a fee of $15.00.\\n\\nTroubleshooting steps:\\n- Review your transaction history for outgoing domestic wires on the date the fee posted.\\n- Check whether a team member initiated a wire or if a scheduled/recurring wire executed.\\n- If you see multiple fees for a single wire, compare timestamps and reference numbers; submit both entries for review if they appear duplicative.\\n\\nHow to avoid:\\n- Where possible, consider alternative transfer methods for domestic payments that do not incur the $15.00.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## ATM Fees\\n\\n### Domestic out-of-network ATM usage\\n- Fee: $2.00 per transaction when using non‑Rho ATMs within the U.S.\\n- You may also see a separate surcharge from the ATM operator; this is set by the ATM owner.\\n\\nTroubleshooting steps:\\n- Match the ATM withdrawal date/time and location to the fee posted.\\n- If you were using an in-network ATM but still see $2.00, provide the ATM address and receipt for review.\\n\\n### Foreign (international) ATM withdrawals\\n- Fee: 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00.\\n- In addition, the ATM operator may add its own surcharge.\\n\\nHow the fee is calculated:\\n- The fee is the greater of:\\n  - Withdrawal amount × 2.5%\\n  - $4.00\\n\\nExamples:\\n- Withdrawing 80.00 in local currency equivalent: 80.00 × 2.5% = 2.00; minimum $4.00 applies, so the fee is $4.00.\\n- Withdrawing 400.00 in local currency equivalent: 400.00 × 2.5% = 10.00; since this exceeds $4.00, the fee is 10.00.\\n\\nIf a foreign ATM fee looks incorrect:\\n- Confirm the final settled withdrawal amount (in USD equivalent) used for the percentage calculation.\\n- Check for any separate ATM-operator surcharge on your receipt.\\n- If you see both a foreign ATM fee and a domestic out-of-network fee for the same international withdrawal, share the transaction details for review.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Sustainability Allocations Within Fees\\n\\nSome fees on Hunter Green include a carbon-offset allocation. If you see a note or line item indicating a contribution tied to a fee:\\n- This does not increase the total you pay beyond the published fee amounts (e.g., $25.00, $15.00, $2.00).\\n- If you believe a separate charge was added in error rather than noted as an allocation within an existing fee, share the statement line items for review.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Quick Reference: Fees Discussed Here\\n\\n| Charge type                          | Amount/Calculation |\\n|-------------------------------------|--------------------|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee             | $25.00 |\\n| Waiver threshold (per period)       | $5,000 |\\n| Domestic wire (outgoing)            | $15.00 |\\n| Domestic out-of-network ATM         | $2.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal              | 2.5% (minimum $4.00) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Requesting a Fee Review\\n\\nProvide the following to expedite resolution:\\n- Statement period and the specific fee(s) in question\\n- For maintenance fee reviews: balance evidence relative to $5,000 during the period\\n- For domestic wire fees: wire date, amount, and reference\\n- For ATM fees: date/time, location, receipt (showing any operator surcharge), and the withdrawal amount used to compute the fee\\n\\nSubmit this information through your usual Rho support channel.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEc_7UD5cdBtxtopjzsoZSfMgFHlt26BGC3Y9foNMz1MeWwcCZ139T1sl5N0YELTwP0NYXaN_k1DaBIfXhgYlj5bLb2SgR83nOmu7n7mUW4z3--Q2KC9UHkl0dYoP7WhfzRSoCrCE5wx2xuEshH8RpK7A2gediVYV9HnvAAJFBGBzB-y9Mpe3T0oRNs5_hFohQ5zOsPJR31qEVd6rXAMHoIfFkPk9spBzhPhcvVzLRKeAsq_jhilejinDY7GZfSw71j5A8ZxSyhm8YoTQSO8YEUEMfXFIO2w8gNb58wqxd2bVhXX-vL-iwueGo-JK24KWtIplVE8QoI5gDKQ9DI-hp8YLrNTlDn4E2IRi-OOojmx9bvEEex9e7OA616WaozWPVVMKboXWpdrmXbyQgvXoQE84nx8UCNxKzJgA-At1of9L3WRnZ_JONZhhsU_doRHkYbhySEDLrONzVSYlV4gafzSHwRBII7W7cC9UjPb3cQv6FSNaDfAxlGldHE1ByvR7loK6nW_zL9PN4R4b0gwUcVwdoxfH92WN0FWE0tGEh4Oa9cAhWHvKtJeOYX7qAVa4NjStOS9YkHiS44GW-l7PcNb_0R5Q1HsiIUqQHxO5s-AHRiJ2h-moQg3MmA-qWtL0ey5vXNvCCmrM9coLdR3EmTqRkZtAwXoESo9IW-WQ0H_2_dsjHKOZGnF5sy2OmdwQIY3AXD6eOYPlwGPDDrkCvktLPWOlT2dYj9D--VEFO9HbD3xPLWLWJjITzZR5pJ3zNrpIfp2vrhEQROT3xRQljs5QHoaKBvaudtdqcA4QApElxM8VbW9dD1RFhYkxaWpoDyYj-P0m2Jzn8vi9y07Ll0eEW69zWp2uqxWe2yQihJkquhRtElkHk8W0mQGrbHguOrlqwTlaw2XtE0elRN6jDfXmtZyEU3RvYipAgQpsSSXjtljEkCHeHG00mj4CP25jl_gESAXv62O3rI0mK9fLmR8_ZHKHr5kpCZ21MrOUW3Sbc60WunTi5naRdnkHyr-1s2Z3xM0uub-ftnMOCH7tQqBo3RiAhxKTU67OP3TsjwM0zQCAdYo_GPeVVsajk0a-d5kK9ZIZbMJOHDh0NhEPTDn9RYAwTYzhnC4jfH4QVZBVwxgTzB1rqfqmk5nVW7Aex7EhF2_wGUVDU_cbgMwQO1CKM9OP4m2wWQUtukNMHa7QIGEocO6WYql2FHiyZBGgOVq_1RI0su8QL-bbDXrq4UepSLRvGt2DKUDJAbx5G0VuzAx3zCfOrueT3nKIEq25IUhoTMY6rgRK6fvE-SctoCv9FC7X3oRmEBzpAEBJxsXwwyvh8Dw1Knm3NSgZ7MndgmiP5gkvumFCiAVCBfbeutnkg==\",\"id\":\"rs_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc473ccd8887d18f208b05c4d513a4\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Refining query approach**\\n\\nI realize that longer queries aren't effective for retrieving the right results. Instead, I need to focus on using targeted, specific names like “Cobalt,” “Sky,” and “Lime.” That should help me get better, more relevant guidance. Keeping it concise seems key for efficiency! Let’s aim for proper names only moving forward. This should definitely streamline my search process. I'm excited to see how this improves my results!\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Cobalt Blue\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_PXKMiBVfwstIoP0dDfiX8kko\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc473ed72487d1bd22a7ae5b8013e8\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Sky Blue\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_wersEzKlmkqyoV4LCB1HH8xh\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc473ed74487d194a85ba7038af683\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Lime Green\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_0vEoEjDWUNvoWabctT0AI66G\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc473ed75487d18eb631add6ca84a1\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_PXKMiBVfwstIoP0dDfiX8kko\",\"output\":\"1. Troubleshooting: Unexpected Charges on Cobalt Blue\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_009\\n   Score: 6.3937\\n   Content: ## Identify the charge\\n- Review the exact transaction description on your statement or in your transaction history (e.g., “Monthly Maintenance Fee,” “Wire Transfer – Domestic,” “ATM Fee,” “International ATM Withdrawal Fee,” “Excess Transaction Fee”).\\n- Note the posting date, amount, and any memo or terminal/location details.\\n- Compare the posting date to your recent account activity (wires sent, ATM withdrawals, transaction volume, month-end).\\n\\n## Common Cobalt Blue charges that may appear\\n| Line item on statement | Why it appears | How to confirm | Amount |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly Maintenance Fee | Your account did not meet the balance waiver requirement during the statement period. | Check the Fee Summary on your statement and verify whether your balance met $2,500 for the period. | $20.00 |\\n| Excess Transaction Fee | You exceeded your monthly free transaction limit. | Count your posted transactions for the statement period and compare to your free allowance; the fee line often notes the number of excess items. | $0.25 per excess transaction |\\n| Wire Transfer Fee – Domestic | You initiated a domestic wire transfer. | Confirm a wire was submitted on or near the posting date in your transfer history. | $20.00 |\\n| ATM Fee – Out of Network | You used a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | Match the fee date to an ATM withdrawal at a non‑Rho terminal. Note: the ATM owner may also assess a separate surcharge. | $2.00 per ATM transaction |\\n| International ATM Withdrawal Fee | You withdrew cash at a foreign (international) ATM. | Match the fee date/location to an overseas ATM withdrawal. | 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, minimum $4.00 |\\n\\nNote: Cobalt Blue does not assess overdraft fees. If you see a charge that appears to be an overdraft fee, review the line’s exact description—it may correspond to one of the fees above. If still unclear, request a review.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting by charge type\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee posted unexpectedly\\n- Verify whether your account met the waiver balance requirement of $2,500 during the statement period.\\n- Check if the fee posted at or just after the statement cycle date.\\n- Compare your balance history for the full period; large debits near period‑end can affect waiver eligibility.\\n- If you believe you qualified for the waiver, request a fee review and include your statement period dates and balance evidence.\\n\\n### Excess Transaction Fee you didn’t anticipate\\n- Add up your posted transactions for the statement period and compare to your plan’s free monthly transaction limit.\\n- Open the fee detail to see how many items were assessed at $0.25 each.\\n- If the count appears off, provide a list of the transactions you believe were miscounted when requesting a review.\\n\\n### Wire Transfer Fee – Domestic you didn’t expect\\n- Confirm whether a domestic wire was sent on the fee date (or one business day prior).\\n- Distinguish wires from other transfers by the transaction description (“Wire,” routing via Fedwire, etc.).\\n- If you did not authorize a wire, report immediately for investigation. Otherwise, the standard fee is $20.00.\\n\\n### ATM fees: domestic vs. international\\n- Out‑of‑network (domestic) ATM usage: Expect $2.00 per ATM transaction. This is separate from any surcharge by the ATM owner, which can appear as a separate line item.\\n- Foreign (international) ATM withdrawals: The fee is 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00. Example: for a withdrawal, multiply the amount by 2.5%; if that result is less than $4.00, the minimum applies.\\n\\n## Quick checklist before requesting a review\\n- Match the fee’s posting date to a specific action (wire, ATM withdrawal, month‑end, spike in transaction volume).\\n- Capture screenshots of:\\n  - The fee line item (showing date, amount, and description)\\n  - Any related transaction (wire confirmation, ATM withdrawal)\\n  - The relevant statement page (Fee Summary and balance history for the period)\\n- Briefly explain why the fee appears incorrect (e.g., you met $2,500 during the period, transaction count appears miscalculated, withdrawal was domestic vs. international, etc.).\\n\\n## Requesting a review or dispute\\n- Contact us as soon as you notice the charge.\\n- Include: account name, last 4 digits, statement period, fee date/amount/description, and your supporting screenshots or documents.\\n- We will investigate and correct any misapplied fees. If additional information is needed (e.g., to verify ATM location or wire authorization), we will follow up.\\n\\n2. Internal: Opening Business Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_003\\n   Score: 6.2571\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nTo open a business checking account, ensure all of the following are true:\\n1. The customer is verified.\\n2. The customer has at least one existing personal checking account with status OPEN.\\n3. The customer does not exceed 6 business checking accounts.\\n4. The customer has no accounts with status CLOSED.\\n5. The customer's existing checking account has a balance of at least $500.\\n\\n## Opening Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify customer identity.\\n2. Check eligibility requirements listed above.\\n3. Confirm the customer's desired account_class selection.\\n   - Business checking account_class options include Navy Blue, Cobalt Blue, True Blue, etc.\\n4. Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account.\\n\\n3. How to transition a Light Green Account to Blue or Green Account (checking)\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_light_green_account_010\\n   Score: 6.1398\\n   Content: ## Determine if the change is automatic\\n- If Yes is True, your account will convert to an eligible adult checking option automatically at the appropriate time.\\n\\n## If the change is not automatic\\n- If Yes is False, initiate a move to Blue or Green Account (checking) by submitting an upgrade request and selecting your preferred account type.\\n\\n### Before you switch\\n- Compare features and fees of Blue and Green Account (checking) to choose the best fit.\\n- Confirm that any scheduled payments or deposits will continue without interruption after the transition.\\n\\n4. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_013\\n   Score: 5.7650\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Sky Blue account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Lime Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Sky Blue nor Lime Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our startup and premium business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n5. FAQ: Blue Account\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_010\\n   Score: 5.6319\\n   Content: ## Frequently asked questions\\n\\n### What does a paper statement cost?\\nPaper statements are available for $2.50 per month.\\n\\n### What APY do I earn on my balance?\\nYour Blue Account earns 0.01% APY on balances.\\n\\n### Can I set low-balance alerts?\\nYes. You can enable alerts at a threshold such as $62 so you are notified when your available balance reaches that level.\\n\\n### How long do external bank transfers take?\\nTransfers to another bank typically complete in 2 business days.\\n\\n### What happens if a deposited check is returned unpaid?\\nIf a deposited check is returned by the issuing bank, a returned deposit fee of $15.00 applies.\\n\\n### Is there a fee to receive a domestic wire?\\nYes. Incoming domestic wires are assessed a fee of $12.50 per wire.\\n\\n### Does the Blue Account have a referral program?\\nYes. When you refer someone to open a Blue Account, you earn $35 for each successful referral. The person you refer receives $30 as a welcome bonus.\\n\\n### What are the requirements for the referral bonus?\\nThe referred person must deposit at least $500 within 60 days of opening their account. A minimum banking relationship of 30 days is required to participate—this is measured from when you first opened any checking account with us.\\n\\n### Is there a limit to how many referral bonuses I can earn?\\nYes. You can earn up to 5 referral bonuses per calendar year.\\n\\n6. Light Blue Account Referral Program\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_light_blue_account_007\\n   Score: 5.4332\\n   Content: ## Earn rewards by referring friends\\n\\nShare the Light Blue Account with others and earn cash bonuses.\\n\\n### What you earn\\n- Referral bonus: $30 for each successful referral\\n- Maximum referrals: 5 per calendar year\\n\\n### What they receive\\n- Welcome bonus: $20 when they open and fund their account\\n\\n### Requirements\\n\\n| Requirement | Detail |\\n|---|---|\\n| Qualifying deposit | $500 |\\n| Deposit window | Within 60 days of account opening |\\n| Referrer tenure | 30 days |\\n\\n### How it works\\n1. Share your unique referral link with friends and family\\n2. They open a Light Blue Account using your link\\n3. They deposit at least $500 within 60 days\\n4. You receive $30 and they receive $20\\n\\n### Eligibility\\n- To qualify as a referrer, you must have been a Rho-Bank checking account holder for 30 days or longer.\\n- You can earn up to 5 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n\\n7. True Blue Account: Fee Waivers and Balance Requirements\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_002\\n   Score: 5.2901\\n   Content: ## Waiving your monthly maintenance fee\\n- You will be charged $75.00 each month unless you meet the waiver threshold.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is waived when your balance is at least $50,000 during the statement period.\\n\\n## Minimum balance requirement vs. fee waiver threshold\\n- Minimum balance requirement: $25,000 to maintain the account and access premium features.\\n- Fee waiver threshold: $50,000 to waive the $75.00 monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Falling below $25,000 may limit access to premium features until your balance is restored.\\n\\n## Overdrafts and shortfalls\\n- If your balance goes negative, a per-occurrence overdraft fee of $25.00 may apply.\\n\\n## How to avoid fees\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $50,000 to waive the monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Set internal processes to monitor balances against both $25,000 and $50,000.\\n- If a shortfall is anticipated, transfer funds promptly to avoid the $25.00 and preserve eligibility for the fee waiver.\\n\\n## True Blue Referral Program\\n\\nRefer other high-volume businesses to True Blue and earn significant rewards:\\n\\n| Benefit | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Referrer bonus | $350 per referral |\\n| New member bonus | $250 |\\n| Maximum referrals per year | 15 |\\n| Qualifying deposit | $50,000 |\\n| Deposit window | 120 days |\\n| Account age requirement | 90 days |\\n\\n### Referral requirements\\n- The referred business must deposit $50,000 within 120 days of opening their True Blue account.\\n- Eligibility is based on how long you've been a Rho-Bank checking customer. The account age threshold is 90 days, calculated from when you opened your oldest checking account.\\n- Referral bonuses are paid after qualification is confirmed and are subject to the annual limit of 15.\\n\\n8. Cobalt Blue: Payments and Transfers Explained\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_005\\n   Score: 4.6772\\n   Content: ## ACH transfers\\n- Standard ACH transfers are available with no fee\\n- Same-day ACH transfers are available with a fee of $0.00\\n- Submission and approval cutoffs apply for same-day processing; initiate early to improve the likelihood of same-day delivery\\n\\n## Domestic wire transfers\\n- Outgoing domestic wire transfer fee: $20.00\\n- Use wires when you need confirmed, rapid delivery to U.S. financial institutions\\n\\n## Incoming wires\\n- You get 5 incoming domestic wire transfers per month at no charge\\n- Additional incoming domestic wires beyond this included amount may incur a fee\\n\\n## Choosing the right method\\n- Prefer ACH for routine payments where timing is flexible\\n- Use same-day ACH when faster delivery is needed at the same-day ACH timetable\\n- Select domestic wires for time-sensitive or high-assurance payments\\n\\n## Tracking and confirmations\\n- Review transfer status in your activity feed\\n- Save beneficiary details to reduce entry errors and speed up future payments\\n\\n## Referral bonus requirements\\nIf you're referring another business to Cobalt Blue, here are the qualification details:\\n- Qualifying deposit: The referred business must deposit at least $7,500 to trigger the referral bonus\\n- Time window: This deposit must be made within 90 days of account opening\\n- Your eligibility: To participate, your earliest-opened Rho-Bank checking account must have reached 60 days of age.\\n\\n9. Linked Checking Account APY Boosts for Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_012\\n   Score: 4.4821\\n   Content: Certain personal checking and savings account pairings provide bonus APY on your savings account balance. When you hold both a qualifying checking account and savings account under the same customer profile, the APY boost is automatically applied to your savings account. The following checking and savings account pairings qualify for APY boosts:\\n\\n1. Green Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n3. Evergreen Account (checking) + Green Account (savings)\\n4. Blue Account (checking) + Silver Plus Account (savings)\\n5. Light Green Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n6. Dark Green Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n7. Bluest Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n8. Purple Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n9. Gold Years Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n10. Light Green Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n11. Green Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n12. Evergreen Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n13. Bluest Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n14. Purple Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n15. Gold Years Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n16. Blue Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n17. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n18. Dark Green Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n\\nNote: Only these specific pairings qualify for the linked checking account APY boost. All other checking and savings account combinations do not receive any APY boost from linking. The boost is additive to your savings account's base APY and any credit card APY bonuses you may already have. For the exact APY boost percentages for each pairing, please refer to the specific savings account documentation.\\n\\n10. Getting Started with World Blue International Checking\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_world_blue_001\\n   Score: 4.2730\\n   Content: ## Quick checklist before you begin\\n- Confirm you can maintain at least $10,000 across currencies to keep the account in good standing\\n- Be aware of the monthly maintenance fee of $50.00\\n- Decide which of the up to 35 supported currencies you plan to hold and transact in\\n- Verify that your intended counterparties and destinations are within the $140 supported regions for sending and receiving payments\\n\\n## Initial setup steps\\n- Fund your account so you can meet ongoing balance needs\\n- Add the currency wallets you will use for operations and settlements\\n- Set a primary operating currency for reporting and reconciliation\\n- Configure payee profiles for your frequent counterparties within the supported regions\\n- Review user access and prepare to assign permissions based on roles and responsibilities\\n\\n## Key thresholds and limits at a glance\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $50.00 |\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $10,000 |\\n| Supported currencies | 35 |\\n| Supported regions for payments | $140 |\\n\\n## First-week best practices\\n- Keep an operating buffer above $10,000 to avoid service interruptions\\n- Start with a small set of currency wallets and expand as your payment flows stabilize\\n- Validate a test payment to a known counterparty in one of the supported regions and confirm posting and reconciliation\\n- Set alerts and reports aligned to your treasury cadence to monitor balances and activity\\n\\n## Referring other businesses to World Blue\\n\\nAs a Rho-Bank checking account holder, you can refer other businesses to World Blue. To be eligible to refer:\\n- You must have maintained checking account status with Rho-Bank for at least 90 days\\n\\nFor a referral to qualify:\\n- The referred business must open a World Blue account\\n- They must deposit at least $25,000 within 90 days of account opening\\n\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_wersEzKlmkqyoV4LCB1HH8xh\",\"output\":\"1. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_013\\n   Score: 14.2273\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Sky Blue account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Lime Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Sky Blue nor Lime Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our startup and premium business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n2. How to transition a Light Green Account to Blue or Green Account (checking)\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_light_green_account_010\\n   Score: 6.1398\\n   Content: ## Determine if the change is automatic\\n- If Yes is True, your account will convert to an eligible adult checking option automatically at the appropriate time.\\n\\n## If the change is not automatic\\n- If Yes is False, initiate a move to Blue or Green Account (checking) by submitting an upgrade request and selecting your preferred account type.\\n\\n### Before you switch\\n- Compare features and fees of Blue and Green Account (checking) to choose the best fit.\\n- Confirm that any scheduled payments or deposits will continue without interruption after the transition.\\n\\n3. FAQ: Blue Account\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_010\\n   Score: 5.6319\\n   Content: ## Frequently asked questions\\n\\n### What does a paper statement cost?\\nPaper statements are available for $2.50 per month.\\n\\n### What APY do I earn on my balance?\\nYour Blue Account earns 0.01% APY on balances.\\n\\n### Can I set low-balance alerts?\\nYes. You can enable alerts at a threshold such as $62 so you are notified when your available balance reaches that level.\\n\\n### How long do external bank transfers take?\\nTransfers to another bank typically complete in 2 business days.\\n\\n### What happens if a deposited check is returned unpaid?\\nIf a deposited check is returned by the issuing bank, a returned deposit fee of $15.00 applies.\\n\\n### Is there a fee to receive a domestic wire?\\nYes. Incoming domestic wires are assessed a fee of $12.50 per wire.\\n\\n### Does the Blue Account have a referral program?\\nYes. When you refer someone to open a Blue Account, you earn $35 for each successful referral. The person you refer receives $30 as a welcome bonus.\\n\\n### What are the requirements for the referral bonus?\\nThe referred person must deposit at least $500 within 60 days of opening their account. A minimum banking relationship of 30 days is required to participate—this is measured from when you first opened any checking account with us.\\n\\n### Is there a limit to how many referral bonuses I can earn?\\nYes. You can earn up to 5 referral bonuses per calendar year.\\n\\n4. Light Blue Account Referral Program\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_light_blue_account_007\\n   Score: 5.4332\\n   Content: ## Earn rewards by referring friends\\n\\nShare the Light Blue Account with others and earn cash bonuses.\\n\\n### What you earn\\n- Referral bonus: $30 for each successful referral\\n- Maximum referrals: 5 per calendar year\\n\\n### What they receive\\n- Welcome bonus: $20 when they open and fund their account\\n\\n### Requirements\\n\\n| Requirement | Detail |\\n|---|---|\\n| Qualifying deposit | $500 |\\n| Deposit window | Within 60 days of account opening |\\n| Referrer tenure | 30 days |\\n\\n### How it works\\n1. Share your unique referral link with friends and family\\n2. They open a Light Blue Account using your link\\n3. They deposit at least $500 within 60 days\\n4. You receive $30 and they receive $20\\n\\n### Eligibility\\n- To qualify as a referrer, you must have been a Rho-Bank checking account holder for 30 days or longer.\\n- You can earn up to 5 referral bonuses per calendar year\\n\\n5. True Blue Account: Fee Waivers and Balance Requirements\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_002\\n   Score: 5.2901\\n   Content: ## Waiving your monthly maintenance fee\\n- You will be charged $75.00 each month unless you meet the waiver threshold.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is waived when your balance is at least $50,000 during the statement period.\\n\\n## Minimum balance requirement vs. fee waiver threshold\\n- Minimum balance requirement: $25,000 to maintain the account and access premium features.\\n- Fee waiver threshold: $50,000 to waive the $75.00 monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Falling below $25,000 may limit access to premium features until your balance is restored.\\n\\n## Overdrafts and shortfalls\\n- If your balance goes negative, a per-occurrence overdraft fee of $25.00 may apply.\\n\\n## How to avoid fees\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $50,000 to waive the monthly maintenance fee.\\n- Set internal processes to monitor balances against both $25,000 and $50,000.\\n- If a shortfall is anticipated, transfer funds promptly to avoid the $25.00 and preserve eligibility for the fee waiver.\\n\\n## True Blue Referral Program\\n\\nRefer other high-volume businesses to True Blue and earn significant rewards:\\n\\n| Benefit | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Referrer bonus | $350 per referral |\\n| New member bonus | $250 |\\n| Maximum referrals per year | 15 |\\n| Qualifying deposit | $50,000 |\\n| Deposit window | 120 days |\\n| Account age requirement | 90 days |\\n\\n### Referral requirements\\n- The referred business must deposit $50,000 within 120 days of opening their True Blue account.\\n- Eligibility is based on how long you've been a Rho-Bank checking customer. The account age threshold is 90 days, calculated from when you opened your oldest checking account.\\n- Referral bonuses are paid after qualification is confirmed and are subject to the annual limit of 15.\\n\\n6. Internal: Closing Business Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_007\\n   Score: 5.0004\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n- Customer has no linked business savings accounts that are still OPEN (close those first)\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Navy Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $50 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 7 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (True Blue, Sky Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $100 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 14 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Cobalt Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $200 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 21 days\\n  - Requires supervisor review\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (accounts with credit lines over $100,000)\\n  - Early closure fee: $400 if closed within 270 days\\n  - Notice period: 30 days\\n  - Requires manager approval\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. For PREMIUM tier, obtain supervisor review. For ELITE tier, obtain manager approval.\\n4. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n7. Getting Started with Sky Blue: Startup Account Setup\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_sky_blue_001\\n   Score: 4.9446\\n   Content: ## Verify Eligibility\\n- Confirm your company is within 4 years of formation.\\n- Check whether you meet the funding requirement: 0.\\n\\n## Understand Key Cost Terms Before You Apply\\n- Your startup receives a free period of 6 months.\\n- After the free period, the monthly maintenance fee is $25.00.\\n- If your balance goes negative, the overdraft fee is $0.00.\\n\\n## Prepare Your Application\\n- Gather company formation documents and ownership details.\\n- Be ready to provide basic business information and authorized signers.\\n- Plan initial account settings, such as user permissions and card controls, so you can activate quickly after approval.\\n\\n## Submit and Configure\\n- Complete the online application and upload requested documents.\\n- After approval, log in to set user roles, spending controls, and alerts.\\n- Link external accounts to enable seamless transfers.\\n\\n## Startup Referral Program\\nHelp other startups get started with Sky Blue:\\n- Your bonus: $150 for each successful referral\\n- Their bonus: $250 welcome bonus\\n- Annual limit: 8 referrals per year\\n\\n## First-Funding and Go-Live Checklist\\n- Make an initial deposit from a linked account.\\n- Confirm your free period of 6 months is visible in your billing section.\\n- Review your fee settings to ensure you understand the transition to $25.00 and the overdraft policy of $0.00.\\n\\n8. Linked Checking Account APY Boosts for Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_012\\n   Score: 4.4821\\n   Content: Certain personal checking and savings account pairings provide bonus APY on your savings account balance. When you hold both a qualifying checking account and savings account under the same customer profile, the APY boost is automatically applied to your savings account. The following checking and savings account pairings qualify for APY boosts:\\n\\n1. Green Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n3. Evergreen Account (checking) + Green Account (savings)\\n4. Blue Account (checking) + Silver Plus Account (savings)\\n5. Light Green Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n6. Dark Green Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n7. Bluest Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n8. Purple Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n9. Gold Years Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n10. Light Green Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n11. Green Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n12. Evergreen Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n13. Bluest Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n14. Purple Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n15. Gold Years Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n16. Blue Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n17. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n18. Dark Green Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n\\nNote: Only these specific pairings qualify for the linked checking account APY boost. All other checking and savings account combinations do not receive any APY boost from linking. The boost is additive to your savings account's base APY and any credit card APY bonuses you may already have. For the exact APY boost percentages for each pairing, please refer to the specific savings account documentation.\\n\\n9. Getting Started with World Blue International Checking\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_world_blue_001\\n   Score: 4.2730\\n   Content: ## Quick checklist before you begin\\n- Confirm you can maintain at least $10,000 across currencies to keep the account in good standing\\n- Be aware of the monthly maintenance fee of $50.00\\n- Decide which of the up to 35 supported currencies you plan to hold and transact in\\n- Verify that your intended counterparties and destinations are within the $140 supported regions for sending and receiving payments\\n\\n## Initial setup steps\\n- Fund your account so you can meet ongoing balance needs\\n- Add the currency wallets you will use for operations and settlements\\n- Set a primary operating currency for reporting and reconciliation\\n- Configure payee profiles for your frequent counterparties within the supported regions\\n- Review user access and prepare to assign permissions based on roles and responsibilities\\n\\n## Key thresholds and limits at a glance\\n\\n| Item | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $50.00 |\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $10,000 |\\n| Supported currencies | 35 |\\n| Supported regions for payments | $140 |\\n\\n## First-week best practices\\n- Keep an operating buffer above $10,000 to avoid service interruptions\\n- Start with a small set of currency wallets and expand as your payment flows stabilize\\n- Validate a test payment to a known counterparty in one of the supported regions and confirm posting and reconciliation\\n- Set alerts and reports aligned to your treasury cadence to monitor balances and activity\\n\\n## Referring other businesses to World Blue\\n\\nAs a Rho-Bank checking account holder, you can refer other businesses to World Blue. To be eligible to refer:\\n- You must have maintained checking account status with Rho-Bank for at least 90 days\\n\\nFor a referral to qualify:\\n- The referred business must open a World Blue account\\n- They must deposit at least $25,000 within 90 days of account opening\\n\\n\\n10. Internal: Closing Personal Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_005\\n   Score: 3.6714\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Light Blue Account, Light Green Account, Green Fee-Free Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $15 if closed within 30 days\\n  - Notice period: 0 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (Blue Account, Green Account (checking))\\n  - Early closure fee: $25 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 3 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Evergreen Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $50 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 7 days\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (Bluest Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $100 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 14 days\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=0ms, reranking=0ms, total=0ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_0vEoEjDWUNvoWabctT0AI66G\",\"output\":\"1. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - October 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_014\\n   Score: 13.0374\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 10/12/2025 TO 11/12/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Lime Green account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Hunter Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Lime Green nor Hunter Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our premium and eco-conscious business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n2. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_013\\n   Score: 12.1403\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Sky Blue account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Lime Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Sky Blue nor Lime Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our startup and premium business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n3. Lime Green Account: Your Dedicated Account Manager\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_003\\n   Score: 9.6978\\n   Content: ## Response commitments\\n- Direct messages receive a response within 2 business hours.\\n- When calling the priority line, the maximum expected wait is 6 minutes.\\n\\n## How to reach your manager\\n- Send a secure message from within your account's support center and select the option to route to your dedicated manager.\\n- For urgent matters, call the priority support line; your call is queued with elevated priority and subject to the 6 minute maximum wait.\\n\\n## Getting the most out of manager support\\n- Provide context upfront:\\n  - The specific transaction or transfer you need help with.\\n  - Any relevant dates and counterparties.\\n  - Screenshots of error messages (if applicable).\\n- Set your preferred contact method so your manager can follow up quickly.\\n- For time-sensitive requests, note the deadline in your initial message; your manager will respond within 2 business hours.\\n\\n## Escalations\\n- If an issue requires faster handling than messaging, use the priority phone line for a live update within the 6 minute window.\\n\\n## Referral program for Lime Green members\\n\\nAs a Rho-Bank checking account holder, you can refer other businesses to Lime Green and earn substantial rewards:\\n\\n- **Your bonus**: $200 for each successful referral\\n- **Their bonus**: $150 welcome bonus for the referred business\\n- **Annual cap**: 12 referrals per year\\n- **Qualification**: Referred business must deposit $15,000 within 90 days\\n- **Eligibility**: You must have maintained checking account status with Rho-Bank for a minimum of 90 days.\\n\\nSpeak with your dedicated account manager for personalized referral strategies and tracking.\\n\\n4. EcoCard: How to Earn Sustainability Points on Green Purchases\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_ecocard_002\\n   Score: 5.3061\\n   Content: ## Earning Rates\\n- Green purchases: Earn $5.00 sustainability points per dollar spent at qualifying green merchants and categories.\\n- Other purchases: Earn $1.00 sustainability points per dollar.\\n\\n## How to Maximize Green Earnings\\n- Use your card at certified green partners and eco-friendly categories (e.g., public transit, EV charging, renewable energy subscriptions) to receive the higher earn rate.\\n- When shopping online, check that the merchant is listed as a qualifying green merchant before checkout.\\n\\n## Examples\\n- A $100 purchase at a qualifying green merchant earns 100 × $5.00 points.\\n- A $100 purchase at a non-green merchant earns 100 × $1.00 points.\\n\\n## Tips to Ensure You Earn Correctly\\n- Keep transactions separate: If a cart mixes green and non-green items at a non-partner merchant, the entire purchase may earn at the non-green rate.\\n- Save receipts for any purchases you believe should qualify as green; this helps in resolving any earn-rate disputes.\\n- If a transaction is returned or refunded, the corresponding points will be reversed at the original earn rate.\\n\\n5. EcoCard: Which Merchants and Purchases Qualify as Green?\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_ecocard_003\\n   Score: 5.2948\\n   Content: ## What Qualifies as Green\\n- You earn $5.00 points per dollar on purchases that meet our green criteria, which generally include:\\n  - Public transportation passes and fares\\n  - Electric vehicle charging\\n  - Renewable energy subscriptions and providers\\n  - Certified sustainable retailers and eco-labeled products\\n  - Local bike share and micromobility services\\n\\n## Partner Network\\n- We maintain a network of approximately 3 certified green merchant partners.\\n- Purchases at these partners are recognized automatically as green.\\n\\n## Verifying Merchant Eligibility\\n- Look for a green badge in our merchant directory before you pay.\\n- On receipts and statements, eligible transactions may display a green indicator.\\n- If you believe a purchase should qualify, contact support with your receipt and merchant details for review.\\n\\n## Common Edge Cases\\n- Marketplaces and delivery platforms may process payments through non-green parent entities; in those cases, the purchase may not qualify.\\n- Mixed carts at non-partner merchants may not qualify if the merchant cannot provide item-level green data.\\n- Gift cards and cash equivalents typically do not qualify as green purchases.\\n\\n6. Linked Checking Account APY Boosts for Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_012\\n   Score: 5.2112\\n   Content: Certain personal checking and savings account pairings provide bonus APY on your savings account balance. When you hold both a qualifying checking account and savings account under the same customer profile, the APY boost is automatically applied to your savings account. The following checking and savings account pairings qualify for APY boosts:\\n\\n1. Green Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n2. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n3. Evergreen Account (checking) + Green Account (savings)\\n4. Blue Account (checking) + Silver Plus Account (savings)\\n5. Light Green Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n6. Dark Green Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n7. Bluest Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n8. Purple Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n9. Gold Years Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n10. Light Green Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n11. Green Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n12. Evergreen Account (checking) + Diamond Elite Account (savings)\\n13. Bluest Account (checking) + Bronze Account (savings)\\n14. Purple Account (checking) + Gold Account (savings)\\n15. Gold Years Account (checking) + Silver Account (savings)\\n16. Blue Account (checking) + Platinum Account (savings)\\n17. Green Fee-Free Account (checking) + Gold Plus Account (savings)\\n18. Dark Green Account (checking) + Platinum Plus Account (savings)\\n\\nNote: Only these specific pairings qualify for the linked checking account APY boost. All other checking and savings account combinations do not receive any APY boost from linking. The boost is additive to your savings account's base APY and any credit card APY bonuses you may already have. For the exact APY boost percentages for each pairing, please refer to the specific savings account documentation.\\n\\n7. Why am I being charged a fee on my Lime Green Account?\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_lime_green_008\\n   Score: 4.8683\\n   Content: ## Common reasons you may see a fee\\n\\nYou may see one or more of the following fees on your Lime Green Account:\\n\\n- Monthly maintenance fee if your balance does not meet the waiver threshold\\n- Fees for sending domestic or international wire transfers\\n- Fees for using non‑Rho ATMs, including percentage‑based fees for foreign ATM withdrawals\\n\\n### Quick reference\\n\\n| Fee type | When it’s charged | Amount |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | Your balance does not meet the waiver threshold | $25.00 |\\n| Domestic wire transfer | You send a domestic wire | $10.00 |\\n| International wire transfer | You send an international wire to a foreign bank | $25.00 |\\n| Non‑Rho ATM (U.S.) | You withdraw cash at a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | $1.00 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal | You withdraw cash at an international ATM | 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, minimum $2.50 |\\n\\n## Monthly maintenance fee\\n\\n- You are charged $25.00 when your account balance does not meet $15,000.\\n- To avoid this fee, maintain a balance at or above $15,000.\\n\\n## Wire transfer fees\\n\\n- Domestic wires: Each outgoing domestic wire you send incurs a fee of $10.00.\\n- International wires: Each outgoing international wire to a foreign bank incurs a fee of $25.00.\\n\\n## ATM‑related fees\\n\\n- Non‑Rho ATMs in the U.S.: You are charged $1.00 per withdrawal when using a non‑Rho ATM.\\n- Foreign (international) ATMs: You are charged 1.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum fee of $2.50.\\n  - How to estimate: Multiply your withdrawal amount by 1.5% and compare the result to $2.50. The higher number is the fee.\\n\\n## How to confirm which fee was charged\\n\\n1. Review your transaction history for a separate fee line item (for example, a description referencing maintenance, wire, or ATM).\\n2. Match the amount to one of the following:\\n   - $25.00\\n   - $10.00\\n   - $25.00\\n   - $1.00\\n   - For foreign ATM withdrawals, the greater of:\\n     - 1.5% of your withdrawal amount, or\\n     - $2.50\\n\\n## Ways to avoid or reduce fees\\n\\n- Maintain a balance of at least $15,000 to waive $25.00.\\n- Use Rho‑network ATMs to avoid the $1.00.\\n- Plan international cash needs to minimize the number of foreign ATM withdrawals subject to 1.5% (minimum $2.50).\\n\\n## If you believe a fee is incorrect\\n\\n- Gather details (date, amount, and description of the fee; related transaction, if any).\\n- Contact support with these details so we can review and correct any errors promptly.\\n\\n8. Green Account (savings): Pairing with EcoCard for bonus APY\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_003\\n   Score: 4.7472\\n   Content: ## Bonus APY with eligible eco cards\\n\\n### How the bonus works\\n- Your Green Account (savings) earns 4.0% on your balance.\\n- When you also hold an EcoCard, you receive an additional bonus of 0.5%.\\n- Your effective APY becomes 4.0% plus 0.5% while eligibility is maintained.\\n\\n### Extra rewards at eco-certified merchants\\n- Eligible purchases at eco-certified merchants can earn an extra cashback bonus of 2.0% when using an EcoCard.\\n\\n## Credit card APY bonuses\\n- Other Rho-Bank credit cards also provide APY bonuses on your Green Account (savings):\\n  - Bronze Rewards Card: +0%\\n  - Silver Rewards Card: +0.45%\\n  - Gold Rewards Card: +0%\\n  - Platinum Rewards Card: +0.35%\\n  - Diamond Elite Card: +0.6%\\n  - Green Rewards Card: +0.4%\\n  - Crypto-Cash Back Card: +0%\\n\\n### Maintaining eligibility\\n- Keep your eligible card in good standing and ensure it remains linked to your Green Account (savings).\\n- If the card is closed or unlinked, the bonus of 0.5% and the extra cashback of 2.0% will not apply.\\n\\n9. Emerald Saver vs Green Account (savings): What is the difference?\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_emerald_saver_003\\n   Score: 4.7074\\n   Content: ## Key differences to consider\\n\\n### Statement delivery\\n- Emerald Saver requires paperless statements: Yes.\\n- If you need mailed statements, review the Green Account (savings) terms to confirm its delivery options before choosing.\\n\\n### Environmental impact reporting cadence\\n- Emerald Saver provides environmental impact reporting on this schedule: monthly.\\n- If you prefer a different reporting cadence, compare the Green Account (savings) specification to see how it aligns with your needs.\\n\\n## Choosing between the two\\n- Select Emerald Saver when you want mandatory e‑statements and an impact update cadence of monthly.\\n- If printed statements or a different report timing is essential for your operations, verify the Green Account (savings) details prior to opening.\\n\\n10. EcoCard: Partner Merchants and Eco-Friendly Shopping Guide\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_ecocard_007\\n   Score: 4.5538\\n   Content: ## Finding Partner Merchants\\n- Shop confidently with our network of approximately 3 certified green merchant partners.\\n\\n## How to Locate Partners\\n- Use the in-app merchant directory and filter for certified green partners.\\n- Look for the green badge on merchant profiles and at checkout pages.\\n\\n## Shopping Tips\\n- Plan recurring eco-friendly expenses (e.g., transit passes, EV charging) with partner merchants to simplify tracking.\\n- When buying online, confirm the seller of record is the certified partner (not a third-party marketplace) to ensure recognition.\\n- Keep receipts for any purchases you believe should be recognized as eco-friendly if you need to request a review.\\n\\n## Staying Up to Date\\n- Partner lists can evolve; check the directory before large purchases.\\n- If your favorite eco merchant isn’t listed, suggest it through the feedback option in the directory.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEdBl5km10QJY060FmI2y3YBJtkvKzuCl_FJB6gf9MSSZ8IcF5AV7FxI28vBgcr2TqD0DsmKOoAmEs2fzeD1MA-sPT18uMW_3QfHPIxWYGH-6Rh72ttvoyfl2eR8wyEyuui1jD5zRxRtJuRPJe4zhiiTdR5xNBF9UYvlgrvAmjaX7XujfUDrq7JNfDamflQQvuNwPn2Umme3hkxAaDzUBzz2-j5Bq6DENRnpMd8SlXelhAZdvpJ_cVrFgW0m4oJDKjM1_htaawEt3Tvn0YkJhcPOWxV0GgwIeYeKder4Mk5P06c23iRgi3d94B7fKWDYj33HXHzMJ0yYDRIK0PqDlRSeVcffVmqrqB-9dTKfkdIu1PNPzOj02pCGhmXbSABP6aprhZLF9T5E6TCGhybJK-VB49OhKU2YsUH_h05Laxy5h7zl5YNIx-UlvazSkR8ynckTAv8ta8cw7xH3n3-mQR77N7usw9PeenfbvwMywbQrH9KCAPg1NoY1cYrSv3DlTOFE9xBeuezTEPzUUciYaPpfa85mmb1Gu4cHxsOPhYx2HOfF-rnIZoT1xO2TvcgOcjeW9QJO8mzc1aXFYfAYsVnwh9liEvlxvlkjnBiXm8TF7zcXJAG9v_pGGeK-vK_X6Zr0n22RgkdODF32fhwtUMGJZzAMHdR-pg2C5cZ7P_oAnn_WPPO3ukQIbfnABHjaQhOW5smC7bkFyt8BaQ8rWlsteWRtKY4jy4NV_NDsjwXVtJWLOCzAXccvpwT_OZdwdQ-EcUCTwS0BDYdk6CWgMogZHdYX6q_1iBtueUDkeOFBAweMJZfTwu6wLikSDDo8nj3qnOdf04QuFSlgQ8YQBIeKPFGocaTFvDdsPY3iwXzlMiXA9lknwjCGcNoQhj9deh90BgJ6pPru--hcqyihrsEnqeORZoReD3tThb6NrBpqfc1lIlPo-owxODep7zJAmU-X-6Wrw7e9sTNHrY3VkPa1bKYuDETFtsBW_AsRHLZaRZkY2qI-eWCSDmvyL4_y_K0hcqcx8LZiSkAx8DAYdm0PNPhaDcz8p622DiC8sVLlu75qd3YjOuHWo7AUgVu1rTk6bV_0Ieg3OkEIlS6EoGjO2kHGJHSLzNhxsuU7KgvPpXP-3uPoUrgS8mdfPHNt0zAOxKpEyBpSgSbPIFqgMNcYRI2oMDjvKok1RCb_nUWxR-yzl8qwtE_20xVz6WLrUFUBa6jVnIlPRFUVAdYHOtAyFg==\",\"id\":\"rs_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc4740d0a887d1ac4f6c90fee12d8c\",\"summary\":[],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Cobalt\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_kybtA9Sx7WV2z9GCl5hl9iVN\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc474194ec87d181603ed12c2392f4\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Sky\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_pCh66qo9H87NNF45iAXFDcIu\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc474194fc87d1a4d8af70bf129b45\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_kybtA9Sx7WV2z9GCl5hl9iVN\",\"output\":\"1. Internal: Opening Business Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_003\\n   Score: 6.2571\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nTo open a business checking account, ensure all of the following are true:\\n1. The customer is verified.\\n2. The customer has at least one existing personal checking account with status OPEN.\\n3. The customer does not exceed 6 business checking accounts.\\n4. The customer has no accounts with status CLOSED.\\n5. The customer's existing checking account has a balance of at least $500.\\n\\n## Opening Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify customer identity.\\n2. Check eligibility requirements listed above.\\n3. Confirm the customer's desired account_class selection.\\n   - Business checking account_class options include Navy Blue, Cobalt Blue, True Blue, etc.\\n4. Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account.\\n\\n2. Cobalt Blue: Payments and Transfers Explained\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_005\\n   Score: 4.6772\\n   Content: ## ACH transfers\\n- Standard ACH transfers are available with no fee\\n- Same-day ACH transfers are available with a fee of $0.00\\n- Submission and approval cutoffs apply for same-day processing; initiate early to improve the likelihood of same-day delivery\\n\\n## Domestic wire transfers\\n- Outgoing domestic wire transfer fee: $20.00\\n- Use wires when you need confirmed, rapid delivery to U.S. financial institutions\\n\\n## Incoming wires\\n- You get 5 incoming domestic wire transfers per month at no charge\\n- Additional incoming domestic wires beyond this included amount may incur a fee\\n\\n## Choosing the right method\\n- Prefer ACH for routine payments where timing is flexible\\n- Use same-day ACH when faster delivery is needed at the same-day ACH timetable\\n- Select domestic wires for time-sensitive or high-assurance payments\\n\\n## Tracking and confirmations\\n- Review transfer status in your activity feed\\n- Save beneficiary details to reduce entry errors and speed up future payments\\n\\n## Referral bonus requirements\\nIf you're referring another business to Cobalt Blue, here are the qualification details:\\n- Qualifying deposit: The referred business must deposit at least $7,500 to trigger the referral bonus\\n- Time window: This deposit must be made within 90 days of account opening\\n- Your eligibility: To participate, your earliest-opened Rho-Bank checking account must have reached 60 days of age.\\n\\n3. Getting Started with Cobalt Blue Business Checking\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_001\\n   Score: 4.0416\\n   Content: ## Set up your account\\nFollow these steps to start using your account immediately:\\n\\n- Fund your account to begin transacting and to work toward waiving the monthly fee\\n- Enroll in online and mobile banking to monitor balances, interest, and transaction activity\\n- Set account alerts for balance thresholds and transaction activity so you can stay on top of usage\\n- Add authorized users and establish permissions as needed for your business operations\\n\\n## Know your core costs and how to avoid them\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: $20.00\\n- How to waive it: maintain a daily balance at or above $2,500\\n\\nTip: Use balance alerts to help you remain above $2,500 throughout the statement cycle.\\n\\n## Start earning interest\\n- Your balance earns an APY of 0.5%\\n- Interest begins accruing once your initial deposit is received and available\\n\\n## Manage your monthly activity\\n- You get $175 free transactions per month (deposits, withdrawals, and transfers)\\n- After you use your included allotment, additional transactions may incur a fee\\n\\n## Grow your network with referrals\\nOnce you're established, refer other businesses to Cobalt Blue:\\n- You earn: $150 per successful referral\\n- They receive: $100 as a welcome bonus\\n- Maximum referrals: 10 per calendar year\\n\\n## First-week checklist\\n- Make your initial deposit and confirm it has posted\\n- Set a balance alert at or slightly above $2,500\\n- Review your current month's usage against the $175 limit\\n- Verify interest is accruing at 0.5% on your available balance\\n\\n## Where to find these details\\n- Account summary: shows current balance against the $2,500 waiver requirement\\n- Activity tracker: displays monthly usage versus the $175 limit\\n- Interest section: displays the current APY of 0.5% and accrued interest to date\\n\\n4. Troubleshooting: Unexpected Charges on Cobalt Blue\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_009\\n   Score: 3.7272\\n   Content: ## Identify the charge\\n- Review the exact transaction description on your statement or in your transaction history (e.g., “Monthly Maintenance Fee,” “Wire Transfer – Domestic,” “ATM Fee,” “International ATM Withdrawal Fee,” “Excess Transaction Fee”).\\n- Note the posting date, amount, and any memo or terminal/location details.\\n- Compare the posting date to your recent account activity (wires sent, ATM withdrawals, transaction volume, month-end).\\n\\n## Common Cobalt Blue charges that may appear\\n| Line item on statement | Why it appears | How to confirm | Amount |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Monthly Maintenance Fee | Your account did not meet the balance waiver requirement during the statement period. | Check the Fee Summary on your statement and verify whether your balance met $2,500 for the period. | $20.00 |\\n| Excess Transaction Fee | You exceeded your monthly free transaction limit. | Count your posted transactions for the statement period and compare to your free allowance; the fee line often notes the number of excess items. | $0.25 per excess transaction |\\n| Wire Transfer Fee – Domestic | You initiated a domestic wire transfer. | Confirm a wire was submitted on or near the posting date in your transfer history. | $20.00 |\\n| ATM Fee – Out of Network | You used a non‑Rho ATM in the U.S. | Match the fee date to an ATM withdrawal at a non‑Rho terminal. Note: the ATM owner may also assess a separate surcharge. | $2.00 per ATM transaction |\\n| International ATM Withdrawal Fee | You withdrew cash at a foreign (international) ATM. | Match the fee date/location to an overseas ATM withdrawal. | 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, minimum $4.00 |\\n\\nNote: Cobalt Blue does not assess overdraft fees. If you see a charge that appears to be an overdraft fee, review the line’s exact description—it may correspond to one of the fees above. If still unclear, request a review.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting by charge type\\n\\n### Monthly Maintenance Fee posted unexpectedly\\n- Verify whether your account met the waiver balance requirement of $2,500 during the statement period.\\n- Check if the fee posted at or just after the statement cycle date.\\n- Compare your balance history for the full period; large debits near period‑end can affect waiver eligibility.\\n- If you believe you qualified for the waiver, request a fee review and include your statement period dates and balance evidence.\\n\\n### Excess Transaction Fee you didn’t anticipate\\n- Add up your posted transactions for the statement period and compare to your plan’s free monthly transaction limit.\\n- Open the fee detail to see how many items were assessed at $0.25 each.\\n- If the count appears off, provide a list of the transactions you believe were miscounted when requesting a review.\\n\\n### Wire Transfer Fee – Domestic you didn’t expect\\n- Confirm whether a domestic wire was sent on the fee date (or one business day prior).\\n- Distinguish wires from other transfers by the transaction description (“Wire,” routing via Fedwire, etc.).\\n- If you did not authorize a wire, report immediately for investigation. Otherwise, the standard fee is $20.00.\\n\\n### ATM fees: domestic vs. international\\n- Out‑of‑network (domestic) ATM usage: Expect $2.00 per ATM transaction. This is separate from any surcharge by the ATM owner, which can appear as a separate line item.\\n- Foreign (international) ATM withdrawals: The fee is 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00. Example: for a withdrawal, multiply the amount by 2.5%; if that result is less than $4.00, the minimum applies.\\n\\n## Quick checklist before requesting a review\\n- Match the fee’s posting date to a specific action (wire, ATM withdrawal, month‑end, spike in transaction volume).\\n- Capture screenshots of:\\n  - The fee line item (showing date, amount, and description)\\n  - Any related transaction (wire confirmation, ATM withdrawal)\\n  - The relevant statement page (Fee Summary and balance history for the period)\\n- Briefly explain why the fee appears incorrect (e.g., you met $2,500 during the period, transaction count appears miscalculated, withdrawal was domestic vs. international, etc.).\\n\\n## Requesting a review or dispute\\n- Contact us as soon as you notice the charge.\\n- Include: account name, last 4 digits, statement period, fee date/amount/description, and your supporting screenshots or documents.\\n- We will investigate and correct any misapplied fees. If additional information is needed (e.g., to verify ATM location or wire authorization), we will follow up.\\n\\n5. Internal: Opening Personal Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_001\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nTo open a personal checking account, ensure all of the following are true:\\n1. The customer is verified.\\n2. The customer is at least 18 years old.\\n3. The customer does not exceed 4 personal checking accounts.\\n4. The customer has no checking accounts closed for cause in the past 6 months.\\n\\n## Opening Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify customer identity.\\n2. Check eligibility requirements listed above.\\n3. Confirm the customer's desired account_class selection.\\n   - Personal checking account_class options must use the full official name ending with 'Account' (e.g., 'Blue Account', 'Green Account (checking)').\\n4. Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account.\\n\\n6. Internal: Opening Personal Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_002\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Scope and Focus\\n\\nProcedure for opening personal savings accounts. Eligibility requirements: 1) Customer must be verified, 2) Customer must already have at least one active Rho-Bank checking account, 3) Cannot have more than 5 personal savings accounts, 4) Must not have any accounts in collections or with negative balances, 5) Must have held their checking account for at least 14 days. Steps: 1) Verify customer identity, 2) Check eligibility requirements, 3) Confirm account selection with customer, 4) Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account (note: account_class must use the full official name ending with 'Account', e.g., 'Silver Plus Account', 'Gold Account'), 5) Ask the customer if they would like you to transfer the opening deposit from their checking account now. If yes, use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount. If no, inform them they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Eligibility Requirements (Internal Checklist)\\n\\nConfirm all of the following before proceeding:\\n- Customer identity is verified in our systems.\\n- Customer has at least one active Rho-Bank checking account.\\n- Customer currently holds fewer than 5 personal savings accounts.\\n- Customer has no accounts in collections and no negative balances.\\n- The customer’s checking account tenure is at least 14 days.\\n\\nDo not proceed if any item above is not met.\\n\\n## Step-by-Step Procedure\\n\\n1) Verify identity\\n- Authenticate the customer and confirm identity verification status on file.\\n\\n2) Check eligibility\\n- Confirm an active checking account exists and meets the 14-day tenure requirement.\\n- Count existing personal savings accounts; ensure the customer is below the 5 limit.\\n- Review account status; there must be no collections activity and no negative balances.\\n\\n3) Confirm account selection\\n- Discuss available personal savings account options with the customer.\\n- Capture the exact account_class string. It must be the full official name ending with “Account” (for example, “Silver Plus Account”, “Gold Account”).\\n\\n4) Open the savings account (agent action)\\n- Use the open_bank_account_4821 tool with account_type set to 'savings' and the confirmed account_class.\\n\\n5) Arrange opening deposit\\n- Ask the customer if they want you to transfer the opening deposit from their checking account now.\\n  - If yes: use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount from the customer’s checking account to the newly opened savings account.\\n  - If no: inform the customer they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n6) Confirm completion\\n- Provide the new account details and confirm the funding status or the funding deadline.\\n\\n## Agent Tool Usage (Internal Only)\\n\\nThe AGENT calls these tools directly to perform actions on behalf of the customer. Do not ask the customer to call tools or provide tool parameters.\\n\\n- Tool: open_bank_account_4821(user_id, account_type, account_class)\\n  - When to call: After steps 1–3, once eligibility is confirmed and the customer has selected an account_class.\\n  - How to set parameters:\\n    - user_id: the authenticated customer’s user identifier.\\n    - account_type: 'savings' for personal savings accounts.\\n    - account_class: the full official account name ending with 'Account' exactly as confirmed with the customer.\\n  - Expected outcome: Creates a new personal savings account for the customer.\\n\\n- Tool: transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291(source_account_id, destination_account_id, amount)\\n  - When to call: In step 5, only if the customer authorizes an immediate transfer for the opening deposit.\\n  - How to set parameters:\\n    - source_account_id: the customer's Rho-Bank checking account to be debited.\\n    - destination_account_id: the newly opened personal savings account to be credited.\\n    - amount: the required opening deposit amount confirmed with the customer.\\n  - Expected outcome: Moves funds from checking to savings to complete the opening deposit.\\n\\n## Decision Points and Handling\\n\\n- Exceeds savings account limit: If the customer already has 5 personal savings accounts, do not open a new one. Inform the customer they have reached the maximum.\\n- Insufficient checking tenure: If the checking account has been open fewer than 14 days, advise the customer when they will become eligible.\\n- Collections or negative balances: Resolve these issues first; do not proceed until all accounts are in good standing.\\n- Customer defers funding: Clearly communicate the 30-day funding window and the consequence of closure if unfunded. Document the acknowledgment in the interaction notes.\\n\\n7. Internal: Opening Business Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_004\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Description\\n\\nProcedure for opening business savings accounts. Eligibility requirements: 1) Customer must be verified, 2) Customer must already have at least one business checking account with status OPEN, 3) Customer cannot have more than 4 business savings accounts, 4) Customer must not have any accounts with negative balances, 5) Existing business checking account must have been open for at least 30 days, 6) Existing business checking account must have a balance of at least $2,500. Steps: 1) Verify customer identity, 2) Check eligibility requirements, 3) Confirm account selection with customer (business savings account_class options include Bronze Saver Account, Silver Saver Account, etc.), 4) Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account, 5) Ask the customer if they would like you to transfer the opening deposit from their business checking account now. If yes, use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount. If no, inform them they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nConfirm all of the following before proceeding:\\n- Customer identity is verified.\\n- Customer has at least one business checking account with status OPEN.\\n- Customer has fewer than 4 existing business savings accounts.\\n- Customer has no accounts with negative balances.\\n- At least one existing business checking account has been open for at least 30 days.\\n- That business checking account has a current balance of at least $2,500.\\n\\nNotes:\\n- Use the qualifying OPEN business checking account that meets both the tenure and balance thresholds as the source for the optional opening deposit transfer.\\n\\n## Step-by-Step Procedure\\n\\n1) Verify customer identity.\\n2) Check eligibility requirements (see list above).\\n3) Confirm account selection with the customer:\\n   - Ask for the desired business savings account_class (e.g., Bronze Saver Account, Silver Saver Account, etc.).\\n   - Ensure you capture the exact official account_class name ending with “Account.”\\n4) Open the new business savings account using the agent tool (see Tool Instructions below).\\n5) Funding the opening deposit:\\n   - Ask the customer if they want you to transfer the opening deposit now from their eligible business checking account.\\n   - If yes: initiate the internal transfer using the agent tool (see Tool Instructions below).\\n   - If no: inform the customer they have 30 days to fund the account via internal transfer or external deposit; otherwise, the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Agent Tool Instructions\\n\\nThe AGENT calls these tools directly to perform actions on behalf of the customer. Do not expose tool details to the customer.\\n\\n### Tool: open_bank_account_4821\\n\\n- Signature:\\n  - open_bank_account_4821(user_id, account_type, account_class)\\n- When to call:\\n  - After eligibility is confirmed and the customer has selected the desired business savings account_class.\\n- How to call:\\n  - Set account_type to 'savings'.\\n  - Set account_class to the exact official name provided by the customer (e.g., 'Bronze Saver Account').\\n- Expected outcome:\\n  - Returns a new savings account record (capture the new account_id for subsequent actions).\\n\\n### Tool: transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291\\n\\n- Signature:\\n  - transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291(source_account_id, destination_account_id, amount)\\n- When to call:\\n  - Only if the customer authorizes transferring the opening deposit now.\\n- How to call:\\n  - source_account_id: the qualifying OPEN business checking account that meets the 30-day tenure and $2,500 balance requirements.\\n  - destination_account_id: the newly opened business savings account_id.\\n  - amount: the required opening deposit amount confirmed with the customer.\\n- If the transfer fails (e.g., insufficient funds):\\n  - Inform the customer and remind them they have 30 days to fund the account via internal transfer or external deposit, or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Checklist Before Opening\\n\\n- Customer identity verified.\\n- OPEN business checking account identified and qualified (≥ 30 days open and ≥ $2,500 balance).\\n- Savings account count confirmed is < 4.\\n- No negative balances across any accounts.\\n- Customer-confirmed account_class captured exactly.\\n\\n## Post-Opening Actions\\n\\n- If the customer funds now: complete the transfer and confirm success.\\n- If the customer defers funding: clearly communicate the 30-day deadline and acceptable methods (internal transfer or external deposit), and note that the account will be closed if not funded within that timeframe.\\n\\n8. Internal: Closing Personal Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_005\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Light Blue Account, Light Green Account, Green Fee-Free Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $15 if closed within 30 days\\n  - Notice period: 0 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (Blue Account, Green Account (checking))\\n  - Early closure fee: $25 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 3 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Evergreen Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $50 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 7 days\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (Bluest Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $100 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 14 days\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n9. Internal: Closing Personal Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_006\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Bronze Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $20 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 1 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (Silver Account, Silver Plus Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $35 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 5 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Gold Account, Gold Plus Account, Gold Years Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $75 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 10 days\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (Platinum Account, Platinum Plus Account, Diamond Elite Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $150 if closed within 270 days\\n  - Notice period: 21 days\\n  - Requires manager approval\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. For ELITE tier, obtain manager approval before proceeding.\\n4. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n10. Internal: Closing Business Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_007\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n- Customer has no linked business savings accounts that are still OPEN (close those first)\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Navy Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $50 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 7 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (True Blue, Sky Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $100 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 14 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Cobalt Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $200 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 21 days\\n  - Requires supervisor review\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (accounts with credit lines over $100,000)\\n  - Early closure fee: $400 if closed within 270 days\\n  - Notice period: 30 days\\n  - Requires manager approval\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. For PREMIUM tier, obtain supervisor review. For ELITE tier, obtain manager approval.\\n4. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=0ms, reranking=0ms, total=0ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_pCh66qo9H87NNF45iAXFDcIu\",\"output\":\"1. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_013\\n   Score: 8.4624\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Sky Blue account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Lime Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Sky Blue nor Lime Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our startup and premium business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n2. Internal: Closing Business Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_007\\n   Score: 5.0004\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n- Customer has no linked business savings accounts that are still OPEN (close those first)\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Navy Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $50 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 7 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (True Blue, Sky Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $100 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 14 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Cobalt Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $200 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 21 days\\n  - Requires supervisor review\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (accounts with credit lines over $100,000)\\n  - Early closure fee: $400 if closed within 270 days\\n  - Notice period: 30 days\\n  - Requires manager approval\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. For PREMIUM tier, obtain supervisor review. For ELITE tier, obtain manager approval.\\n4. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n3. Getting Started with Sky Blue: Startup Account Setup\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_sky_blue_001\\n   Score: 4.9446\\n   Content: ## Verify Eligibility\\n- Confirm your company is within 4 years of formation.\\n- Check whether you meet the funding requirement: 0.\\n\\n## Understand Key Cost Terms Before You Apply\\n- Your startup receives a free period of 6 months.\\n- After the free period, the monthly maintenance fee is $25.00.\\n- If your balance goes negative, the overdraft fee is $0.00.\\n\\n## Prepare Your Application\\n- Gather company formation documents and ownership details.\\n- Be ready to provide basic business information and authorized signers.\\n- Plan initial account settings, such as user permissions and card controls, so you can activate quickly after approval.\\n\\n## Submit and Configure\\n- Complete the online application and upload requested documents.\\n- After approval, log in to set user roles, spending controls, and alerts.\\n- Link external accounts to enable seamless transfers.\\n\\n## Startup Referral Program\\nHelp other startups get started with Sky Blue:\\n- Your bonus: $150 for each successful referral\\n- Their bonus: $250 welcome bonus\\n- Annual limit: 8 referrals per year\\n\\n## First-Funding and Go-Live Checklist\\n- Make an initial deposit from a linked account.\\n- Confirm your free period of 6 months is visible in your billing section.\\n- Review your fee settings to ensure you understand the transition to $25.00 and the overdraft policy of $0.00.\\n\\n4. Internal: Opening Personal Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_001\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nTo open a personal checking account, ensure all of the following are true:\\n1. The customer is verified.\\n2. The customer is at least 18 years old.\\n3. The customer does not exceed 4 personal checking accounts.\\n4. The customer has no checking accounts closed for cause in the past 6 months.\\n\\n## Opening Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify customer identity.\\n2. Check eligibility requirements listed above.\\n3. Confirm the customer's desired account_class selection.\\n   - Personal checking account_class options must use the full official name ending with 'Account' (e.g., 'Blue Account', 'Green Account (checking)').\\n4. Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account.\\n\\n5. Internal: Opening Personal Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_002\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Scope and Focus\\n\\nProcedure for opening personal savings accounts. Eligibility requirements: 1) Customer must be verified, 2) Customer must already have at least one active Rho-Bank checking account, 3) Cannot have more than 5 personal savings accounts, 4) Must not have any accounts in collections or with negative balances, 5) Must have held their checking account for at least 14 days. Steps: 1) Verify customer identity, 2) Check eligibility requirements, 3) Confirm account selection with customer, 4) Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account (note: account_class must use the full official name ending with 'Account', e.g., 'Silver Plus Account', 'Gold Account'), 5) Ask the customer if they would like you to transfer the opening deposit from their checking account now. If yes, use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount. If no, inform them they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Eligibility Requirements (Internal Checklist)\\n\\nConfirm all of the following before proceeding:\\n- Customer identity is verified in our systems.\\n- Customer has at least one active Rho-Bank checking account.\\n- Customer currently holds fewer than 5 personal savings accounts.\\n- Customer has no accounts in collections and no negative balances.\\n- The customer’s checking account tenure is at least 14 days.\\n\\nDo not proceed if any item above is not met.\\n\\n## Step-by-Step Procedure\\n\\n1) Verify identity\\n- Authenticate the customer and confirm identity verification status on file.\\n\\n2) Check eligibility\\n- Confirm an active checking account exists and meets the 14-day tenure requirement.\\n- Count existing personal savings accounts; ensure the customer is below the 5 limit.\\n- Review account status; there must be no collections activity and no negative balances.\\n\\n3) Confirm account selection\\n- Discuss available personal savings account options with the customer.\\n- Capture the exact account_class string. It must be the full official name ending with “Account” (for example, “Silver Plus Account”, “Gold Account”).\\n\\n4) Open the savings account (agent action)\\n- Use the open_bank_account_4821 tool with account_type set to 'savings' and the confirmed account_class.\\n\\n5) Arrange opening deposit\\n- Ask the customer if they want you to transfer the opening deposit from their checking account now.\\n  - If yes: use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount from the customer’s checking account to the newly opened savings account.\\n  - If no: inform the customer they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n6) Confirm completion\\n- Provide the new account details and confirm the funding status or the funding deadline.\\n\\n## Agent Tool Usage (Internal Only)\\n\\nThe AGENT calls these tools directly to perform actions on behalf of the customer. Do not ask the customer to call tools or provide tool parameters.\\n\\n- Tool: open_bank_account_4821(user_id, account_type, account_class)\\n  - When to call: After steps 1–3, once eligibility is confirmed and the customer has selected an account_class.\\n  - How to set parameters:\\n    - user_id: the authenticated customer’s user identifier.\\n    - account_type: 'savings' for personal savings accounts.\\n    - account_class: the full official account name ending with 'Account' exactly as confirmed with the customer.\\n  - Expected outcome: Creates a new personal savings account for the customer.\\n\\n- Tool: transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291(source_account_id, destination_account_id, amount)\\n  - When to call: In step 5, only if the customer authorizes an immediate transfer for the opening deposit.\\n  - How to set parameters:\\n    - source_account_id: the customer's Rho-Bank checking account to be debited.\\n    - destination_account_id: the newly opened personal savings account to be credited.\\n    - amount: the required opening deposit amount confirmed with the customer.\\n  - Expected outcome: Moves funds from checking to savings to complete the opening deposit.\\n\\n## Decision Points and Handling\\n\\n- Exceeds savings account limit: If the customer already has 5 personal savings accounts, do not open a new one. Inform the customer they have reached the maximum.\\n- Insufficient checking tenure: If the checking account has been open fewer than 14 days, advise the customer when they will become eligible.\\n- Collections or negative balances: Resolve these issues first; do not proceed until all accounts are in good standing.\\n- Customer defers funding: Clearly communicate the 30-day funding window and the consequence of closure if unfunded. Document the acknowledgment in the interaction notes.\\n\\n6. Internal: Opening Business Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_003\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nTo open a business checking account, ensure all of the following are true:\\n1. The customer is verified.\\n2. The customer has at least one existing personal checking account with status OPEN.\\n3. The customer does not exceed 6 business checking accounts.\\n4. The customer has no accounts with status CLOSED.\\n5. The customer's existing checking account has a balance of at least $500.\\n\\n## Opening Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify customer identity.\\n2. Check eligibility requirements listed above.\\n3. Confirm the customer's desired account_class selection.\\n   - Business checking account_class options include Navy Blue, Cobalt Blue, True Blue, etc.\\n4. Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account.\\n\\n7. Internal: Opening Business Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_004\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Description\\n\\nProcedure for opening business savings accounts. Eligibility requirements: 1) Customer must be verified, 2) Customer must already have at least one business checking account with status OPEN, 3) Customer cannot have more than 4 business savings accounts, 4) Customer must not have any accounts with negative balances, 5) Existing business checking account must have been open for at least 30 days, 6) Existing business checking account must have a balance of at least $2,500. Steps: 1) Verify customer identity, 2) Check eligibility requirements, 3) Confirm account selection with customer (business savings account_class options include Bronze Saver Account, Silver Saver Account, etc.), 4) Use open_bank_account_4821 to open the account, 5) Ask the customer if they would like you to transfer the opening deposit from their business checking account now. If yes, use transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291 to transfer the required amount. If no, inform them they have 30 days to fund the account (via internal transfer or external deposit) or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Eligibility Requirements\\n\\nConfirm all of the following before proceeding:\\n- Customer identity is verified.\\n- Customer has at least one business checking account with status OPEN.\\n- Customer has fewer than 4 existing business savings accounts.\\n- Customer has no accounts with negative balances.\\n- At least one existing business checking account has been open for at least 30 days.\\n- That business checking account has a current balance of at least $2,500.\\n\\nNotes:\\n- Use the qualifying OPEN business checking account that meets both the tenure and balance thresholds as the source for the optional opening deposit transfer.\\n\\n## Step-by-Step Procedure\\n\\n1) Verify customer identity.\\n2) Check eligibility requirements (see list above).\\n3) Confirm account selection with the customer:\\n   - Ask for the desired business savings account_class (e.g., Bronze Saver Account, Silver Saver Account, etc.).\\n   - Ensure you capture the exact official account_class name ending with “Account.”\\n4) Open the new business savings account using the agent tool (see Tool Instructions below).\\n5) Funding the opening deposit:\\n   - Ask the customer if they want you to transfer the opening deposit now from their eligible business checking account.\\n   - If yes: initiate the internal transfer using the agent tool (see Tool Instructions below).\\n   - If no: inform the customer they have 30 days to fund the account via internal transfer or external deposit; otherwise, the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Agent Tool Instructions\\n\\nThe AGENT calls these tools directly to perform actions on behalf of the customer. Do not expose tool details to the customer.\\n\\n### Tool: open_bank_account_4821\\n\\n- Signature:\\n  - open_bank_account_4821(user_id, account_type, account_class)\\n- When to call:\\n  - After eligibility is confirmed and the customer has selected the desired business savings account_class.\\n- How to call:\\n  - Set account_type to 'savings'.\\n  - Set account_class to the exact official name provided by the customer (e.g., 'Bronze Saver Account').\\n- Expected outcome:\\n  - Returns a new savings account record (capture the new account_id for subsequent actions).\\n\\n### Tool: transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291\\n\\n- Signature:\\n  - transfer_funds_between_bank_accounts_7291(source_account_id, destination_account_id, amount)\\n- When to call:\\n  - Only if the customer authorizes transferring the opening deposit now.\\n- How to call:\\n  - source_account_id: the qualifying OPEN business checking account that meets the 30-day tenure and $2,500 balance requirements.\\n  - destination_account_id: the newly opened business savings account_id.\\n  - amount: the required opening deposit amount confirmed with the customer.\\n- If the transfer fails (e.g., insufficient funds):\\n  - Inform the customer and remind them they have 30 days to fund the account via internal transfer or external deposit, or the account will be closed.\\n\\n## Checklist Before Opening\\n\\n- Customer identity verified.\\n- OPEN business checking account identified and qualified (≥ 30 days open and ≥ $2,500 balance).\\n- Savings account count confirmed is < 4.\\n- No negative balances across any accounts.\\n- Customer-confirmed account_class captured exactly.\\n\\n## Post-Opening Actions\\n\\n- If the customer funds now: complete the transfer and confirm success.\\n- If the customer defers funding: clearly communicate the 30-day deadline and acceptable methods (internal transfer or external deposit), and note that the account will be closed if not funded within that timeframe.\\n\\n8. Internal: Closing Personal Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_005\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Light Blue Account, Light Green Account, Green Fee-Free Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $15 if closed within 30 days\\n  - Notice period: 0 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (Blue Account, Green Account (checking))\\n  - Early closure fee: $25 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 3 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Evergreen Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $50 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 7 days\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (Bluest Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $100 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 14 days\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n9. Internal: Closing Personal Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_006\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Bronze Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $20 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 1 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (Silver Account, Silver Plus Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $35 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 5 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Gold Account, Gold Plus Account, Gold Years Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $75 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 10 days\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (Platinum Account, Platinum Plus Account, Diamond Elite Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $150 if closed within 270 days\\n  - Notice period: 21 days\\n  - Requires manager approval\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. For ELITE tier, obtain manager approval before proceeding.\\n4. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n10. Internal: Closing Business Savings Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_008\\n   Score: 0.0000\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n- Customer must have at least one active business checking account remaining (business savings requires a linked business checking account)\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Bronze Saver Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $75 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 10 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (Silver Saver Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $125 if closed within 120 days\\n  - Notice period: 14 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Gold Saver Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $250 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 21 days\\n  - Requires supervisor review\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (Platinum Reserve Account)\\n  - Early closure fee: $500 if closed within 270 days\\n  - Notice period: 30 days\\n  - Requires manager approval\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. For PREMIUM tier, obtain supervisor review. For ELITE tier, obtain manager approval.\\n4. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=0ms, reranking=0ms, total=0ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqvEdGN8AqRXOS0CFTE8LyeVwbr6w_n_3FkFXuVyZ0wtyHos_I6qgKJyUXfnrKBh8jhS8XlZso9JJRkV04dpF-l-DbpPrS9we5MFEEry2CtAWuFjNGiaR5rUF4Pwsmj7CJ3DE14-eofLGDwzbs1eA-CiWoKkRyaCw-FNwZy1R0_H_wgtK6AbrWoWjiPCm_Twp9kVSbrk8O7H9CWOjkJGu-xe11evq-vjZmLI0Blp-xBBU9VWUtAw4r6Ba18_DWTVHqrcVamXXMYK-OfPqkKG4nNzB9_x38qZyyXpkBPGYe-FqUB83LNKywW74TbW_laHRJu-zPkudJ85B40nAOS6HSRLBp-b28nmkTRjdkw0s1rKOFOAWV_Hf3puIPtGYcTPs7Bo__7BQuPfeoS5fa7WMCCvwnuIDTWt7Q0P6fH7KLeCrCbV8L3Aw6UjHdQLY9wFwHnv7vuTL-paiTwWJvyBseltTEE9KiCnV8xav6s1luD7lVuiPlH_vGXhJ9_WkPUV4HGhMX6FMU4GyvMrfZe3h3P1egZuEZCippdbHkO-8V9SRi8Uez9zcwAVZsfswit72JfNMN7JgWuCS3KMBVGIOcL2Um-NbPPylIP_9cqvNOm-63iFrNiHVSd31vlRKO_TACOKcIKXkdZvdJ_1UQmFLNAyPpPoZNAOH4hpSk5PfFjjYo4L9vgaF8l1E-sDPuvtIpAcr8FirCLgkYVUXfNfc1s1TOvhqvAWp2OUSY5rmIX7zSLLwk4k4RxtpA8TPV5vlkdQvZgpedDwk0PLRNZosTG8OdJ9Ig54gysIIujo9clSfR7MdGTkEu2iEXN94DxRwHVnvLQ--3Jvrw_6RumAg17_XCxJmItVQ-9hSVBb3C1bTOGL8BEHm7jhONiDLNV_kroTHhmOwPyht-nDE-arr19lWHa1rY55zH47iNdbLwNQGymfLlgyRMZvUNpV_5r_f5buVe8C9z6PCu3tYtAB2HvNwgb1kyOIOLazKUHQ768R1lXi2QKGPlSl8yjSVb8SiveHBFssQF856wIjNJhsVfMsVgYH1IWye0FGyyZh8tmOyDw-jEVAUvPEKZ097jsyZxZbUwP9A3D4PotkIZC64kAIpI4xYE7h19WL-GjLvRAa4Y414UlPzOwHI01YWAB04A2znyc_UAMmUy_LKyitBcGdi3YLPBmwG5NhWJEIRoOlBAh5o6k8Eb7GI1ZZ1DPzUZJLd70UgrTx63IV3bKFQe8rMIxcCenjn4bhYayU1yoA1oLsk9IJ3NCHoUXUTZGI9uBOgG1JZgtZ0v8RXBx3yp45fU_FIKcCMmzpqfrG7YD7j2EVMcBtVaY8U8fR2FrSz5mwcQeU6GSyINsOcMfR5V8oKpTZ-aCHlbpN8wgCOfNV4OJgM=\",\"id\":\"rs_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc4743fc3087d18c1a86d484966719\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Searching for documents**\\n\\nI need to look for the Cobalt ATM rebate documents using the exact query \\\"Cobalt Blue ATM rebates.\\\" It seems that BM25 might not find the title contents or the specific text if it doesn't include \\\"cobalt\\\" in the correct format. I should be careful about how I structure my search to ensure I locate the right documents. I'll focus on those key terms for a more effective query.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Cobalt ATM rebates\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_OZW0kJrphgt6taJUKDodvTYN\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc4745f1bc87d188d7c7bfdf89af4d\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Sky waiver\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_ddaD6GsH8ZN3AR96uT1ttoQx\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc4745f1c887d1bab010b8db299729\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"arguments\":\"{\\\"query\\\":\\\"Cobalt overdraft protection\\\"}\",\"call_id\":\"call_636PhHcmUVnvIeF8373AokCV\",\"id\":\"fc_07c7d4b1f89c4c20016abc4745f1d487d18ca4fc781de8cb19\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"type\":\"function_call\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_OZW0kJrphgt6taJUKDodvTYN\",\"output\":\"1. Silver Plus: ATM fee rebate program\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_silver_plus_account_003\\n   Score: 10.7687\\n   Content: ## Monthly rebate allowance\\n- You are eligible for ATM fee rebates up to 25 per month.\\n\\n### How rebates apply\\n- Rebates are intended to offset ATM operator surcharges incurred on eligible ATM cash withdrawals.\\n- Once your monthly rebate total reaches 25, additional ATM fees will not be rebated for that month.\\n\\n### Important distinctions\\n- The ATM fee rebates are separate from any excess withdrawal charges. If you exceed your monthly free withdrawal limit, an excess withdrawal fee of $1.00 per additional withdrawal may apply.\\n\\n### Tips for maximizing rebates\\n- Use ATMs as needed and track your cumulative rebates so you stay within the 25 monthly allowance.\\n- Keep your withdrawal count in mind to avoid the separate excess withdrawal fee of $1.00 when you pass the free limit.\\n\\n2. ATM fee rebates for Bluest\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_bluest_account_007\\n   Score: 10.6278\\n   Content: ## Daily ATM withdrawal limit\\n- Your Bluest Account debit card has a daily ATM withdrawal limit of $1,500. This applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n## Monthly rebate cap\\n- You are eligible for ATM fee rebates up to $50 per month.\\n\\n### How rebates are applied\\n- Rebates are credited until you reach the monthly maximum of $50.\\n- If your aggregate ATM fees exceed $50 in a given month, the excess will not be rebated.\\n\\n### Tips for maximizing rebates\\n- Keep track of your cumulative ATM fees during the month to stay within the $50 cap.\\n- Consider using fee-free ATMs once you approach the monthly cap.\\n\\n3. Using ATMs worldwide\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_purple_account_004\\n   Score: 10.0793\\n   Content: ## Daily ATM withdrawal limit\\n- Your Purple Account debit card has a daily ATM withdrawal limit of $1,000. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals worldwide within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n## How ATM rebates work\\n- You are eligible for refunds of ATM operator fees up to a monthly cap of $30.\\n- Rebates apply after eligible ATM fees post to your account and are credited up to the monthly cap.\\n\\n## Best practices when withdrawing cash abroad\\n- Choose the checking account option on the ATM when prompted.\\n- Retain the ATM receipt if it shows a surcharge to help with any rebate review.\\n- Avoid optional dynamic currency conversion at the ATM if you prefer to be billed in the local currency.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n- If you believe a rebate is missing, verify whether your monthly total rebates have reached $30 and confirm that the charge was coded as an ATM operator fee.\\n\\n4. Cobalt Blue Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_010\\n   Score: 9.9755\\n   Content: ## Summary of ATM Fees\\n\\n- Domestic out-of-network ATM withdrawal: $2.00 per transaction\\n- International ATM withdrawal: 2.5% of the withdrawal amount (minimum $4.00 per transaction)\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates: Up to $15 in out-of-network ATM fee rebates per month\\n\\nNote: ATM owners/operators may charge additional surcharges that you will see at the terminal before you complete the transaction.\\n\\n## Domestic Out-of-Network ATM Usage\\n\\nWhen you use an ATM outside the in-network system within the United States:\\n- You are charged $2.00 per withdrawal.\\n- Some ATM owners add their own surcharge. You can choose to cancel the transaction if you do not want to accept an operator surcharge.\\n- You can receive up to $15 in ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network usage. These rebates can offset qualifying out-of-network ATM fees you incur, up to the monthly cap.\\n\\nTips to minimize domestic fees:\\n- Combine cash needs into fewer withdrawals to reduce per-transaction fees.\\n- Check the ATM’s on-screen disclosure for any operator surcharges before accepting.\\n\\n## International ATM Withdrawals\\n\\nFor withdrawals at foreign (international) ATMs:\\n- You are charged 2.5% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $4.00 per transaction.\\n- Local ATM owners may add their own surcharges at the terminal.\\n- Exchange rates and any third-party conversion choices at the ATM can affect your total cost.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- Withdraw $200: 2.5% of $200 = $5.00; the fee is $5.00 (exceeds the $4.00 minimum).\\n- Withdraw $100: 2.5% of $100 = $2.50; the $4.00 minimum applies, so the fee is $4.00.\\n\\n## Monthly ATM Fee Rebates\\n\\n- You can receive up to $15 in ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network ATM usage.\\n- The rebate limit applies on a monthly basis; once you reach $15, additional out-of-network ATM fees will not be rebated that month.\\n\\nExample:\\n- If you make two domestic out-of-network withdrawals, your bank-assessed fees would be 2 × $2.00. Up to $15 of qualifying out-of-network ATM fees may be rebated that month.\\n\\n5. Beige Account: Enterprise ATM Benefits\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_beige_011\\n   Score: 9.8490\\n   Content: ## What’s included with Enterprise ATM access\\n\\n- No Rho out-of-network ATM fee: You pay $0.00 per out-of-network ATM transaction.\\n- Monthly rebates for ATM operator surcharges: Receive up to $50 in rebates each month for fees charged by out-of-network ATM operators.\\n- International ATM withdrawals: A Rho fee of 1% of the withdrawal amount applies at foreign ATMs, with a minimum charge of $2.00 per withdrawal.\\n\\n## Fee summary\\n\\n| Scenario | Rho fee | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Out-of-network ATM usage (Rho fee) | $0.00 per transaction | ATM operators may charge their own surcharges. |\\n| Rebates for out-of-network ATM operator surcharges | Up to $50 per month | Rebates are capped monthly; once reached, additional surcharges are your responsibility. |\\n| Foreign (international) ATM withdrawal | 1% of withdrawal amount, minimum $2.00 | This Rho fee may apply in addition to any ATM operator surcharge. |\\n\\n## Examples\\n\\n- Domestic, out-of-network ATM\\n  - You withdraw $200 and the ATM operator charges a $3 surcharge.\\n  - Rho out-of-network fee: $0.00.\\n  - The $3 operator surcharge counts toward your monthly rebate limit of $50.\\n\\n- Foreign ATM withdrawal\\n  - You withdraw $400 abroad.\\n  - Rho foreign ATM fee: 1% of $400 = $4.00 (meets the $2.00 minimum).\\n  - If the ATM operator adds its own surcharge, it may count toward your monthly rebate limit of $50 for out-of-network usage.\\n\\n## How to maximize your benefits\\n\\n- Consolidate cash needs into fewer withdrawals to reduce multiple operator surcharges.\\n- Track your cumulative ATM operator-fee rebates against the $50 monthly cap.\\n- When traveling internationally, factor in the 1% (minimum $2.00) fee on each withdrawal.\\n\\n## FAQs\\n\\n- Is there a Rho fee for using an out-of-network ATM?\\n  - No. The Rho fee is $0.00 per transaction. ATM operators may still charge their own surcharges.\\n\\n- What happens after I reach the monthly rebate cap?\\n  - Once you reach $50 in rebated out-of-network ATM surcharges for the month, additional surcharges are not rebated.\\n\\n- Do foreign ATM withdrawals have a separate fee?\\n  - Yes. Each foreign ATM withdrawal incurs a Rho fee of 1% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $2.00 per withdrawal.\\n\\n6. Navy Blue Account: Mobile Deposits and Daily Limits\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_navy_blue_005\\n   Score: 9.5441\\n   Content: ## Mobile check deposits\\n- Daily mobile deposit limit: $5,000\\n- Endorse checks according to the app instructions and submit clear images to avoid delays.\\n\\n## Digital transfer limits\\n- Daily digital transfer limit: $25,000\\n- If your planned transfer exceeds $25,000, schedule it in multiple submissions across business days.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n- Monthly cap on ATM fee rebates for out-of-network usage: 10\\n- Rebates are applied to qualifying ATM surcharge amounts up to the monthly cap.\\n\\n## Best practices\\n- Deposit earlier in the business day to allow for review and availability under standard timelines.\\n- Retain original checks until you confirm the deposit has posted.\\n- Plan outgoing transfers with the daily ceiling of $25,000 in mind.\\n\\n7. Mobile Deposits and ATM Access on Cobalt Blue\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_cobalt_blue_006\\n   Score: 9.3957\\n   Content: ## Mobile check deposits\\n- Daily mobile deposit limit: $10,000\\n- Endorse checks and include any required mobile deposit notation before capture\\n- Submit clear images in good lighting and verify amounts before sending\\n- Keep checks secure until you confirm the deposit has been accepted and posted\\n\\n## Tips to stay within limits\\n- If you reach the daily limit of $10,000, wait for the next day’s cycle before depositing additional checks\\n- Combine smaller checks into a single day’s batch when possible, up to the limit\\n\\n## ATM access and rebates\\n- You receive up to 15 per month in rebates for fees charged by out-of-network ATMs\\n- Rebates are applied after the ATM operator’s fee posts to your account\\n- Keep ATM receipts until you see the rebate appear in your activity\\n\\n## Best practices\\n- Use in-network ATMs when available; rely on rebates up to 15 when you must use out-of-network machines\\n- Monitor your monthly rebate tally to understand remaining rebate capacity\\n\\n8. True Blue Account: ATM Fees and Out-of-Network Usage\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_true_blue_011\\n   Score: 9.3782\\n   Content: ## Fees at a glance\\n\\n| Transaction type | Where it applies | Fee |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal | Domestic (U.S.) non-Rho ATMs | $1.00 per transaction |\\n| Foreign ATM cash withdrawal | International ATMs | 2% of the withdrawal amount; minimum $3.00 per withdrawal |\\n| Monthly ATM fee rebates (cap) | Out-of-network ATM usage | Up to $30 per month |\\n\\nNote: ATM owners may assess their own surcharges on out-of-network transactions. Those surcharges are separate from Rho’s fees.\\n\\n## Domestic out-of-network ATM usage (U.S.)\\n\\n- When you use a non-Rho ATM domestically, you are charged $1.00 per transaction.\\n- The ATM owner may also charge a separate surcharge at the terminal; you can accept or cancel the transaction after the surcharge is disclosed.\\n\\nExample:\\n- If you complete 5 out-of-network withdrawals in a month, Rho’s fees would total 5 × $1.00. Any ATM owner surcharges would be in addition to this amount.\\n\\n## International ATM withdrawals\\n\\n- For cash withdrawals at foreign (international) ATMs, the fee is 2% of the withdrawal amount, with a minimum of $3.00 per withdrawal.\\n- The percentage is applied to each withdrawal; if the calculated amount is below $3.00, the minimum applies.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- $100 withdrawal: 2% = $2.00, which is below the $3.00 minimum, so the fee is $3.00.\\n- $200 withdrawal: 2% = $4.00, so the fee is $4.00.\\n\\n## Monthly ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You can receive up to $30 in ATM fee rebates per month for out-of-network ATM usage.\\n- The cap is applied on a monthly basis; once total eligible ATM fees reach $30 for the month, no additional ATM fee rebates are provided for that month.\\n\\nExamples:\\n- If your monthly out-of-network ATM fees total $12, up to $12 may be rebated (within the $30 cap).\\n- If your monthly out-of-network ATM fees total $36, the maximum rebate is $30.\\n\\n## Tips to manage costs\\n\\n- Prefer Rho ATMs to avoid the $1.00 out-of-network fee.\\n- Abroad, consider fewer, larger withdrawals to reduce the impact of the $3.00 per-withdrawal minimum.\\n- Track your monthly ATM fees so you know when you are approaching the $30 cap.\\n\\n9. Mobile Banking and Deposits on Sky Blue\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_sky_blue_007\\n   Score: 9.0323\\n   Content: ## Mobile Check Deposits\\n- Your daily mobile deposit limit is $25,000.\\n- Endorse the check, capture clear images, and submit through the mobile app.\\n- Monitor deposit status in your deposit history and retain the check until confirmation.\\n\\n## Interest on Balances\\n- Your account earns an APY of 1.25%.\\n- Interest is compounded daily.\\n\\n## ATM Access and Rebates\\n- Out-of-network ATM fees are rebated up to 15 per month.\\n- Keep ATM receipts and review posted rebates in your statements.\\n\\n## Best Practices\\n- Use well-lit photos for deposits and avoid folded or damaged checks.\\n- Set balance and deposit alerts to track funds availability and interest accrual.\\n\\n10. Green Account (savings): EcoCard holder exclusive benefits\\n   ID: doc_savings_accounts_green_account_(savings)_009\\n   Score: 8.8758\\n   Content: ## EcoCard holder benefits overview\\n\\nGreen Account (savings) holders who also have an EcoCard receive enhanced benefits that make eco-conscious banking even more rewarding. Your monthly withdrawal limit is increased by 7 additional free withdrawals, bringing your total to 8 + 7 = 15 withdrawals per month. You also receive 20 in ATM fee rebates monthly. Combined with the existing 0.5% bonus APY for EcoCard holders on top of the base 4.0% rate, this creates a comprehensive eco-friendly savings experience with maximum flexibility.\\n\\n## What you get as an EcoCard holder\\n\\n- Increased monthly free withdrawals: 8 + 7 = 15 total free withdrawals per month\\n- ATM fee rebates: up to $20 in rebates each month\\n- Rate boost: 0.5% bonus APY on top of the base 4.0% rate (example total: 4.75%)\\n\\n## Increased free withdrawals\\n\\n- Your free withdrawal allowance increases by 7 each month, for a total of 15 free withdrawals.\\n- Examples:\\n  - 10 withdrawals in a month: all 10 are free.\\n  - 15 withdrawals in a month: all 15 are free.\\n  - More than 15 withdrawals in a month: any withdrawals beyond 15 are not free.\\n\\n## ATM fee rebates\\n\\n- You receive up to $20 in ATM fee rebates each month.\\n- If total ATM operator fees in a month exceed $20, the excess amount is not rebated.\\n- Tip: Keep your receipts or review your statements to track how much of the $20 monthly cap you have used.\\n\\n## Bonus APY for EcoCard holders\\n\\n- Your Green Account earns the base 4.0% APY plus a 0.5% bonus when you hold an EcoCard.\\n- Example: 4.0% + 0.5% = 4.75% APY.\\n\\n## Quick reference\\n\\n- Total free withdrawals per month: 8 + 7 = 15\\n- Monthly ATM fee rebates: $20\\n- APY boost: 4.0% base + 0.5% bonus\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_ddaD6GsH8ZN3AR96uT1ttoQx\",\"output\":\"1. Internal: Business Checking Account Promotion - November 2025\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_013\\n   Score: 8.4624\\n   Content: PROMOTION NOTICE - ACTIVE FROM 11/01/2025 TO 11/30/2025: When recommending business checking accounts to customers, if multiple accounts meet all of the customer's stated requirements, agents should prioritize recommending accounts in the following order: (1) Sky Blue account should be recommended first, as it is currently under promotional priority; (2) Lime Green account should be recommended second, as it is also under promotional priority; (3) All other qualifying accounts may be recommended only if neither Sky Blue nor Lime Green meet the customer's requirements. This promotion is designed to increase adoption of our startup and premium business offerings. Always ensure the recommended account still meets ALL of the customer's stated requirements - do not recommend a promotional account if it does not satisfy the customer's needs.\\n\\n2. Business Platinum Rewards Card: New Customer First Year Fee Waiver\\n   ID: doc_business_credit_cards_business_platinum_rewards_card_011\\n   Score: 5.9115\\n   Content: ## Promotion Window\\n- Offer start date: 2025-11-01\\n- Offer end date: 2026-02-28\\n\\n## First-Year Annual Fee\\n- First-year annual fee for new customers: 0\\n- After the first year, the standard annual fee applies: $450.00\\n\\n## How the Waiver Is Applied\\n- The fee waiver is reflected on your account during the first year of membership, provided your account is opened within the promotion dates.\\n- If you upgrade or change products during the promotional period, the waiver continues only if the account remains eligible.\\n\\n## Eligibility Guidelines\\n- Offer is for new customers only and applies to new accounts opened within the promotion window.\\n- The account must remain open and in good standing to retain the waived first-year fee.\\n\\n3. Diamond Elite Card: Understanding Your Annual Fee and Elite Benefits\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_diamond_elite_card_006\\n   Score: 5.3867\\n   Content: ## Annual fee\\n- Your standard annual fee is $495.00. It appears on your first statement and on the anniversary each year thereafter unless waived by a qualifying promotion.\\n- Interest on carried balances, if any, accrues at 15.99% and is separate from the annual fee.\\n\\n## Invitation promo: fee waiver and credit\\n- If you meet the invitation spending requirement of $50,000 within the specified promo period, your annual fee is waived (Yes).\\n- You also receive a $5,000 statement credit after qualification.\\n\\n## How the waiver and credit apply\\n- The $495.00 will be waived on the billing statement after you satisfy the $50,000.\\n- The $5,000 posts after qualification is confirmed; timing may vary by billing cycle.\\n\\n## If you do not meet the requirement\\n- The standard $495.00 remains on your account.\\n- You can still avoid interest by paying your statement balance in full, even if the fee is not waived.\\n\\n## Verification tips\\n- Track your cumulative spend toward $50,000 during the promo window and keep all receipts.\\n- Review the first two statements carefully to confirm the waiver and credit have posted.\\n\\n4. Business Silver Rewards Card: New Customer First Year Fee Waiver\\n   ID: doc_business_credit_cards_business_silver_rewards_card_011\\n   Score: 5.2925\\n   Content: ## Offer terms\\n- New customers who open an account during the promotional window receive a first-year annual fee of 0\\n- After the first year, the standard annual fee of $122.50 applies\\n\\n## Promotional window\\n- Start date: 2025-11-15\\n- End date: 2026-01-15\\n\\n## How to qualify\\n- Open your account within the promotional window and meet new customer eligibility criteria\\n- The fee waiver is applied to the first year of card membership at 0\\n\\n## Verifying the waiver\\n- Review your cardholder agreement and first statement for confirmation of the waived fee\\n- If the statement does not reflect 0, contact support so your account can be reviewed for promotional eligibility\\n\\n5. Platinum Rewards Card: New Customer Promo - First Year Annual Fee Waived\\n   ID: doc_credit_cards_platinum_rewards_card_009\\n   Score: 5.0182\\n   Content: ## Offer Summary\\n- Apply during the promo window and, if approved, your first year annual fee is $0.00 instead of $200.00.\\n\\n## Promo Window\\n- Start date: 2024-06-01\\n- End date: 2024-12-31\\n\\n## How to Qualify\\n- Submit your application within the promo window and be approved.\\n- The waiver applies to the first 12 months from account opening; after the first anniversary, the standard $200.00 annual fee applies.\\n\\n## What to Expect on Statements\\n- Your first statement should show no annual fee charge for the first year.\\n- If you see an annual fee during the promo period in error, contact support for correction.\\n\\n## Important Notes\\n- The waiver cannot be retroactively applied to accounts opened outside the promo window.\\n- Closing and reopening an account does not guarantee eligibility; new approval during the promo window is required.\\n\\n6. Internal: Closing Business Checking Accounts\\n   ID: doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_007\\n   Score: 5.0004\\n   Content: ## Pre-Closure Requirements\\n\\nVerify all of the following before closing:\\n- If an early closure fee applies, the account balance must be at least the fee amount; otherwise, account balance (current_holdings) must be $0. The fee is deducted directly from the account balance and there is no alternative payment method.\\n- Account status is OPEN\\n- No pending transactions for this account\\n- Customer has no linked business savings accounts that are still OPEN (close those first)\\n\\n## Tier-Specific Closure Requirements\\n\\n- ENTRY TIER (Navy Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $50 if closed within 60 days\\n  - Notice period: 7 days\\n\\n- MID TIER (True Blue, Sky Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $100 if closed within 90 days\\n  - Notice period: 14 days\\n\\n- PREMIUM TIER (Cobalt Blue)\\n  - Early closure fee: $200 if closed within 180 days\\n  - Notice period: 21 days\\n  - Requires supervisor review\\n\\n- ELITE TIER (accounts with credit lines over $100,000)\\n  - Early closure fee: $400 if closed within 270 days\\n  - Notice period: 30 days\\n  - Requires manager approval\\n\\n## Closure Procedure\\n\\n1. Verify pre-closure requirements are met.\\n2. Determine the account tier and applicable fees/notice period.\\n3. For PREMIUM tier, obtain supervisor review. For ELITE tier, obtain manager approval.\\n4. Use close_bank_account_7392 to close the account.\\n\\n7. Getting Started with Sky Blue: Startup Account Setup\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_sky_blue_001\\n   Score: 4.9446\\n   Content: ## Verify Eligibility\\n- Confirm your company is within 4 years of formation.\\n- Check whether you meet the funding requirement: 0.\\n\\n## Understand Key Cost Terms Before You Apply\\n- Your startup receives a free period of 6 months.\\n- After the free period, the monthly maintenance fee is $25.00.\\n- If your balance goes negative, the overdraft fee is $0.00.\\n\\n## Prepare Your Application\\n- Gather company formation documents and ownership details.\\n- Be ready to provide basic business information and authorized signers.\\n- Plan initial account settings, such as user permissions and card controls, so you can activate quickly after approval.\\n\\n## Submit and Configure\\n- Complete the online application and upload requested documents.\\n- After approval, log in to set user roles, spending controls, and alerts.\\n- Link external accounts to enable seamless transfers.\\n\\n## Startup Referral Program\\nHelp other startups get started with Sky Blue:\\n- Your bonus: $150 for each successful referral\\n- Their bonus: $250 welcome bonus\\n- Annual limit: 8 referrals per year\\n\\n## First-Funding and Go-Live Checklist\\n- Make an initial deposit from a linked account.\\n- Confirm your free period of 6 months is visible in your billing section.\\n- Review your fee settings to ensure you understand the transition to $25.00 and the overdraft policy of $0.00.\\n\\n8. Troubleshooting: My World Blue fee wasn't waived\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_world_blue_008\\n   Score: 4.9443\\n   Content: ## Check what was charged\\n- Confirm the amount matches the monthly maintenance charge: $50.00.\\n- Note the statement period and the posting date of the charge on your statement.\\n\\n## Why your fee may not have been waived\\n- Balance threshold not met: Your account balance did not meet or exceed $25,000 during the waiver evaluation period for the statement cycle.\\n- Timing of deposits/credits: Funds that were pending or posted after the cycle’s cutoff would not count toward meeting $25,000 for that cycle.\\n- Multi-currency effects: If you hold balances in multiple currencies, the USD-equivalent total at the time of evaluation may have fallen below $25,000 due to exchange-rate movements.\\n- Intra-period dips: If your balance dropped below $25,000 at any point during the evaluation period, the waiver may not have applied.\\n- Reversals/adjustments: Chargebacks, refunds, or other adjustments posted before the evaluation could have reduced your qualifying balance.\\n\\nNote: If you cannot view fees or statements due to your permission level, ask an administrator to verify on your behalf.\\n\\n## How to self-audit quickly\\n1. Identify the exact statement cycle in which the fee posted.\\n2. Review your posted transactions and end-of-day balances for that cycle.\\n3. If you hold multiple currencies, estimate the USD-equivalent totals for those dates and compare your total to $25,000.\\n4. Look for any day or cutoff moment when the total may have fallen below $25,000, or when key deposits posted after the cutoff.\\n\\n## If you believe the waiver should have applied\\n- Gather:\\n  - The statement showing the $50.00 charge\\n  - Your balance history for the cycle\\n  - Any notes on the timing of deposits and currency holdings\\n- Contact support and request a review of the waiver for that cycle. Indicate that your balances met or exceeded $25,000 and include your supporting details.\\n- If a correction is warranted, we will reverse the $50.00 for that cycle.\\n\\n## Tips to avoid this next cycle\\n- Maintain a buffer above $25,000 to account for FX fluctuations.\\n- Ensure deposits post before the cycle cutoff; avoid relying on pending credits.\\n- Monitor balances near the end of the cycle, especially if holding multiple currencies.\\n\\n9. Silver Saver Account: Understanding the $25K Balance Threshold\\n   ID: doc_business_savings_accounts_silver_saver_account_002\\n   Score: 4.8650\\n   Content: ## How the balance threshold affects your APY\\n- The higher tier applies when your qualifying balance meets or exceeds the threshold.\\n- During periods you qualify, your APY is 4.0% in accordance with the account’s interest calculation method.\\n\\n## Coordinating with the maintenance fee waiver\\n- Maintaining a minimum daily balance of at least $10,000 waives the monthly maintenance fee.\\n- If you operate close to the threshold, keeping a buffer can help you retain eligibility for the waiver and higher APY tier simultaneously.\\n\\n## Practical scenarios\\n- Temporary dips below the threshold may move you to a lower APY tier for the affected period; restoring the qualifying balance can return you to 4.0% thereafter.\\n- If you expect incoming funds, consider timing them so the deposit settles before the applicable evaluation point for the tier in your cycle.\\n- Keep an eye on large outgoing payments that might reduce your qualifying balance during a key evaluation period.\\n\\n10. Implementing Beige: Enterprise Treasury Onboarding\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_beige_001\\n   Score: 4.8014\\n   Content: ## Onboarding timeline and responsibilities\\n- Confirm executive sponsorship and authorized signers before initiating onboarding.\\n- Prepare onboarding documentation, treasury policy, and internal approval matrix.\\n- Identify primary funding sources for initial deposits and recurring cash flows.\\n\\n## Funding and balance setup\\n- Maintain at least $250,000 to keep your enterprise-level treasury account in good standing.\\n- The monthly maintenance fee is $200.00. This fee is waived when your average balance meets or exceeds $500,000.\\n- If you anticipate balance variability during early implementation, align funding schedules to preserve eligibility for the fee waiver threshold.\\n\\n## Dedicated support structure\\n- You are assigned 2 dedicated account managers who coordinate onboarding milestones, entitlements, and operational readiness.\\n- Establish a recurring operating cadence with your account team for progress tracking and rapid issue resolution.\\n\\n## Overdraft settings during go-live\\n- Overdrafts incur a fee of $0.00.\\n- If you plan to stagger incoming funds across multiple institutions, configure conservative payment windows and internal approvals to avoid negative balances.\\n\\n## Operational readiness checklist\\n- Set signer roles and entitlements consistent with your treasury policy.\\n- Add internal approval rules for payments and administrative changes in line with your governance model.\\n- Validate statement delivery preferences, reporting formats, and reconciliation identifiers prior to first close.\\n- Confirm that funding sources are scheduled to achieve at least $250,000 and, if desired, the waiver threshold of $500,000.\\n\\n## Reference values for onboarding\\n| Item | Value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $200.00 |\\n| Minimum balance requirement | $250,000 |\\n| Fee waiver balance threshold | $500,000 |\\n| Dedicated account managers | 2 |\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=0ms, reranking=0ms, total=0ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"},{\"call_id\":\"call_636PhHcmUVnvIeF8373AokCV\",\"output\":\"1. Navy Blue Account: Overdraft Protection and Fees\\n   ID: doc_business_checking_accounts_navy_blue_002\\n   Score: 11.4622\\n   Content: ## Overdraft options\\nYou can choose whether transactions are covered when your available balance is not sufficient.\\n\\n### If an overdraft occurs\\n- Overdraft fee per occurrence: $0.00\\n- The fee is assessed when a covered transaction settles into a negative available balance.\\n\\n### Overdraft protection via linked account\\n- When enabled, funds can be transferred automatically from a linked eligible account to cover a shortfall.\\n- Transfer fee for overdraft protection: $0.00\\n\\n### How to manage your settings\\n- In your online or mobile banking, navigate to account settings and choose your overdraft preference.\\n- If you enable protection, confirm the linked funding source and authorize automatic transfers.\\n- You can change your preference at any time before a transaction settles.\\n\\n### When fees do not apply\\n- If a transaction is declined due to insufficient funds, no overdraft occurs and $0.00 does not apply.\\n- If overdraft protection fully covers the shortfall, only the protection transfer fee $0.00 may apply.\\n\\n### Disputes and adjustments\\n- If you believe an overdraft was charged in error, contact support promptly with the transaction details.\\n- Reversals are evaluated case by case based on posting order and available balance at the time of settlement.\\n\\n2. Setting up overdraft protection for your Blue Account\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_004\\n   Score: 10.6982\\n   Content: ## What overdraft protection does\\nWhen enabled, overdraft protection can move funds from a linked account to cover transactions that would otherwise cause a negative balance. Each transfer triggered by this service incurs a fee of $12.50.\\n\\n## Before you begin\\n- Confirm you have an eligible account to link as the funding source.\\n- Understand that each protection-triggered transfer is assessed $12.50.\\n- If you choose to fund your linked account by requesting a cashier’s check, the issuance fee is $10.\\n\\n## How to enroll\\n- Open your account settings and select Overdraft Protection.\\n- Choose the account to link as your funding source and confirm.\\n- Review and accept the $12.50 per-transfer fee disclosure, then enable the service.\\n\\n## Managing the service\\n- You can change or remove the linked funding source at any time from the same settings page.\\n- Transfers initiated by the protection service will each incur $12.50.\\n\\n3. Blue Account: How overdraft transfer fees work\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_006\\n   Score: 10.0688\\n   Content: ## When the fee applies\\nIf you enable overdraft protection, the bank may transfer funds from your linked account to cover a shortfall. Each such transfer incurs a fee of $12.50.\\n\\n## How the fee is assessed\\n- The fee of $12.50 is charged per transfer initiated by the overdraft protection service.\\n- The fee may apply whether the transfer covers all or only part of the shortfall.\\n\\n## Ways to minimize transfers\\n- Keep a buffer in the protected account to reduce the number of protection-triggered transfers.\\n- Monitor your pending activity and available balance so you can move funds proactively rather than relying on protection transfers that incur $12.50.\\n\\n4. Why can't I overdraft my Green Account (checking)?\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_account_(checking)_009\\n   Score: 9.9765\\n   Content: ## Overdrafts are not supported\\n- Transactions are authorized only up to your available balance, so attempts that would create a negative balance are declined.\\n\\n## No overdraft transfers\\n- The account does not perform overdraft protection transfers from other accounts; as a result, there is no fee for such transfers: $0.00.\\n\\n## How to avoid declines\\n- Keep sufficient funds available before initiating payments.\\n- If a decline occurs, add funds and retry the transaction rather than relying on overdraft coverage.\\n\\n5. Dark Green Account specifications and requirements\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_dark_green_account_002\\n   Score: 9.7137\\n   Content: ## Eligibility requirements\\n- The primary account holder must be at least 17.\\n- You can maintain the account through 26.\\n\\n## Fee schedule\\nThe following fees apply to this account.\\n\\n| Fee | Amount |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Monthly maintenance | $10.00 |\\n| Overdraft protection transfer | 0 |\\n| Foreign ATM withdrawal | 2.5% of amount (max $6.00) |\\n| Returned deposit | $10.00 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire | $7.50 |\\n\\n## Foreign ATM withdrawals\\n- When you withdraw cash from an ATM abroad, a fee of 2.5% of the withdrawal amount is charged.\\n- The fee is capped at a maximum of $6.00 per transaction, protecting you from excessive fees on larger withdrawals.\\n- Third-party ATM operator fees may still apply.\\n\\n## Transaction limits\\n- Debit card daily purchase limit: $1,500\\n- Daily ATM withdrawal limit: $300\\n\\n## Overdraft protection transfers\\n- When enabled and available, transfers from a linked funding source to cover an overdraft incur a transfer fee of 0.\\n\\n6. Blue Account features and fees\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_blue_account_003\\n   Score: 9.6255\\n   Content: ## Key Features\\n- No overdraft fees on the account\\n- Waivable monthly maintenance fee: $20.00; waived when your minimum daily balance is at least $625\\n\\n## Optional Add-On\\n### Overdraft Protection Transfers\\n- If you opt in to overdraft protection, each transfer from a linked account to cover a negative balance incurs a $12.50 fee\\n- No overdraft fees are charged by the account itself\\n\\n## Fees\\n| Item | Amount | When it applies |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $20.00 | Charged monthly; waived with a minimum daily balance of $625 |\\n| Paper statement fee | $2.50 | Per month if you choose mailed paper statements |\\n| Returned deposit | $15.00 | Per deposited item returned unpaid |\\n| Incoming domestic wire transfer | $12.50 | Per incoming domestic wire |\\n| Stop payment on a check | $30 | Per stop payment request |\\n\\n## Linked Savings APY Boosts\\n- When linked to a Silver Plus Savings Account: +0.35% APY boost\\n- When linked to a Platinum Savings Account: +0.8% APY boost\\n\\n## Ways to Reduce or Avoid Fees\\n- Maintain a minimum daily balance of $625 to waive the $20.00 monthly maintenance fee\\n- Choose e-statements to avoid the $2.50 paper statement fee\\n- Use in-network ATMs to avoid out-of-network ATM fees\\n- Only enable overdraft protection if you need it, as each transfer incurs a $12.50 fee\\n\\n7. How Green Account (checking) prevents overdrafts\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_account_(checking)_004\\n   Score: 9.5498\\n   Content: ## Authorization flow that stops negative balances\\n- Real-time authorization checks your available balance before each transaction.\\n- A small buffer of up to 5 may be considered during authorization to account for minor final-amount differences; beyond that threshold, the transaction is declined.\\n- There are no automatic overdraft transfers; the overdraft protection transfer fee is $0.00.\\n\\n### What this means for you\\n- If a transaction would exceed your balance by more than 5, it is declined rather than creating a negative balance.\\n- Because there are no overdraft transfers, you do not incur transfer fees; the fee amount is $0.00.\\n\\n8. No-overdraft checking explained\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_green_account_(checking)_003\\n   Score: 8.9986\\n   Content: ## How no-overdraft works in this account\\n- Transactions that would push your available balance negative are declined at authorization.\\n- There are no overdraft transfers from linked accounts; the overdraft protection transfer fee is $0.00.\\n\\n## Checks and guaranteed funds\\n- When you request a cashier's check, your account must have sufficient available funds at issuance; the fee to issue is 8.\\n- If there are not enough available funds, the cashier's check request is not completed rather than overdrawing your account.\\n\\n### What to expect at the point of sale\\n- Card purchases and ATM withdrawals are authorized only up to your available balance.\\n- If a merchant attempts a charge above your available funds, the authorization is declined immediately, with no overdraft and no transfer assessed at $0.00.\\n\\n9. Light Blue Account features and fees\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_light_blue_account_004\\n   Score: 7.8115\\n   Content: ## Fees and features\\n| Item | Amount |\\n|---|---|\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $0.00 |\\n| Overdraft fee | $0.00 |\\n| Overdraft protection transfer fee | $0.00 |\\n| Free out-of-network ATM withdrawals per month | 2 |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee (after free) | $2.50 |\\n| Paper statement fee (monthly) | $0.00 |\\n| Returned deposit fee | $0.00 |\\n| Incoming domestic wire fee | $0.00 |\\n| Stop payment fee (per request) | $30 |\\n| APY on balances | 0% |\\n| Daily ATM withdrawal limit | $400 |\\n\\n## Out-of-network ATM withdrawals\\n- You receive 2 free out-of-network ATM withdrawals each month.\\n- After using your free allowance, each additional withdrawal costs $2.50.\\n- ATM owners may charge their own surcharge, separate from our fee.\\n\\n## Daily ATM withdrawal limit\\n- Your daily ATM withdrawal limit is $400. This limit applies to all ATM withdrawals within a 24-hour period.\\n\\n## Helpful notes\\n- Returned checks may be subject to the $0.00 even if the return reason is outside your control.\\n- If you prefer paper statements, factor in the $0.00 each cycle.\\n- If you link an account for overdraft protection, each transfer to cover a shortfall is $0.00.\\n\\n10. Dark Green Account at a glance\\n   ID: doc_checking_accounts_dark_green_account_001\\n   Score: 7.8010\\n   Content: ## Snapshot\\n\\nQuick reference to core details you will use most often.\\n\\n### Eligibility\\n- Minimum primary holder age: 17\\n- Maximum primary holder age: 26\\n\\n### Fees and rates\\n- Monthly maintenance fee: $10.00\\n- Overdraft protection transfer fee: 0\\n- Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee: 1% (min $1.50)\\n- Annual percentage yield (APY): 1.5%\\n\\n### Rewards and perks\\n- Student loan payment cashback: 1.25%\\n- Annual academic standing bonus: $62.50\\n- Partner textbook retailer discount: 10.0%\\n- Graduation transition bonus: $100.00\\n\\n### Limits\\n- Mobile check deposit daily limit: $1,500\\n\\n### Direct deposit\\n- Early direct deposit: 1 day(s) before payday\\n\\n### Quick tables\\n\\n#### Eligibility and costs\\n| Item | Value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Minimum age | 17 |\\n| Maximum age | 26 |\\n| Monthly maintenance fee | $10.00 |\\n| Overdraft protection transfer fee | 0 |\\n| Out-of-network ATM withdrawal fee | 1% (min $1.50) |\\n\\n#### Rewards and limits\\n| Item | Value |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| APY | 1.5% |\\n| Student loan payment cashback | 1.25% |\\n| Annual academic standing bonus | $62.50 |\\n| Partner textbook discount | 10.0% |\\n| Graduation transition bonus | $100.00 |\\n| Mobile deposit daily limit | $1,500 |\\n| Early direct deposit | 1 day(s) before payday |\\n\\n### Notes\\n- Rewards and limits apply when eligibility conditions are met and verification is provided where required.\\n- Fees and rates may change with required notice.\\n- Get paid 1 day(s) early with direct deposit.\\n\\n\\n[Timing: retrieval=1ms, reranking=0ms, total=1ms]\",\"type\":\"function_call_output\"}],\"model\":\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\"reasoning\":{\"effort\":\"xhigh\",\"summary\":\"auto\"},\"tool_choice\":\"auto\",\"tools\":[{\"description\":\"Search the knowledge base for relevant documents.\",\"name\":\"KB_search\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"query\":{\"description\":\"The search query to find relevant documents\",\"title\":\"Query\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"query\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Transfer the user to a human agent.\\n\\nThe proper transfer reason enum can be found in the knowledge base: search it before calling this tool to select the proper applicable reason.\",\"name\":\"transfer_to_human_agents\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"reason\":{\"default\":\"other\",\"description\":\"The specific reason code for the transfer.\",\"enum\":[\"fraud_or_security_concern\",\"account_closure_request\",\"deceased_account_holder\",\"legal_or_regulatory_matter\",\"account_ownership_dispute\",\"complex_billing_dispute\",\"abusive_customer_behavior\",\"third_party_inquiry\",\"technical_system_error\",\"unconfirmed_external_communication\",\"customer_demands_after_unavailable_offer_refusal\",\"kb_search_unsuccessful_customer_requests_transfer\",\"specialized_department_required\",\"accessibility_or_special_needs\",\"customer_frustrated_demands_human\",\"supervisor_request_service_complaint\",\"customer_requests_human_no_specific_reason\",\"request_completed_customer_wants_human_followup\",\"other\"],\"title\":\"Reason\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"summary\":{\"description\":\"A summary of the user's issue and what was attempted before transfer.\",\"title\":\"Summary\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"summary\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Get the current time. Use this to get the current timestamp for logging verification records.\",\"name\":\"get_current_time\",\"parameters\":{\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Get the information (date of birth, email, phone number, address) for a user by their user id.\",\"name\":\"get_user_information_by_id\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"user_id\":{\"description\":\"The ID of the user\",\"title\":\"User Id\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"user_id\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Get the information (date of birth, email, phone number, address) for a user by their name. Case Sensitive.\",\"name\":\"get_user_information_by_name\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"customer_name\":{\"description\":\"The name of the user\",\"title\":\"Customer Name\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"customer_name\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Get the information (date of birth, email, phone number, address) for a user by their email.\",\"name\":\"get_user_information_by_email\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"email\":{\"description\":\"The email of the user\",\"title\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"email\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Change the email address for a user.\",\"name\":\"change_user_email\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"new_email\":{\"description\":\"The new email address to set for the user\",\"title\":\"New Email\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"user_id\":{\"description\":\"The ID of the user whose email should be changed\",\"title\":\"User Id\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"user_id\",\"new_email\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Get all referrals made by a user.\",\"name\":\"get_referrals_by_user\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"user_id\":{\"description\":\"The ID of the user (referrer) to look up referrals for\",\"title\":\"User Id\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"user_id\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Get all credit card transactions for a user.\",\"name\":\"get_credit_card_transactions_by_user\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"user_id\":{\"description\":\"The ID of the user to look up transactions for\",\"title\":\"User Id\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"user_id\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Get all credit card accounts for a user.\\n\\nReturns information about each credit card account including card type,\\ndate opened, current balance, and reward points.\",\"name\":\"get_credit_card_accounts_by_user\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"user_id\":{\"description\":\"The ID of the user to look up credit card accounts for\",\"title\":\"User Id\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"user_id\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Log a verification record after successfully verifying a user's identity.\\n\\nCall this tool after you have verified a user by confirming 2 out of 4 identity fields\\n(date of birth, email, phone number, address). This creates an audit record of the verification.\",\"name\":\"log_verification\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"address\":{\"description\":\"The verified user's address\",\"title\":\"Address\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"date_of_birth\":{\"description\":\"The verified user's date of birth (MM/DD/YYYY format)\",\"title\":\"Date Of Birth\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"email\":{\"description\":\"The verified user's email\",\"title\":\"Email\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"name\":{\"description\":\"The verified user's full name\",\"title\":\"Name\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"phone_number\":{\"description\":\"The verified user's phone number\",\"title\":\"Phone Number\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"time_verified\":{\"description\":\"The timestamp of the verification (e.g., \\\"2025-11-14 03:40:00 EST\\\")\",\"title\":\"Time Verified\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"user_id\":{\"description\":\"The verified user's ID\",\"title\":\"User Id\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"name\",\"user_id\",\"address\",\"email\",\"phone_number\",\"date_of_birth\",\"time_verified\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Pass a tool to the user so they can execute it themselves.\\n\\nUse this when the knowledge base indicates that the user should perform\\nan action themselves (e.g., \\\"to do X, have the user call tool_name(args)\\\").\\n\\nThe user will then be able to call `call_discoverable_tool` with the same\\ntool name and arguments to simulate executing the action.\",\"name\":\"give_discoverable_user_tool\",\"parameters\":{\"properties\":{\"arguments\":{\"default\":\"{}\",\"description\":\"JSON string of arguments for the tool (e.g., '{\\\"url\\\": \\\"https://example.com\\\"}')\",\"title\":\"Arguments\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"discoverable_tool_name\":{\"description\":\"The name of the discoverable tool (e.g., \\\"open_webpage\\\", \\\"navigate_to_section\\\")\",\"title\":\"Discoverable Tool Name\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"discoverable_tool_name\"],\"title\":\"parameters\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"description\":\"Unlock an agent discoverable tool that was found in the knowledge base.\\n\\nUse this when the knowledge base indicates that you have access to a specialized\\ninternal tool. The knowledge base will tell you the tool name to unlock.\\n\\nAfter unlocking, you can